\id PSA - Brenton English Septuagint
\h Psalms 
\toc1 Psalms 
\toc2 Psalms 
\toc3 Ps. 
\mt1 PSALMS 
\c 1 
\q1
\v 1 \sc Blessed\sc* is the man who has not walked in the counsel of the ungodly,
\q2 and has not stood in the way of sinners, 
\q2 and has not sat in the seat of \f + \fr 1:1 \fqa Gr. \ft pestilent.\f*evil men. 
\q1
\v 2 But his \f + \fr 1:2 \fqa Gr. \ft will.\f*pleasure is in the law of the Lord; 
\q2 and in his law will he meditate day and night.
\q1
\v 3 He will be like a tree planted by the brooks of waters, 
\q2 which yields its fruit in its season, 
\q2 and its leaf will not fall off; 
\q2 and whatever he does will prosper. 
\q1
\v 4 Not so the ungodly;—not so: 
\q2 but rather as the \f + \fr 1:4 \fqa Or, \ft dust or down.\f*chaff which the wind scatters away from the face of the earth. 
\q1
\v 5 Therefore the ungodly will not rise in judgment, 
\q2 nor sinners in the counsel of the just. 
\q1
\v 6 For the Lord knows the way of the righteous; 
\q2 but the way of the ungodly will perish. 
\c 2 
\q1
\v 1 \x + \xo 2:1 \xt Acts 4. 25.\x* Why did the nations rage,
\q2 and the peoples devise vain things? 
\q1
\v 2 The kings of the earth stood up, 
\q2 and the rulers gathered themselves together, 
\q2 against the Lord, and against his Christ; 
\q1
\v 3 \add saying\add*, Let us break through their bonds, 
\q2 and cast away their yoke from us. 
\q1
\v 4 He who dwells in the heavens will laugh them to scorn, 
\q2 and the Lord will mock them. 
\q1
\v 5 Then he will speak to them in his anger, 
\q2 and trouble them in his fury. 
\q1
\v 6 But I have been made king by him 
\q2 on Zion his holy mountain, 
\q1
\v 7 declaring the ordinance of the Lord: 
\q2 the Lord said to me, \x + \xo 2:7 \xt Acts 13. 33; Heb. 1. 5.\x* You are my Son, 
\q2 today have I begotten you. 
\q1
\v 8 Ask of me, and I will give you the nations \add for\add* your inheritance, 
\q2 and the ends of the earth \add for\add* your possession. 
\q1
\v 9 You will \x + \xo 2:9 \xt Rev. 2. 27.\x*shepherd them with a rod of iron; 
\q2 you will shatter them like a potter's vessel. 
\p
\q1
\v 10 Now therefore understand, you kings: 
\q2 be instructed, all you who judge the earth. 
\q1
\v 11 Serve the Lord with fear, 
\q2 and rejoice in him with trembling. 
\q1
\v 12 Lay hold of instruction, 
\q2 lest the Lord become angry, 
\q2 and you perish from the righteous way: 
\q2 when his wrath is suddenly kindled, 
\q2 blessed are all those who trust in him. 
\c 3 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm of David, when he fled from the presence of his son Absalom. 
\q1
\v 2 O Lord, why are those who afflict me multiplied? 
\q2 Many rise up against me. 
\q1
\v 3 Many say concerning my soul, 
\q2 There is no deliverance for him in his God. \f + \fr 3:3 \ft The word Διάψαλμα (Selah) has been rendered Pause, as most intelligible to the English reader.\f*\qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 4 But you, O Lord, are my helper:
\q2 my glory, and the one who lifts up my head. 
\q1
\v 5 I cried to the Lord with my voice, 
\q2 and he heard me out of his holy mountain. \qs Pause.\qs*
\q1
\v 6 I lay down and slept; 
\q2 I awoke; for the Lord will help me. 
\q1
\v 7 I will not be afraid of ten thousands of people, 
\q2 who beset me all around. 
\q1
\v 8 Arise, Lord; deliver me, my God: 
\q2 for you have struck all who were my enemies without cause; 
\q2 you have broken the teeth of sinners. 
\q1
\v 9 Deliverance is the Lord's, 
\q2 and your blessing is upon your people. 
\c 4 
\d
\v 1 For the end: with Psalms. A Song of David.
\q1
\v 2 When I called,
\q2 the God of my righteousness heard me: 
\q1 in distress you made room for me; 
\q2 pity me, and hear my prayer. 
\q1
\v 3 O you sons of men, 
\q2 how long \add will you be\add* \f + \fr 4:3 \fqa Lit. \ft heavy of heart.\f*slow of heart? 
\q1 Why do you love vanity, 
\q2 and seek falsehood? \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 4 But know that the Lord has done wondrous things for his holy one: 
\q2 the Lord will hear me when I cry to him. 
\q1
\v 5 \x + \xo 4:5 \xt Eph. 4. 26.\x* Be angry, and do not sin; 
\q2 speak in your hearts, and upon your beds be pierced. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 6 Offer the sacrifice of righteousness, 
\q2 and trust in the Lord. 
\q1
\v 7 Many say, Who will show us good things? 
\q2 The light of your face, O Lord, has been shown upon us. 
\q1
\v 8 You have put gladness into my heart: 
\q2 from the time their grain and wine and oil increased, they multiplied.
\q1
\v 9 I will \f + \fr 4:9 \fqa Or, \ft at the same time.\f*both lie down in peace and sleep: 
\q2 for you, Lord, only have settled me in hope.
\c 5 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm of David, concerning an heiress.
\p
\q1
\v 2 Listen to my words, O Lord,
\q2 \f + \fr 5:2 \fqa Lit. \ft understand.\f*pay attention to my cry. 
\q1
\v 3 Pay attention to the voice of my supplication, my King, and my God:
\q2 for to you, O Lord, I will pray. 
\q1
\v 4 In the morning you will hear my voice: 
\q2 in the morning I will wait on you, and will look up. 
\q1
\v 5 For you are not a God who desires wickedness; 
\q2 neither will the worker of wickedness dwell with you. 
\q1
\v 6 Neither will the transgressors continue in your sight: 
\q2 you hate, O Lord, all those who work wickedness. 
\q1
\v 7 You will destroy all who speak falsehood: 
\q2 the Lord abhors the man of blood and deceit. 
\q1
\v 8 But I will enter into your house in the multitude of your mercy: 
\q2 In fear of you I will worship toward your holy temple. 
\p
\q1
\v 9 Lead me, O Lord, in your righteousness because of my enemies; 
\q2 make my way plain before your face. 
\q1
\v 10 For there is no truth in their mouth; 
\q2 their heart is vain; 
\q1 their \x + \xo 5:10 \xt Rom. 3. 13.\x* throat is an open sepulchre; 
\q2 with their tongues they have used deceit. 
\q1
\v 11 Judge them, O God; 
\q2 let them fall away from their schemes;
\q1 cast them out according to the abundance of their ungodliness; 
\q2 for they have provoked you, O Lord. 
\p
\q1
\v 12 But let all who trust in you be glad in you: 
\q2 they will exult forever, and you will dwell among them; 
\q2 and all that love your name will rejoice in you. 
\q1
\v 13 For you, Lord, will bless the righteous: 
\q2 you have crowned us as with a shield of favour. 
\c 6 
\d
\v 1 For the end, among the Hymns; for the eighth: a Psalm of David. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 O Lord, don't rebuke me in your wrath, 
\q2 nor chasten me in your anger. 
\q1
\v 3 Pity me, O Lord; for I am weak: 
\q2 heal me, O Lord; for my bones are vexed. 
\q1
\v 4 My soul also is grievously vexed: 
\q2 but you, O Lord, how long? 
\q1
\v 5 Return, O Lord, deliver my soul: 
\q2 save me for your mercy's sake. 
\q1
\v 6 For in death no man remembers you: 
\q2 and who will give you thanks in Hades? 
\q1
\v 7 \f + \fr 6:7 \fqa Gr. \ft I have laboured.\f*I am wearied with my groaning; 
\q2 I will wash my bed every night; 
\q2 I will water my couch with my tears. 
\q1
\v 8 My eye is troubled because of my wrath; 
\q2 I am worn out because of all my enemies. 
\p
\q1
\v 9 Depart from me, all you who work wickedness; 
\q2 for the Lord has heard the voice of my weeping. 
\q1
\v 10 The Lord has listened to my petition; 
\q2 the Lord has accepted my prayer. 
\q1
\v 11 Let all my enemies be put to shame and greatly troubled: 
\q2 let them be turned back and utterly put to shame at once. 
\c 7 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm of David, which he sang to the Lord because of the words of Chusi the \f + \fr 7:1 \fqa Lit. \ft son of Jemini.\f*Benjamite. 
\q1
\v 2 O Lord my God, in you have I trusted:  
\q2 save me from all those who persecute me, and deliver me. 
\q1
\v 3 Lest he seize my soul like a lion,  
\q2 while there is no one to redeem, nor to save. 
\q1
\v 4 O Lord my God, if I have done this, 
\q2 if there is unrighteousness in my hands, 
\q1
\v 5 if I have repayed with evil those who repayed me, 
\q2 then may I fall empty before my enemies. 
\q1
\v 6 Let the enemy persecute my soul, and take it;  
\q2 and let him trample my life on the ground,  
\q2 and lay my glory in the dust. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 7 Arise, O Lord, in your wrath;  
\q2 be exalted at the boundaries of my enemies:  
\q2 awake, O Lord my God, according to the decree which you commanded. 
\q1
\v 8 The congregation of the peoples will surround you:  
\q2 and because of this, return on high. 
\q1
\v 9 The Lord will judge the nations:  
\q2 judge me, O Lord, according to my righteousness,  
\q2 and according to my innocence that is in me. 
\q1
\v 10 Oh let the wickedness of sinners come to an end;  
\q2 and you will guide the righteous,  
\q2 O God who searches the hearts and kidneys. 
\p
\q1
\v 11 My help is righteous,  
\q2 \add coming\add* from God who saves the upright in heart. 
\q1
\v 12 God is a righteous judge, and strong, and patient,  
\q2 not inflicting vengeance every day. 
\q1
\v 13 If you will not repent, he will furbish his sword;  
\q2 he has bent his bow, and made it ready. 
\q1
\v 14 On it he has fitted the instruments of death;  
\q2 he has completed his arrows for the \f + \fr 7:14 \ft See \fqa Heb. \ft perhaps 'persecuting ones.'\f*raging ones. 
\q1
\v 15 Behold, he has travailed with unrighteousness,  
\q2 he has conceived trouble, and brought forth wickedness. 
\q1
\v 16 He has opened a pit, and dug it up,  
\q2 and he will fall into the ditch which he has made. 
\q1
\v 17 His trouble will return on his own head,  
\q2 and his unrighteousness will come down on his own crown. 
\q1
\v 18 I will give thanks to the Lord according to his righteousness;  
\q2 I will sing to the name of the Lord most high. 
\c 8 
\d
\v 1 For the end, concerning the wine-presses, a Psalm of David. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 O Lord, our Lord, how wonderful is your name in all the earth! For your magnificence is exalted above the heavens. 
\q1
\v 3 \x + \xo 8:3 \xt Mat. 21. 16.\x* Out of the mouth of babes and sucklings have you perfected praise, because of your enemies; that you might put down the enemy and avenger. 
\p
\q1
\v 4 For I will regard the heavens, the work of your fingers; the moon and stars, which you have established. 
\q1
\v 5 \x + \xo 8:5 \xt Heb. 2. 6-9.\x* What is man, that you are mindful of him? Or the son of man, that you visitest him? 
\q1
\v 6 You made him a little less than angels, you have crowned him with glory and honour; 
\q1
\v 7 and you have set him over the works of your hands: you have put all things under his feet: 
\q1
\v 8 sheep and all \f + \fr 8:8 \fqa Gr. \ft cows.\f*oxen, yes, and the cattle of the field; 
\q1
\v 9 the birds of the sky, and the fish of the sea, the \add creatures\add* passing through the paths of the sea. 
\q1
\v 10 O Lord our Lord, how wonderful is your name in all the earth! 
\c 9 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm of David, concerning the secrets of the Son. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 I will give thanks to you, O Lord, with my whole heart; I will recount all your wonderful works. 
\q1
\v 3 I will be glad and exult in you: I will sing to your name, O you Most High. 
\p
\q1
\v 4 When my enemies are turned back, they will be feeble and perish at your presence. 
\q1
\v 5 For you have maintained my cause and my right; you satest on the throne, that judgest righteousness. 
\q1
\v 6 You have rebuked the nations, and the ungodly one has perished; you have blotted out their name forever, even forever and ever. 
\q1
\v 7 The swords of the enemy have failed completely; and you have destroyed cities: their memorial has been destroyed with a noise, 
\q1
\v 8 but the Lord endures forever: he has prepared his throne for judgment. 
\q1
\v 9 He will judge the world in righteousness, he will judge the nations in uprightness. 
\q1
\v 10 The Lord also is become a refuge for the poor, a seasonable help, in affliction. 
\q1
\v 11 Let those who know your name hope in you: for you, O Lord, have not failed those who diligently seek you. 
\p
\q1
\v 12 Sing praises to the Lord, who dwells in Zion: declare his dealings among the nations. 
\q1
\v 13 For he remembered them, \add in\add* making inquisition for blood: he has not forgotten the supplication of the poor. 
\p
\q1
\v 14 Have mercy upon me, O Lord; look upon my affliction \add which I suffer\add* of my enemies, you who lift me up from the gates of death: 
\q1
\v 15 that I may declare all your praises in the gates of the daughter of Zion: I will exult in your salvation. 
\p
\q1
\v 16 The nations are caught in the destruction which they planned: in the very snare which they hid is their foot taken. 
\q1
\v 17 The Lord is known as executing judgments: the sinner is taken in the works of his hands. A song of \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 18 Let sinners be driven away into Hades, \add even\add* all the nations that forget God. 
\q1
\v 19 For the poor will not be forgotten forever: the patience of the needy ones will not perish forever. 
\q1
\v 20 Arise, O Lord, don't let man prevail: let the nations be judged before you. 
\q1
\v 21 Appoint, O Lord, a lawgiver over them: let the nations know that they are men. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 22 \f + \fr 9:22 \fqa Note.\ft —Here begins a change of numbers as compared with the \fqa Heb. \ft which continues to Ps. 146, this psalm having no number, and the eleventh being called the tenth. The following verses 22-39 are numbered 1-18 in the original text.\f*Why standest you afar off, O Lord? \add why\add* do you overlook \add us\add* in times of need, in affliction? 
\q1
\v 23 While the ungodly one acts proudly, the poor is \f + \fr 9:23 \fqa Gr. \ft inflamed, as in a fever.\f*hotly pursued: \add the wicked\add* are taken in the crafty counsels which they imagine. 
\q1
\v 24 Because the sinner praises himself for the desires of his heart; and the unjust one blesses himself. 
\q1
\v 25 The sinner has provoked the Lord: according to the abundance of his \f + \fr 9:25 \fqa Or, \ft anger.\f*pride he will not seek after \add him\add*: God isn't before him. 
\q1
\v 26 His ways are \f + \fr 9:26 \fqa Gr. \ft profaned.\f*profane at all times; your judgments are removed from before him: he will gain the mastery over all his enemies. 
\q1
\v 27 For he has said in his heart, I will not be moved, \add continuing\add* without evil from generation to generation. \x + \xo 9:27 \xt Rom. 8. 14.\x* 
\q1
\v 28 Whose mouth is full of cursing, and bitterness, and fraud: under his tongue are trouble and pain. 
\q1
\v 29 He lies in wait with rich \add men\add* in secret places, in order to kill the innocent: his eyes are \f + \fr 9:29 \fqa Gr. \ft look.\f*set against the poor. 
\q1
\v 30 He lies in wait in secret like a lion in his den: he lies in wait to ravish the poor, to ravish the poor when he draws him \add after him\add*: he will bring him down in his snare. 
\q1
\v 31 He will bow down and fall when he has mastered the poor. 
\q1
\v 32 For he has said in his heart, God has forgotten: he has turned away his face so as never to look. 
\p
\q1
\v 33 Arise, O Lord God; let your hand be lifted up: forget not the poor. 
\q1
\v 34 Why has the wicked provoked God? For he has said in his heart, He will not require \add it\add*. 
\q1
\v 35 You see \add it\add*; for you do observe trouble and wrath, to deliver them into your hands: the poor has been left to you; you were a helper to the orphan. 
\q1
\v 36 Break the arm of the sinner and wicked man: his sin will be sought for, and will not be found. 
\p
\q1
\v 37 The Lord will reign forever, even forever and ever: you nations will perish out of his land. 
\q1
\v 38 The Lord has heard the desire of the poor: your ear has inclined to the preparation of their heart; 
\q1
\v 39 to plead for the orphan and afflicted, that man may no more boast upon the earth. 
\c 10 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm of David. 
\p In the Lord I have put my trust: how will you say to my soul, Flee to the mountains as a sparrow? 
\q1
\v 2 For behold the sinners have bent \add their\add* bow, they have prepared their arrows for the quiver, to shoot \f + \fr 10:2 \fqa Gr. \ft in dark moon, or little moonlight, \fqa q. d. \ft luce malignâ.\f*privily at the upright in heart. 
\q1
\v 3 For they have pulled down what you did frame, but what has the righteous done? 
\p
\q1
\v 4 The Lord is in his holy temple, as for the Lord, his throne is in heaven: his eyes look upon the poor, his eyelids try the sons of men. 
\q1
\v 5 The Lord tries the righteous and the ungodly: and he who loves unrighteousness hates his own soul. 
\q1
\v 6 He will rain upon sinners snares, fire, and brimstone, and a stormy blast \add will be\add* the portion of their cup. 
\q1
\v 7 For the Lord \add is\add* righteous, and loves \f + \fr 10:7 \fqa Gr. \ft righteousnesses.\f*righteousness; his face beholds uprightness. 
\c 11 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm of David, upon the eighth. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 Save me, O Lord; for the godly man has failed; for \f + \fr 11:2 \fqa Gr. \ft truths are become rare.\f*truth is diminished from among the children of men. 
\q1
\v 3 Every one has spoken vanity to his neighbour: their lips are deceitful, they have spoken with a double heart. 
\q1
\v 4 Let the Lord destroy all the deceitful lips, and the tongue that speaks great words: 
\q1
\v 5 who have said, We will magnify our tongue; our lips are our own: who is Lord of us? 
\p
\q1
\v 6 Because of the misery of the poor, and because of the sighing of the needy, now will I arise, says the Lord, I will set \add them\add* in safety; I will speak \add to them\add* of it openly. 
\q1
\v 7 The oracles of the Lord are pure oracles; as silver tried in the fire, proved \add in\add* \f + \fr 11:7 \fqa Gr. \ft the earth.\f*a furnace of earth, purified seven times. 
\q1
\v 8 You, O Lord, will keep us, and will preserve us, from this generation, and forever. 
\q1
\v 9 The ungodly walk around: according to your greatness you have greatly exalted the sons of men. 
\c 12 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm of David. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 How long, O Lord, will you forget me? Forever? How long will you turn away your face from me? 
\q1
\v 3 How long will I take counsel in my soul, \add having\add* sorrows in my heart daily? How long will my enemy be exalted over me? 
\q1
\v 4 Look on me, listen to me, O Lord my God: lighten my eyes, lest I sleep in death; 
\q1
\v 5 lest at any time my enemy say, I have prevailed against him: my persecutors will exult if ever I should be moved. 
\p
\q1
\v 6 But I have hoped in your mercy; my heart will exult in your salvation. I will sing to the Lord who has dealt bountifully with me, and I will sing psalms to the name of the Lord most high. 
\c 13 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm of David. 
\p The fool has said in his heart, There is no God. They have corrupted \add themselves\add*, and become abominable in their devices; there is no one that does goodness, there isn't even so much as one. 
\q1
\v 2 The Lord looked down from heaven upon the sons of men, to see if there were any that understood, or sought after God. 
\q1
\v 3 They are all gone out of the way, they are together become good for nothing, there is no one that does good, no not one. Their throat is an open sepulchre; with their tongues they have used deceit; the poison of asps is under their lips: whose mouth is full of cursing and bitterness; their feet are swift to shed blood: destruction and misery are in their ways; and the way of peace they have not known: there is no fear of God before their eyes. 
\p
\q1
\v 4 Will not all the workers of wickedness know, who eat up my people as they would eat bread? They have not called upon the Lord. 
\q1
\v 5 There were they alarmed with fear, where there was no fear; for God is in the righteous generation. 
\q1
\v 6 You have shamed the counsel of the poor, because the Lord is his hope. 
\q1
\v 7 Who will bring the salvation of Israel out of Zion? When the Lord brings back the captivity of his people, let Jacob exult, and Israel be glad. 
\c 14 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm of David. 
\p O Lord, who will sojourn in your tabernacle? And who will dwell in your holy mountain? 
\p
\q1
\v 2 He who walks blameless, and works righteousness, who speaks truth in his heart. 
\q1
\v 3 Who has not spoken craftily with his tongue, neither has done evil to his neighbour, nor taken up a reproach against those who dwelt nearest to him. 
\q1
\v 4 In his sight an evil-worker is despise, but he honours those who fear the Lord. He swears to his neighbour, and disappoints \add him\add* not. 
\q1
\v 5 He has not \f + \fr 14:5 \fqa Gr. \ft given.\f*lent his money on usury, and has not received bribes against the innocent. He who does these things will never be moved. 
\c 15 
\d
\v 1 A writing of David. 
\p Keep me, O Lord; for I have hoped in you. 
\q1
\v 2 I said to the Lord, You are my Lord; for you have no need of my \f + \fr 15:2 \fqa Gr. \ft good deeds, or things.\f*goodness. 
\q1
\v 3 On behalf of the saints that are in his land, he has magnified all his pleasure in them. 
\q1
\v 4 Their weaknesses have been multiplied; afterward they hasted. I will by no means assemble their bloody meetings, neither will I make mention of their names with my lips. 
\q1
\v 5 The Lord is the portion of my inheritance and of my cup: you are he who restores my inheritance to me. 
\q1
\v 6 The lines have fallen to me in the best places, yes, I have a most excellent heritage. 
\p
\q1
\v 7 I will bless the Lord who has instructed me; my reins too have chastened me even \f + \fr 15:7 \fqa Possibly, \ft during the night. \fqa q. d. \ft as long as night lasted.\f*till night. 
\q1
\v 8 I foresaw the Lord always before my face; for he is on my right hand, that I should not be moved. 
\q1
\v 9 Therefore my heart rejoiced and my tongue exulted; moreover also my flesh will rest in hope: 
\q1
\v 10 because you will not leave my soul in hell, neither will you suffer yours Holy One to see corruption. 
\q1
\v 11 You have made known to me the ways of life; you will fill me with joy with your face: at your right hand \add there are\add* delights forever. 
\c 16 
\d
\v 1 A Prayer of David. 
\p Listen, O Lord \f + \fr 16:1 \fqa Or, \ft to my righteous plea, etc.\f*of my righteousness, pay attention to my petition; give ear to my prayer not \add uttered\add* with deceitful lips. 
\q1
\v 2 Let my judgment come forth from your presence; let my eyes behold righteousness. 
\q1
\v 3 You have proved my heart; you have visited \add me\add* by night; you have tried me as with fire, and unrighteousness has not been found in me: \add I am purposed\add* that my mouth will not speak \add amiss\add*. 
\q1
\v 4 As for the works of men, by the words of your lips I have \f + \fr 16:4 \fqa Lit. \ft I have observed hard ways.\f*guarded \add myself from\add* hard ways. 
\q1
\v 5 Direct my steps in your paths, that my steps slip not. 
\p
\q1
\v 6 I have cried, for you heard me, O God: incline your ear to me, and listen to my words. 
\q1
\v 7 Show the marvels of your mercies, you who savest those who hope in you. 
\q1
\v 8 Keep me as the apple of the eye from those that resist your right hand: you will screen me by the covering of your wings, 
\q1
\v 9 from the face of the ungodly that have afflicted me: my enemies have compassed about my soul. 
\q1
\v 10 They have enclosed \add themselves with\add* their own fat: their mouth has spoken pride. 
\q1
\v 11 They have now cast me out and compassed me all around: they have set their eyes \add so as\add* to bow them down to the ground. 
\q1
\v 12 They laid wait for me like a lion ready for prey, and like a lion's cub dwelling in secret \add places\add*. 
\q1
\v 13 Arise, O Lord, prevent them, and cast them down: deliver my soul from the ungodly: \add draw\add* your sword, 
\q1
\v 14 because of the enemies of your hand: O Lord, destroy them from the earth; scatter them in their life, though their belly has been filled with your hidden \add treasures\add*: they have been satisfied with \f + \fr 16:14 \fqa Alex. \ft children.\f*uncleanness, and have left the remnant \add of their possessions\add* to their babes. 
\p
\q1
\v 15 But I will appear in righteousness before your face: I will be satisfied when your glory appears. 
\c 17 
\d
\v 1 For the end, \add a Psalm\add* of David the servant of the Lord; \add the words\add* which he spoke to the Lord, \add even\add* the words of this Song, in the day in which the Lord delivered him out of the hand of all his enemies, and out of the hand of Saul: and he said: 
\p
\q1
\v 2 I will love you, O Lord, my strength. 
\q1
\v 3 The Lord is my firm support, and my refuge, and my deliverer; my God is my helper, I will hope in him; \add he is\add* my defender, and the horn of my salvation, and my helper. 
\q1
\v 4 I will call upon the Lord with praises, and I will be saved from my enemies. 
\q1
\v 5 The pangs of death compassed me, and the torrents of ungodliness troubled me exceedingly. 
\q1
\v 6 The pangs of hell came all around me: the snares of death prevented me. 
\p
\q1
\v 7 When I was afflicted I called upon the Lord, and cried to my God: he heard my voice out of his holy temple, and my cry will enter before him, \add even\add* into his ears. 
\p
\q1
\v 8 Then the earth shook and quaked, and the foundations of the mountains were disturbed, and were shaken, because God was angry with them. 
\q1
\v 9 There went up a smoke in his wrath, and fire burst into a flame at his presence: coals were kindled at it. 
\q1
\v 10 He bowed the heaven, and came down: and thick darkness was under his feet. 
\q1
\v 11 He mounted on cherubs and flew: he flew on the wings of winds. 
\q1
\v 12 He made darkness his secret place: all around him was his tabernacle, \add even\add* dark water in the clouds of the air. 
\q1
\v 13 At the brightness before him the clouds passed, hail and coals of fire. 
\q1
\v 14 The Lord also thundered from heaven, and the Highest uttered his voice. 
\q1
\v 15 He sent \add his\add* weapons, and scattered them; and multiplied lightnings, and routed them. 
\q1
\v 16 The springs of waters appeared, and the foundations of the world were exposed, at your rebuke, O Lord, at the blasting of the breath of your wrath. 
\p
\q1
\v 17 He sent from on high and took me, he drew me to himself out of many waters. 
\q1
\v 18 He will deliver me from my mighty enemies, and from those who hate me; for they are stronger than I. 
\q1
\v 19 They prevented me in the day of my affliction: but the Lord was my stay against \add them\add*. 
\q1
\v 20 He brought me out into a wide place: he will deliver me, because he has pleasure in me. 
\q1
\v 21 The Lord will recompense me according to my righteousness; even according to the purity of my hands he will recompense me. 
\q1
\v 22 For I have kept the ways of the Lord and have not wickedly departed from my God. 
\q1
\v 23 For all his judgments were before me, and his ordinances didn't depart from me. 
\q1
\v 24 I will be blameless with him, and will keep myself from my wickedness. 
\q1
\v 25 The Lord will recompense me according to my righteousness, and according to the purity of my hands before his eyes. 
\p
\q1
\v 26 With the holy you will be holy; and with the innocent man you will be innocent. 
\q1
\v 27 With the excellent \add man\add* you will be excellent; and with the perverse you will show frowardness. 
\q1
\v 28 For you will save the lowly people, and will humble the eyes of the proud. 
\q1
\v 29 For you, O Lord, will light my lamp: my God, you will lighten my darkness. 
\q1
\v 30 For by you I will be delivered from a troop; and by my God I will pass over a wall. 
\q1
\v 31 \add As for\add* my God, his way is perfect: the oracles of the Lord are tried in the fire; he is a protector of all those who hope in him. 
\q1
\v 32 For who is God but the Lord? And who is a God except our God? 
\p
\q1
\v 33 \add It is\add* God who girds me with strength, and has made my way blameless: 
\q1
\v 34 who strengthens my feet as hart's feet, and sets me upon high places. 
\q1
\v 35 He instructs my hands for war; and you have made my arms \add as\add* a bronze bow. 
\q1
\v 36 You have made me \f + \fr 17:36 \fqa Gr. \ft the protection of.\f*secure in my salvation: and your right hand has helped me, and your correction has upheld me to the end; yes, your correction itself will instruct me. 
\q1
\v 37 You have made room for my goings under me, and my footsteps did not fail. 
\q1
\v 38 I will pursue my enemies, and overtake them; and I will not turn back until they are consumed. 
\q1
\v 39 I will dash them to pieces and they will not be able to stand: they will fall under my feet. 
\q1
\v 40 For you have girded me with strength for war: you have beaten down under me all that rose up against me. 
\q1
\v 41 You have made my enemies turn their backs before me; and you have destroyed those who hated me. 
\q1
\v 42 They cried, but there was no deliverer: \add even\add* to the Lord, but he didn't listen to them. 
\q1
\v 43 I will grind them as the mud of the streets: and I will beat them small as dust before the wind. 
\q1
\v 44 Deliver me from the gainsayings of the people: you will make me head of the nations: a people whom I didn't know served me, 
\q1
\v 45 at the hearing of the ear they obeyed me: the foreign children \f + \fr 17:45 \fqa Or, \ft feigned obedience.\f*lied to me. 
\q1
\v 46 The foreign children waxed old, and fell away from their paths through lameness. 
\p
\q1
\v 47 The Lord lives; and blessed \add be\add* my God; and let the God of my salvation be exalted. 
\q1
\v 48 \add It is\add* God who avenges me, and has subdued the nations under me; 
\q1
\v 49 my deliverer from angry enemies: you will set me on high \f + \fr 17:49 \fqa Or, \ft out of the way of.\f*above those who rise up against me: you will deliver me from the unrighteous man. 
\q1
\v 50 Therefore will I confess to you, O Lord, among the nations, and sing to your name. 
\q1
\v 51 \add God\add* magnifies the deliverances of his king; and deals mercifully with David his anointed, and his seed, forever. 
\c 18 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm of David. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 The heavens declare the glory of God; and the firmament proclaims the work of his hands. 
\q1
\v 3 Day to day \f + \fr 18:3 \fqa Gr. \ft eructat.\f*utters speech, and night to night proclaims knowledge. 
\q1
\v 4 There are no speeches or words, \f + \fr 18:4 \fqa Gr. \ft of which.\f*in which their voices are not heard. 
\q1
\v 5 \x + \xo 18:5 \xt Rom. 10. 18.\x* Their voice is gone out into all the earth, and their words to the ends of the world. 
\q1
\v 6 In the sun he has set his tabernacle; and he comes forth as a bridegroom out of his chamber: he will exult as a giant to run his course. 
\q1
\v 7 His going forth is from the extremity of heaven, and his \f + \fr 18:7 \fqa Gr. \ft meeting.\f*circuit to the \add other\add* end of heaven: and no one will be hidden from his heat. 
\p
\q1
\v 8 The law of the Lord is \f + \fr 18:8 \fqa Gr. \ft spotless.\f*perfect, converting souls: the testimony of the Lord is faithful, instructing babes. 
\q1
\v 9 The ordinances of the Lord are right, rejoicing the heart: the commandment of the Lord is bright, enlightening the eyes. 
\q1
\v 10 The fear of the Lord is pure, enduring forever and ever: the judgments of the Lord are true, \add and\add* justified altogether. 
\q1
\v 11 To be desired more than gold, and much precious stone: sweeter also than honey and the honey-comb. 
\q1
\v 12 For your servant keeps to them: in the keeping of them \add there is\add* great reward. 
\p
\q1
\v 13 Who will understand \add his\add* transgressions? Purge you me from my secret \add sins\add*. 
\q1
\v 14 Spare your servant \add the attack\add* of strangers: if they do not gain the dominion over me, then I will be blameless, and I will be clear from great sin. 
\q1
\v 15 So will the sayings of my mouth, and the meditation of my heart, be pleasing continually before you, O Lord my helper, and my redeemer. 
\c 19 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm of David. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 The Lord hear you in the day of trouble; the name of the God of Jacob defend you. 
\q1
\v 3 Send you help from the sanctuary, and aid you out of Zion. 
\q1
\v 4 Remember all your \f + \fr 19:4 \fqa Or, \ft meat offering.\f*sacrifice, and enrich your whole-burnt-offering. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 5 Grant you according to your heart, and fulfil all your desire. 
\q1
\v 6 We will exult in your salvation, and in the name of our God will we be magnified: the Lord fulfil all your petitions. 
\p
\q1
\v 7 Now I know that the Lord has saved his Christ: he will hear him from his holy heaven: the salvation of his right hand is mighty. 
\q1
\v 8 Some \add glory\add* in chariots, and some in horses: but we will \f + \fr 19:8 \fqa Gr. \ft be magnified.\f*glory in the name of the Lord our God. 
\q1
\v 9 They are overthrown and fallen: but we are risen, and have been set upright. 
\q1
\v 10 O Lord, save the king: and hear us in whatever day we call upon you. 
\c 20 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm of David. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 O Lord, the king will rejoice in your strength; and in your salvation he will greatly exult. 
\q1
\v 3 You have granted him the desire of his soul, and have not withheld from him the request of his lips. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 4 For you have prevented him with blessings of goodness: you have set upon his head a crown of precious stone. 
\q1
\v 5 He asked life of you, and you gave him length of days forever and ever. 
\q1
\v 6 His glory is great in your salvation: you will crown him with glory and majesty. 
\q1
\v 7 For you will give him a blessing forever and ever: you will gladden him with joy with your face. 
\q1
\v 8 For the king trusts in the Lord, and through the mercy of the Highest he will not be moved. 
\p
\q1
\v 9 Let your hand be found by all your enemies: let your right hand find all that hate you. 
\q1
\v 10 You will make them as a fiery oven at the time of your presence: the Lord will trouble them in his anger, and fire will devour them. 
\q1
\v 11 You will destroy their fruit from the earth, and their seed from \add among\add* the sons of men. 
\q1
\v 12 For they intended evils against you; they imagined a device which they will by no means be able to perform. 
\q1
\v 13 For you will make them \add turn their\add* back in your latter end, you will prepare their face. 
\q1
\v 14 Be exalted, O Lord, in your strength: we will sing and praise your mighty acts. 
\c 21 
\d
\v 1 For the end, concerning the morning aid, a Psalm of David. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 \x + \xo 21:2 \xt Mat. 27. 46.\x* O God, my God, pay attention to me: why have you forsaken me? The account of my transgressions is far from my salvation. 
\q1
\v 3 O my God, I will cry to you by day, but you will not hear: and by night, and \add it will\add* not \add be accounted\add* for folly to me. 
\p
\q1
\v 4 But you, the praise of Israel, dwell in a sanctuary. 
\q1
\v 5 Our fathers hoped in you; they hoped, and you did deliver them. 
\q1
\v 6 They cried to you, and were saved: they hoped in you, and were not ashamed. 
\q1
\v 7 But I am a worm, and not a man; a reproach of men, and scorn of the people. 
\q1
\v 8 All that saw me mocked me: they spoke with \add their\add* lips, they shook the head, \add saying\add*, 
\q1
\v 9 He hoped in the Lord: let him deliver him, let him save him, because he takes pleasure in him. 
\q1
\v 10 For you are he who drew me out of the womb; my hope from my mother's breasts. 
\q1
\v 11 I was cast on you from the womb: you are my God from my mother's belly. 
\p
\q1
\v 12 Stand not aloof from me; for affliction is near; for there is no helper. 
\q1
\v 13 Many \f + \fr 21:13 \fqa Gr. \ft calves.\f*bullocks have compassed me: fat bulls have beset me round. 
\q1
\v 14 They have opened their mouth against me, as a ravening and roaring lion. 
\q1
\v 15 I am poured out like water, and all my bones are loosened: my heart among my belly is become like melting wax. 
\q1
\v 16 My strength is dried up like a potsherd; and my tongue is glued to my throat; and you have brought me down to the dust of death. 
\q1
\v 17 For many dogs have compassed me: the assembly of the wicked doers has beset me round: they pierced my hands and my feet. 
\q1
\v 18 They counted all my bones; and they observed and looked upon me. 
\q1
\v 19 \x + \xo 21:19 \xt Mat. 27. 35.\x* They parted my garments \add among\add* themselves, and cast lots upon my clothing. 
\p
\q1
\v 20 But you, O Lord, remove not my help afar off: be ready for my aid. 
\q1
\v 21 Deliver my soul from the sword; my only-begotten one from the power of the dog. 
\q1
\v 22 Save me from the lion's mouth; and \add regard\add* my \f + \fr 21:22 \ft See \fqa Hebrew.\f*lowliness from the horns of the unicorns. 
\p
\q1
\v 23 I will declare your name to my brothers: among the church will I sing praise to you. 
\q1
\v 24 You who fear the Lord, praise him; all you seed of Jacob, glorify him: let all the seed of Israel fear him. 
\q1
\v 25 For he has not despised nor been angry at the supplication of the poor; nor turned away his face from me; but when I cried to him, he heard me. 
\q1
\v 26 My praise is of you in the great congregation: I will pay my vows before those who fear him. 
\p
\q1
\v 27 The poor will eat and be satisfied; and they will praise the Lord who seek him: their heart will live forever. 
\q1
\v 28 All the ends of the earth will remember and turn to the Lord: and all the kindreds of the nations will worship before him. 
\q1
\v 29 For the kingdom is the Lord's; and he is the governor of the nations. 
\q1
\v 30 All the fat ones of the earth have eaten and worshipped: all that go down to the earth will fall down before him: my soul also lives to him. 
\q1
\v 31 My seed will serve him: the generation that is coming will be reported to the Lord. 
\q1
\v 32 They will report his righteousness to the people that will be born, whom the Lord has made. 
\c 22 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm of David. 
\p The Lord tends me as a shepherd, and I will want nothing. 
\q1
\v 2 In a place of green grass, there he has made me dwell: he has nourished me by the water of rest. 
\q1
\v 3 He has restored my soul: he has guided me into the paths of righteousness, for his name's sake. 
\q1
\v 4 Yes, even if I should walk among the shadow of death, I will not be afraid of evils: for you are with me; your rod and your staff, these have comforted me. 
\q1
\v 5 You have prepared a table before me in presence of those who afflict me: you have thoroughly anointed my head with oil; and your cup cheers me like the best \add wine\add*. 
\q1
\v 6 Your mercy also will follow me all the days of my life: and my dwelling \add will be\add* in the house of the Lord for a very long time. 
\c 23 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm for David on the first day of the week. 
\p The earth is the Lord's and the fulness of it; the world, and all that dwell in it. 
\q1
\v 2 He has founded it upon the seas, and prepared it upon the rivers. 
\p
\q1
\v 3 Who will go up to the mountain of the Lord, and who will stand in his holy place? 
\q1
\v 4 He who is innocent in his hands and pure in his heart; who has not lifted up his soul to vanity, nor sworn deceitfully \f + \fr 23:4 \fqa Or, \ft against.\f*to his neighbour. 
\q1
\v 5 He will receive a blessing from the Lord, and mercy from God his Saviour. 
\q1
\v 6 This is the generation of those who seek him, that seek the face of the God of Jacob. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 7 Lift up your gates, you princes, and be lifted up, you everlasting doors; and the king of glory will come in. 
\q1
\v 8 Who is this king of glory? The Lord strong and mighty, the Lord mighty in battle. 
\q1
\v 9 Lift up your gates, you princes; and be lift up, you everlasting doors; and the king of glory will come in. 
\q1
\v 10 Who is this king of glory? The Lord of hosts, he is this king of glory. 
\c 24 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm of David. 
\p To you, O Lord, have I lifted up my soul. 
\q1
\v 2 O my God, I have trusted in you: don't let me be greatly agitated, neither let my enemies laugh me to scorn. 
\q1
\v 3 For none of those who wait on you will in any wise be ashamed: let them be ashamed that transgress without cause. 
\q1
\v 4 Show me your ways, O Lord; and teach me your paths. 
\q1
\v 5 Lead me in your truth, and teach me: for you are God my Saviour: and I have waited on you all the day. 
\q1
\v 6 Remember your compassions, O Lord, and your mercies, for they are from everlasting. 
\q1
\v 7 Don't remember the sins of my youth, nor \add my sins\add* of ignorance: remember me according to your mercy, for your goodness' sake, O Lord. 
\p
\q1
\v 8 Good and upright is the Lord: therefore will he \f + \fr 24:8 \fqa sc. \ft as a law-giver.\f*instruct sinners in \add the\add* way. 
\q1
\v 9 The meek will he guide in judgment: the meek will he teach his ways. 
\q1
\v 10 All the streets of the Lord are mercy and truth to those who seek his covenant and his testimonies. 
\q1
\v 11 For your name's sake, O Lord, do you also be merciful to my sin; for it is great. 
\q1
\v 12 Who is the man who fears the Lord? He will instruct him in the way which he has chosen. 
\q1
\v 13 His soul will dwell in prosperity; and his seed will inherit the earth. 
\q1
\v 14 The Lord is the strength of those who fear him; and his covenant is to manifest \f + \fr 24:14 \fqa Or, \ft 'it,' \fqa sc. \ft what has just been stated.\f*\add truth\add* to them. 
\p
\q1
\v 15 My eyes are continually to the Lord; for he will draw my feet out of the snare. 
\q1
\v 16 Look upon me, and have mercy upon me; for I am an only child and poor. 
\q1
\v 17 The afflictions of my heart have been multiplied; deliver me from my distresses. 
\q1
\v 18 Look upon my affliction and my trouble; and forgive all my sins. 
\q1
\v 19 Look upon my enemies; for they have been multiplied; and they have hated me with unjust hatred. 
\q1
\v 20 Keep my soul, and deliver me: don't let me be ashamed; for I have hoped in you. 
\q1
\v 21 The harmless and upright joined themselves to me: for I waited for you, O Lord. 
\q1
\v 22 Deliver Israel, O God, out of all his afflictions. 
\c 25 
\d
\v 1 \add A Psalm\add* of David. 
\p Judge me, O Lord; for I have walked in my innocence: and hoping in the Lord I will not be moved. 
\q1
\v 2 Prove me, O Lord, and try me; purify as with fire my reins and my heart. 
\p
\q1
\v 3 For your mercy is before my eyes: and I am well pleased with your truth. 
\q1
\v 4 I have not sat with the council of vanity, and will not enter in with transgressors. 
\q1
\v 5 I have hated the assembly of wicked doers; and will not sit with ungodly \add men\add*. 
\q1
\v 6 I will wash my hands in \f + \fr 25:6 \fqa Gr. \ft innocent \fqa things.\f*innocency, and compass your altar, O Lord: 
\q1
\v 7 to hear the voice of praise, and to declare all your wonderful works. 
\q1
\v 8 O Lord, I have loved the beauty of your house, and the place of the tabernacle of your glory. 
\q1
\v 9 Don't destroy my soul together with the ungodly, nor my life with bloody men: 
\q1
\v 10 in whose hands \add are\add* iniquities, \add and\add* their right hand is filled with bribes. 
\q1
\v 11 But I have walked in my innocence: redeem me, and have mercy upon me. 
\q1
\v 12 My foot stands in \f + \fr 25:12 \fqa Gr. \ft in evenness or uprightness.\f*an even place: in the congregations will I bless you, O Lord. 
\c 26 
\d
\v 1 \add A Psalm\add* of David, before he was anointed. 
\p The Lord is my light and my Saviour; whom will I fear? The Lord is the defender of my life; of whom will I be afraid? 
\q1
\v 2 When evil-doers drew near against me to eat up my flesh, my persecutors and my enemies, they fainted and fell. 
\q1
\v 3 Though an army should set itself in array against me, my heart will not be afraid: though war should rise up against me, in this am I confident. 
\q1
\v 4 One thing have I asked of the Lord, this will I earnestly seek: that I should dwell in the house of the Lord all the days of my life, that I should behold the fair beauty of the Lord, and survey his temple. 
\q1
\v 5 For in the day of my afflictions he hid me in his tabernacle: he sheltered me in the secret of his tabernacle; he set me up on a rock. 
\q1
\v 6 Now, behold, he has lifted up my head over my enemies: I went round and offered in his tabernacle the sacrifice of \f + \fr 26:6 \fqa Gr. \ft shouting.\f*joy; I will sing, \f + \fr 26:6 \fqa Or, \ft and play on a psaltery.\f*even sing psalms to the Lord. 
\p
\q1
\v 7 Hear, O Lord, my voice which I have uttered aloud: pity me, and listen to me. 
\q1
\v 8 My heart said to you, I have diligently sought your face: your face, O Lord, I will seek. 
\q1
\v 9 Don't turn your face away from me, don't turn away from your servant in anger: be you my helper, don't forsake me; and, O God my Saviour, overlook me not. 
\q1
\v 10 For my father and my mother have forsaken me, but the Lord has taken me to himself. 
\q1
\v 11 Teach me, O Lord, in your way, and guide me in a right path, because of my enemies. 
\q1
\v 12 Don't deliver me over to the desire of those who afflict me; for unjust witnesses have risen up against me, and injustice has lied within herself. 
\p
\q1
\v 13 I believe that I will see the \f + \fr 26:13 \fqa Gr. \ft good \fqa things.\f*goodness of the Lord in the land of the living. 
\q1
\v 14 Wait on the Lord: be of good courage, and let your heart be strengthened: yes, wait on the Lord. 
\c 27 
\d
\v 1 \add A Psalm\add* of David. 
\p To you, O Lord, have I cried; my God, don't be silent toward me: lest you be silent toward me, and so I should be likened to those who go down to the pit. 
\q1
\v 2 Listen to the voice of my supplication, when I pray to you, when I lift up my hands toward your holy temple. 
\q1
\v 3 Don't draw away my soul with sinners, and don't destroy me with the workers of wickedness, who speak peace with their neighbours, but evils are in their hearts. 
\q1
\v 4 Give them according to their works, and according to the wickedness of their devices: give them according to the works of their hands; give their recompence to them. 
\q1
\v 5 Because they have not attended to the works of the Lord, even to the works of his hands, you will pull them down, and will not build them up. 
\p
\q1
\v 6 Blessed be the Lord, for he has listened to the voice of my petition. 
\q1
\v 7 The Lord is my helper and my defender; my heart has hoped in him, and I am helped: my flesh has revived, and willingly will I \f + \fr 27:7 \fqa Or, \ft confess to him.\f*give praise to him. 
\q1
\v 8 The Lord is the strength of his people, and the \f + \fr 27:8 \fqa Gr. \ft defender of the salvation of.\f*saving defender of his anointed. 
\p
\q1
\v 9 Save your people, and bless your inheritance: and take care of them, and lift them up forever. 
\c 28 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm of David \add on the occasion\add* of the solemn assembly of the Tabernacle. 
\p Bring to the Lord, you sons of God, bring to the Lord young rams; bring to the Lord glory and honour. 
\q1
\v 2 Bring to the Lord glory, \add due\add* to his name; worship the Lord in his holy court. 
\p
\q1
\v 3 The voice of the Lord is upon the waters: the God of glory has thundered: the Lord is upon many waters. 
\q1
\v 4 The voice of the Lord is mighty; the voice of the Lord is full of majesty. 
\q1
\v 5 \add There is\add* the voice of the Lord who breaks the cedars; the Lord will break the cedars of Lebanon. 
\q1
\v 6 He will beat them small, \add even\add* Lebanon itself, like a calf; and the beloved one is as a young unicorn. 
\q1
\v 7 \add There is\add* a voice of the Lord who divides a flame of fire. 
\q1
\v 8 A voice of the Lord who shakes the wilderness; the Lord will shake the wilderness of Cades. 
\q1
\v 9 The voice of the Lord \f + \fr 28:9 \fqa Gr. \ft participle.\f*strengthens the hinds, and will uncover the thickets: and in his temple every one speaks \add of his\add* glory. 
\q1
\v 10 The Lord will dwell on the waterflood: and the Lord will sit a king forever. 
\q1
\v 11 The Lord will give strength to his people; the Lord will bless his people with peace. 
\c 29 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm \f + \fr 29:1 \fqa Gr. \ft of a song.\f*and Song at the dedication of the house of David. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 I will exalt you, O Lord; for you have lifted me up, and not caused my enemies to rejoice over me. 
\q1
\v 3 O Lord my God, I cried to you, and you did heal me. 
\q1
\v 4 O Lord, you have brought up my soul from Hades, you have delivered me from \add among\add* those who go down to the pit. 
\p
\q1
\v 5 Sing to the Lord, you his saints, and give thanks for the remembrance of his holiness. 
\q1
\v 6 For anger is in his wrath, but life in his favour: weeping will tarry for the evening, but joy will be in the morning. 
\p
\q1
\v 7 I said in my prosperity, I will never be moved. 
\q1
\v 8 O Lord, in your good pleasure you did add strength to my beauty: but you did turn away your face, and I was troubled. 
\q1
\v 9 To you, O Lord, will I cry; and to my God will I make supplication. 
\q1
\v 10 What profit is there in my blood, when I go down to destruction? Will the dust give praise to you? Or will it declare your truth? 
\q1
\v 11 The Lord heard, and had compassion upon me; the Lord is become my helper. 
\q1
\v 12 You have turned my mourning into joy for me: you have rent off my sackcloth, and girded me with gladness; 
\q1
\v 13 that my glory may sing praise to you, and I may not be pierced \add with sorrow\add*. O Lord my God, I will give thanks to you forever. 
\c 30 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm of David, \add an utterance\add* of \f + \fr 30:1 \fqa Gr. \ft ecstasy. See title.\f*extreme fear. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 O Lord, I have hoped in you; let me never be ashamed: deliver me in your righteousness and rescue me. 
\q1
\v 3 Incline your ear to me; make haste to rescue me: be to me for a protecting God, and for a house of refuge to save me. 
\q1
\v 4 For you are my strength and my refuge; and you will guide me for your name's sake, and maintain me. 
\q1
\v 5 You will bring me out of the snare which they have hidden for me; for you, O Lord, are my defender. 
\q1
\v 6 Into your hands I will commit my spirit: you have redeemed me, O Lord God of truth. 
\q1
\v 7 You have hated those who idly persist in vanities: but I have hoped in the Lord. 
\q1
\v 8 I will exult and be glad in your mercy: for you have looked upon my affliction; you have saved my soul from distresses. 
\q1
\v 9 You have not shut me up into the hands of the enemy: you have set my feet in a wide place. 
\p
\q1
\v 10 Pity me, O Lord, for I am afflicted: my eye is troubled with indignation, my soul and my belly. 
\q1
\v 11 For my life is spent with grief, and my years with groanings: my strength has been weakened through poverty, and my bones are troubled. 
\q1
\v 12 I became a reproach among all my enemies, but exceedingly so to my neighbours, and a fear to my acquaintance: those who saw me without fled from me. 
\q1
\v 13 I have been forgotten as a dead man out of mind: I have become as a broken vessel. 
\q1
\v 14 For I heard the slander of many that dwelt all around: when they were gathered together against me, they took counsel to take my life. 
\p
\q1
\v 15 But I hoped in you, O Lord: I said, You are my God. 
\q1
\v 16 My lots are in your hands: deliver me from the hand of my enemies, 
\q1
\v 17 and from those who persecute me. Make your face to shine upon your servant: save me in your mercy. 
\q1
\v 18 O Lord, don't let me be ashamed, for I have called upon you: let the ungodly be ashamed, and brought down to Hades. 
\q1
\v 19 Let the deceitful lips become dumb, which speak wickedness against the righteous with pride and scorn. 
\p
\q1
\v 20 How abundant is the multitude of your goodness, O Lord, which you have laid up for those who fear you! You have worked \add it\add* out for those who hope on you, in the presence of the sons of men. 
\q1
\v 21 You will hide them in the secret of your presence from the vexation of man: you will screen them in a tabernacle from the contradiction of tongues. 
\q1
\v 22 Blessed be the Lord: for he has magnified his mercy in a fortified city. 
\q1
\v 23 But I said in my extreme fear, I am cast out from the sight of your eyes: therefore you did listen, O Lord, to the voice of my supplication when I cried to you. 
\p
\q1
\v 24 Love the Lord, all you his saints: for the Lord seeks for truth, and renders \add a reward\add* to those who deal very proudly. 
\q1
\v 25 Be of good courage, and let your heart be strengthened, all you who hope in the Lord. 
\c 31 
\d
\v 1 \add A Psalm\add* of \f + \fr 31:1 \fqa Gr. \ft for \fqa or, \ft of.\f*instruction by David. 
\p \x + \xo 31:1 \xt Rom. 4. 7,8.\x* Blessed \add are they\add* whose transgressions are forgiven, and whose sins are covered. 
\q1
\v 2 Blessed is the man to whom the Lord will not impute sin, and in whose mouth there is no guile. 
\p
\q1
\v 3 Because I kept silence, my bones waxed old, from my crying all the day. 
\q1
\v 4 For day and night your hand was heavy upon me: I became thoroughly miserable while a \f + \fr 31:4 \ft See \fqa Heb.\f*thorn was fastened in \add me\add*. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 5 I acknowledged my sin, and hid not my wickedness: I said, I will confess my wickedness to the Lord against myself; and you forgavest the ungodliness of my heart. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 6 Therefore will every holy one pray to you in a fit time: only in the deluge of many waters they will not come near to him. 
\q1
\v 7 You are my refuge from the affliction that encompasses me; my joy, to deliver me from those who have compassed me. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 8 I will instruct you and guide you in this way wherein you will go: I will fix my eyes upon you. 
\q1
\v 9 Don't you be as horse and mule, which have no understanding: \f + \fr 31:9 \ft See \fqa Alex. \ft ἄγξεις.\f*\add but you must\add* constrain their jaws with bit and curb, lest they should come near to you. 
\q1
\v 10 Many are the scourges of the sinner: but him that hopes in the Lord mercy will compass about. 
\q1
\v 11 Be glad in the Lord, and exult, you righteous: and glory, all you who are upright in heart. 
\c 32 
\d
\v 1 \add A Psalm\add* of David. 
\p Rejoice in the Lord, you righteous; praise becomes the upright. 
\q1
\v 2 \f + \fr 32:2 \ft Rather, 'confess' \fqa or \ft give thanks to.'\f*Praise the Lord on the harp; play to him on a psaltery of ten strings. 
\q1
\v 3 Sing to him a new song; play skilfully with a loud noise. 
\p
\q1
\v 4 For the word of the Lord is right; and all his works are \f + \fr 32:4 \ft Rather, \fqa Gr. \ft in \fqa or \ft with faithfulness.\f*faithful. 
\q1
\v 5 He loves mercy and judgment; the earth is full of the mercy of the Lord. 
\q1
\v 6 By the word of the Lord the heavens were established; and all the host of them by the breath of his \add mouth\add*. 
\q1
\v 7 Who gathers the waters of the sea as \add in\add* a bottle; who lays up the deeps in treasuries. 
\q1
\v 8 Let all the earth fear the Lord; and let all that dwell in the world be moved because of him. 
\q1
\v 9 For he spoke, and they were made; he commanded, and they were created. 
\q1
\v 10 The Lord frustrates the counsels of the nations; he brings to nought also the reasonings of the peoples, and brings to nought the counsels of princes. 
\q1
\v 11 But the counsel of the Lord endures forever, the thoughts of his heart from generation to generation. 
\q1
\v 12 Blessed is the nation whose God is the Lord; the people whom he has chosen for his own inheritance. 
\q1
\v 13 The Lord looks out of heaven; he beholds all the sons of men. 
\q1
\v 14 He looks from his prepared habitation on all the dwellers on the earth; 
\q1
\v 15 who fashioned their hearts \f + \fr 32:15 \ft Perhaps 'individually.' \fqa Vulg. \ft sigillatim.\f*alone; who understands all their works. 
\q1
\v 16 A king isn't saved because of a great host; and a giant will not be delivered by the greatness of his strength. 
\q1
\v 17 A horse is vain for safety; neither he will be delivered by the greatness of his power. 
\p
\q1
\v 18 Behold, the eyes of the Lord are on those who fear him, those that hope in his mercy; 
\q1
\v 19 to deliver their souls from death, and to keep them alive in famine. 
\q1
\v 20 Our soul waits on the Lord; for he is our helper and defender. 
\q1
\v 21 For our heart will rejoice in him, and we have hoped in his holy name. 
\q1
\v 22 Let your mercy, O Lord, be upon us, according as we have hoped in you. 
\c 33 
\d
\v 1 \add A Psalm\add* of David, when he changed his face before Abimelech; and he let him go, and he departed. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 I will bless the Lord at all times: his praise will be continually in my mouth. 
\q1
\v 3 My soul will \f + \fr 33:3 \fqa Gr. \ft be praised.\f*boast herself in the Lord: let the meek hear, and rejoice. 
\q1
\v 4 Magnify you the Lord with me, and let us exalt his name together. 
\p
\q1
\v 5 I sought the Lord diligently, and he listened to me, and delivered me from all my \f + \fr 33:5 \fqa Lit. \ft neighbourhoods.\f*sojournings. 
\q1
\v 6 Draw near to him, and be enlightened: and your faces will not \add by any means\add* be ashamed. 
\q1
\v 7 This poor man cried, and the Lord listened to him, and delivered him out of all his afflictions. 
\q1
\v 8 The angel of the Lord will encamp all around those who fear him, and will deliver them. 
\q1
\v 9 Taste and see that the Lord is good: blessed is the man who hopes in him. 
\q1
\v 10 Fear the Lord, all you his saints: for there is no want to those who fear him. 
\q1
\v 11 The rich have become poor and hungry: but those who seek the Lord diligently will not want any good thing. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 12 Come, you children, hear me: I will teach you the fear of the Lord. 
\q1
\v 13 \x + \xo 33:13 \xt 1 Pet. 3. 10-13.\x* What man is there that desires life, loving to see good days? 
\q1
\v 14 Keep your tongue from evil, and your lips from speaking guile. 
\q1
\v 15 Turn away from evil, and do good; seek peace, and pursue it. 
\p
\q1
\v 16 The eyes of the Lord are over the righteous, and his ears \add are open\add* to their prayer: 
\q1
\v 17 but the face of the Lord is against those who do evil, to destroy their memorial from the earth. The righteous cried, and the Lord listened to them, 
\q1
\v 18 and delivered them out of all their afflictions. 
\q1
\v 19 The Lord is near to \f + \fr 33:19 \fqa Gr. \ft the broken in heart.\f*those who are of a contrite heart; and will save the lowly in spirit. 
\q1
\v 20 Many are the afflictions of the righteous: but out of them all the Lord will deliver them. 
\q1
\v 21 He keeps all their bones: not one of them will be broken. 
\q1
\v 22 The death of sinners is evil: and those who hate righteousness will go wrong. 
\q1
\v 23 The Lord will redeem the souls of his servants: and none of those that hope in him will go wrong. 
\c 34 
\d
\v 1 \add A Psalm\add* of David. 
\p Judge you, O Lord, those who injure me, fight against those who fight against me. 
\q1
\v 2 Take hold of shield and buckler, and arise for my help. 
\q1
\v 3 Bring forth a sword, and stop \add the way\add* against those who persecute me: say to my soul, I am your salvation. 
\q1
\v 4 Let those who seek my soul be ashamed and greatly agitated: let those who devise evils against me be turned back and put to shame. 
\q1
\v 5 Let them be as dust before the wind, and an angel of the Lord afflicting them. 
\q1
\v 6 Let their way be dark and slippery, and an angel of the Lord persecuting them. 
\q1
\v 7 For without cause they have hid for me their destructive snare: without a cause they have reproached my soul. 
\p
\q1
\v 8 Let a snare which they don't know come upon them: and the gin which they hid take them; and let them fall into the very same snare. 
\q1
\v 9 But my soul will exult in the Lord: it will delight in his salvation. 
\q1
\v 10 All my bones will say, O Lord, who is like to you? Delivering the poor out of the hand of those who are stronger than he, yes, the poor and needy one from those who spoil him. 
\p
\q1
\v 11 Unjust witnesses arose, and asked me of things I didn't know. 
\q1
\v 12 They rewarded me evil for good, and bereavement to my soul. 
\q1
\v 13 But I, when they troubled me, put on sackcloth, and humbled my soul with fasting: and my prayer will return to my \add own\add* bosom. 
\q1
\v 14 I behaved agreeably towards them as \add if it had been\add* our neighbour \add or\add* brother: I humbled myself as one mourning and sad of face. 
\q1
\v 15 Yet they rejoiced against me, and plagues were \f + \fr 34:15 \ft The \fqa Gr. \ft is repeated, by a \fqa Hebraism.\f*plentifully brought against me, and I didn't know \add it\add*: they were scattered, but \f + \fr 34:15 \ft See \xt Acts 2. 37.\f*didn't repent. 
\q1
\v 16 They tempted me, they sneered at me most contemptuously, they gnashed their teeth upon me. 
\p
\q1
\v 17 O Lord, when will you look upon me? Deliver my soul from their mischief, my only-begotten one from the lions. 
\q1
\v 18 I will give thanks to you even in a great congregation: in an abundant people I will praise you. 
\q1
\v 19 Don't let those who are my enemies without a cause rejoice against me; who hate me for nothing, and wink with their eyes. 
\q1
\v 20 For to me they spoke peaceably, but imagined deceits in \add their\add* anger. 
\q1
\v 21 They opened wide their mouth upon me; they said, Aha, aha, our eyes have seen \add it\add*. 
\p
\q1
\v 22 You have seen \add it\add*, O Lord: don't keep silence: O Lord, withdraw not \add yourself\add* from me. 
\q1
\v 23 Awake, O Lord, and pay attention to my judgment, \add even\add* to my cause, my God and my Lord. 
\q1
\v 24 Judge me, O Lord, according to your righteousness, O Lord my God; and don't let them rejoice against me. 
\q1
\v 25 Don't let them say in their hearts, Aha, aha, \add it is pleasing\add* to our soul: neither let them say, We have devoured him. 
\q1
\v 26 Let them be greatly agitated and ashamed together that rejoice at my afflictions: let them be clothed with shame and confusion that speak great swelling words against me. 
\q1
\v 27 Let those who rejoice in my righteousness exult and be glad: and let them say continually, The Lord be magnified, who desire the peace of his servant. 
\q1
\v 28 My tongue will meditate on your righteousness, \add and\add* on your praise all the day. 
\c 35 
\d
\v 1 For the end, by David the servant of the Lord. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 The transgressor, that he may sin, says within himself, \add that\add* \x + \xo 35:2 \xt Rom. 3. 18.\x* there is no fear of God before his eyes. 
\q1
\v 3 For he has dealt craftily before him, \f + \fr 35:3 \fqa q. d. \ft with regard to the discovering.\f*to discover his wickedness and hate it. 
\q1
\v 4 The words of his mouth are transgression and deceit: he isn't inclined to understand \add how\add* to do good. 
\q1
\v 5 He devises wickedness on his bed; he gives himself to every evil way; and does not abhor evil. 
\p
\q1
\v 6 O Lord, your mercy is in the heaven; and your truth \add reaches\add* to the clouds. 
\q1
\v 7 Your righteousness is as the \f + \fr 35:7 \fqa Or, \ft vast mountains.\f*mountains of God, your judgments are as a great deep: O Lord, you will preserve men and beasts. 
\q1
\v 8 How have you multiplied your mercy, O God! So the children of men will trust in the shelter of your wings. 
\q1
\v 9 They will be \f + \fr 35:9 \fqa Gr. \ft intoxicated.\f*fully satisfied with the fatness of your house; and you will cause them to drink of the full stream of your delights. 
\q1
\v 10 For with you is the fountain of life: in your light we will see light. 
\p
\q1
\v 11 Extend your mercy to those who know you; and your righteousness to the upright in heart. 
\q1
\v 12 Don't let the foot of pride come against me, and don't let the hand of sinners move me. 
\p
\q1
\v 13 There have all the workers of wickedness fallen: they are cast out, and will not be able to stand. 
\c 36 
\d
\v 1 \add A Psalm\add* of David. 
\p Fret not yourself because of evil-doers, neither be envious of those who do wickedness. 
\q1
\v 2 For they will soon be withered as the grass, and will soon fall away as the green herbs. 
\q1
\v 3 Hope in the Lord, and do good; and dwell on the land, and you will be fed with the wealth of it. 
\q1
\v 4 Delight \add yourself\add* in the Lord; and he will grant you the requests of your heart. 
\q1
\v 5 Disclose your way to the Lord, and hope in him; and he will bring \add it\add* to pass. 
\q1
\v 6 He will bring forth your righteousness as the light, and your judgment as the noon-day. 
\p
\q1
\v 7 Submit yourself to the Lord, and supplicate him: fret not yourself because of him that prospers in his way, at the man who does unlawful deeds. 
\q1
\v 8 Cease from anger, and forsake wrath: fret not yourself so as to do evil. 
\q1
\v 9 For evil-doers will be destroyed: but those who wait on the Lord, they will inherit the land. 
\q1
\v 10 Yet a little while, and the sinner will not be, and you will seek for his place, and will not find \add it\add*. 
\q1
\v 11 But the meek will inherit the earth; and will delight \add themselves\add* in the abundance of peace. 
\p
\q1
\v 12 The sinner will watch for the righteous, and gnash his teeth upon him. 
\q1
\v 13 But the Lord will laugh at him: for he foresees that his day will come. 
\q1
\v 14 Sinners have drawn their swords, they have bent their bow, to cast down the poor and needy one, \add and\add* to kill the upright in heart. 
\q1
\v 15 Let their sword enter into their \add own\add* heart, and their bows be broken. 
\p
\q1
\v 16 A little is better to the righteous than abundant wealth of sinners. 
\q1
\v 17 For the arms of sinners will be broken; but the Lord supports the righteous. 
\p
\q1
\v 18 The Lord knows the ways of the perfect; and their inheritance will be forever. 
\q1
\v 19 They will not be ashamed in an evil time; and in days of famine they will be satisfied. 
\q1
\v 20 For the sinners will perish; and the enemies of the Lord at the moment of their being honoured and exalted have completely vanished like smoke. 
\q1
\v 21 The sinner borrows, and will not pay again: but the righteous has compassion, and gives. 
\q1
\v 22 For those who bless him will inherit the earth; and those who curse him will be completely destroyed. 
\p
\q1
\v 23 The steps of a man are rightly ordered by the Lord: and he will take pleasure in his way. 
\q1
\v 24 When he falls, he will not be ruined: for the Lord supports his hand. 
\q1
\v 25 I was \add once\add* young, indeed I am now old; yet I have not seen the righteous forsaken, nor his seed seeking bread. 
\q1
\v 26 He is merciful, and lends continually; and his seed will be \f + \fr 36:26 \fqa Gr. \ft for a blessing.\f*blessed. 
\p
\q1
\v 27 Turn aside from evil, and do good; and dwell forever. 
\q1
\v 28 For the Lord loves judgment, and will not forsake his saints; they will be preserved forever: the blameless will be \f + \fr 36:28 \fqa Or, \ft cleared in judgement.\f*avenged, but the seed of the ungodly will be completely destroyed. 
\q1
\v 29 But the righteous will inherit the earth, and dwell upon it forever. 
\p
\q1
\v 30 The mouth of the righteous will meditate wisdom, and his tongue will speak of judgment. 
\q1
\v 31 The law of his God is in his heart; and his steps will not \f + \fr 36:31 \fqa Gr. \ft be tripped up, or supplanted.\f*slide. 
\q1
\v 32 The sinner watches the righteous, and seeks to kill him. 
\q1
\v 33 But the Lord will not leave him in his hands, nor by any means condemn him when he is judged. 
\q1
\v 34 Wait on the Lord, and keep his way, and he will exalt you to inherit the land: when the wicked are destroyed, you will see \add it\add*. 
\p
\q1
\v 35 I saw the ungodly very highly exalting himself, and lifting himself up like the cedars of Lebanon. 
\q1
\v 36 Yet I passed by, and lo! He was not: and I sought him, but his place was not found. 
\q1
\v 37 Maintain innocence, and behold uprightness: for there is a remnant to the peaceable man. 
\q1
\v 38 But the transgressors will be completely destroyed together: the remnants of the ungodly will be completely destroyed. 
\q1
\v 39 But the salvation of the righteous is of the Lord; and he is their defender in the time of affliction. 
\q1
\v 40 The Lord will help them, and deliver them: and he will rescue them from sinners, and save them, because they have hoped in him. 
\c 37 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm of David for remembrance concerning the Sabbath-day. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 O Lord, rebuke me not in your wrath, neither chasten me in your anger. 
\q1
\v 3 For your weapons are fixed in me, and you have pressed your hand heavily upon me. 
\p
\q1
\v 4 For there is no health in my flesh because of your anger; there is no peace to my bones because of my sins. 
\q1
\v 5 For my transgressions have gone over my head: they have pressed heavily upon me like a weighty burden. 
\q1
\v 6 My bruises have become noisome and corrupt, because of my foolishness. 
\q1
\v 7 I have been wretched and bowed down continually: I went with a mourning face all the day. 
\q1
\v 8 For my soul is filled with mockings; and there is no health in my flesh. 
\q1
\v 9 I have been afflicted and brought down exceedingly: I have roared for the groaning of my heart. 
\p
\q1
\v 10 But all my desire is before you; and my groaning isn't hidden from you. 
\q1
\v 11 My heart is troubled, my strength has failed me; and the light of my eyes isn't with me. 
\q1
\v 12 My friends and my neighbours drew near before me, and stood still; and my nearest of kin stood afar off. 
\q1
\v 13 While they pressed hard upon me that sought my soul: and those who sought my hurt spoke vanities, and devised deceits all the day. 
\q1
\v 14 But I, as a deaf man, didn't hear; and was as a dumb man not opening his mouth. 
\q1
\v 15 I was as a man who hears not, and who has no reproofs in his mouth. 
\p
\q1
\v 16 For I hoped in you, O Lord: you will hear, O Lord my God. 
\q1
\v 17 For I said, Lest my enemies rejoice against me: for when my feet were moved, they spoke boastingly against me. 
\q1
\v 18 For I am ready for \f + \fr 37:18 \fqa Gr. \ft scourges.\f*plagues, and my grief is continually before me. 
\q1
\v 19 For I will declare my wickedness, and be distressed for my sin. 
\q1
\v 20 But my enemies live, and are mightier than I: and those who hate me unjustly are multiplied. 
\q1
\v 21 Those who reward evil for good slandered me; because I followed righteousness. 
\q1
\v 22 Don't forsake me, O Lord my God: don't depart from me. 
\q1
\v 23 Draw near to my help, O Lord of my salvation. 
\c 38 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Song of David, to Idithun. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 I said, I will take heed to my ways, that I sin not with my tongue: I set a guard on my mouth, while the sinner stood in my presence. 
\q1
\v 3 I was dumb, and humbled myself, and kept silence from good \add words\add*; and my grief was renewed. 
\q1
\v 4 My heart grew hot within me, and a fire would kindle in my meditation: I spoke with my tongue, 
\p
\q1
\v 5 O Lord, make me to know my end, and the number of my days, what it is; that I may know what I lack. 
\q1
\v 6 Behold, you have made my days \f + \fr 38:6 \fqa Alex. \ft a span long.\f*old; and my existence \add is\add* as nothing before you: no, every man living \add is\add* altogether vanity. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 7 Surely man walks in a \f + \fr 38:7 \fqa Gr. \ft image.\f*shadow; no, he is disquieted in vain: he lays up treasures, and doesn't know for whom he will gather them. 
\p
\q1
\v 8 Now what \add is\add* my expectation? \add is it\add* not the Lord? And my ground \add of hope\add* is with you. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 9 Deliver me from all my transgressions: you have made me a reproach to the foolish. 
\q1
\v 10 I was \f + \fr 38:10 \fqa Gr. \ft made dumb.\f*dumb, and opened not my mouth; for you are he who made me. 
\q1
\v 11 Remove your scourges from me: I have fainted because of the strength of your hand. 
\q1
\v 12 You chastenest man with rebukes for wickedness, and you makest his life to consume away like a spider's web: no, every man is disquieted in vain. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 13 O Lord, listen to my prayer and my supplication: pay attention to my tears: don't be silent, for I am a sojourner in the land, and a stranger, as all my fathers \add were\add*. 
\q1
\v 14 Spare me, that I may be refreshed, before I depart, and be no more. 
\c 39 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm of David. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 I waited patiently for the Lord; and he attended to me, and listened to my supplication. 
\q1
\v 3 He brought me up out of a pit of misery, and from miry clay: and he set my feet on a rock, and ordered my goings aright. 
\q1
\v 4 He put a new song into my mouth, \add even\add* a hymn to our God: many will see \add it\add*, and fear, and will hope in the Lord. 
\q1
\v 5 Blessed \add is\add* the man whose hope is the name of the Lord, and \add who\add* has not regarded vanities and false frenzies. 
\p
\q1
\v 6 O Lord my God, you have multiplied your wonderful works, and in your thoughts there is no one who will be likened to you: I declared and spoke \add of them\add*: they exceeded number. 
\q1
\v 7 \x + \xo 39:7 \xt Heb. 10. 5,6.\x* Sacrifice and offering you would not; but a body have you prepared me: whole-burnt-offering and \add sacrifice\add* for sin you did not require. 
\q1
\v 8 Then I said, Behold, I \f + \fr 39:8 \fqa Or, \ft am come.\f*come: in the volume of the book it is written concerning me, 
\q1
\v 9 I desired to do your will, O my God, and your law among my heart. 
\q1
\v 10 I have preached righteousness in the great congregation; lo! I will not refrain my lips; O Lord, you know my righteousness. 
\q1
\v 11 I have not hid your truth within my heart, and I have declared your salvation; I have not hid your mercy and your truth from the great congregation. 
\p
\q1
\v 12 But you, Lord, remove not your compassion far from me; your mercy and your truth have helped me continually. 
\q1
\v 13 For innumerable evils have encompassed me; my transgressions have taken hold of me, and I could not see; they are multiplied more than the hairs of my head; and my heart has failed me. 
\q1
\v 14 Be pleased, O Lord, to deliver me; O Lord, draw near to help me. 
\q1
\v 15 Let those that seek my soul, to destroy it, be ashamed and greatly agitated together; let those that wish me evil be turned backward and put to shame. 
\q1
\v 16 Let those that say to me, Aha, aha, quickly receive shame for their reward. 
\q1
\v 17 Let all those that seek you, O Lord, exult and rejoice in you; and let those who love your salvation say continually, The Lord be magnified. 
\q1
\v 18 But I am poor and needy; the Lord will take care of me; you are my helper, and my defender, O my God, don't delay. 
\c 40 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm of David. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 Blessed \add is the man\add* who thinks on the poor and needy: the Lord will deliver him in an evil day. 
\q1
\v 3 May the Lord preserve him and keep him alive, and bless him on the earth, and not deliver him into the hands of his enemy. 
\q1
\v 4 May the Lord help him upon the bed of his pain; you have made all his bed in his sickness. 
\p
\q1
\v 5 I said, O Lord, have mercy upon me; heal my soul; for I have sinned against you. 
\q1
\v 6 My enemies have spoken evil against me, \add saying\add*, When will he die, and his name perish? 
\q1
\v 7 If he came to see \add me\add*, his heart spoke vainly; he gathered wickedness to himself; he went out and spoke in like manner. 
\q1
\v 8 All my enemies whispered against me; against me they devised my hurt. 
\q1
\v 9 They denounced a wicked word against me, \add saying\add*, Now that he lies, will he not rise up again? 
\q1
\v 10 For even the man of my peace, in whom I trusted, \x + \xo 40:10 \xt John 13. 18.\x* who ate my bread, lifted up \add his\add* heel against me. 
\p
\q1
\v 11 But you, O Lord, have compassion upon me, and raise me up, and I will requite them. 
\q1
\v 12 By this I know that you have delighted in me, because my enemy will not rejoice over me. 
\q1
\v 13 But you did help me because of \add mine\add* innocence, and have established me before you forever. 
\q1
\v 14 Blessed \add be\add* the Lord God of Israel from everlasting, and to everlasting. So be it, so be it. 
\c 41 
\d
\v 1 For the end, \add a Psalm\add* for instruction, for the sons of Core. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 As the hart earnestly desires the fountains of water, so my soul earnestly longs for you, O God. 
\q1
\v 3 My soul has thirsted for the living God: when will I come and appear before God? 
\q1
\v 4 My tears have been bread to me day and night, while they daily said to me, Where is your God? 
\q1
\v 5 I remembered these things, and poured out my soul in me, for I will go to the place of your wondrous tabernacle, \add even\add* to the house of God, with a voice of exultation and thanksgiving and of the sound of those who keep festival.\f + \fr 41:5 \ft See \fqa Appendix.\f* 
\p
\q1
\v 6 Why are you very sad, O my soul? And why do you trouble me? Hope in God; for I will give thanks to him; \add he is\add* the salvation of my face. 
\p
\q1
\v 7 O my God, my soul has been troubled within me: therefore will I remember you from the land of Jordan, and of the Ermonites, from the little hill. 
\q1
\v 8 Deep calls to deep at the voice of your cataracts: all your billows and your waves have gone over me. 
\q1
\v 9 By day the Lord will command his mercy, and \f + \fr 41:9 \fqa Heb. \ft and \fqa Alex. \ft his song shall be, etc.\f*manifest \add it\add* by night: with me \add is\add* prayer to the God of my life. 
\q1
\v 10 I will say to God, You are my helper; why have you forgotten me? Why do I go sad of face, while the enemy oppresses \add me\add*? 
\q1
\v 11 While my bones were breaking, those who afflicted me reproached me; while they said to me daily, Where is your God? 
\p
\q1
\v 12 Why are you very sad, O my soul? And why do you trouble me? Hope in God; for I will give thanks to him; \add he is\add* the health of my face, and my God. 
\c 42 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm of David. 
\p Judge me, O God, and plead my cause, against an ungodly nation: deliver me from the unjust and crafty man. 
\q1
\v 2 For you, O God, are my strength: why have you cast me off? And why do I go sad of face, while the enemy oppresses \add me\add*? 
\q1
\v 3 Send forth your light and your truth: they have led me, and brought me to your holy mountain, and to your tents. 
\q1
\v 4 I will go in to the altar of God, to God who gladdens my youth: I will give thanks to you on the harp, O God, my God. 
\p
\q1
\v 5 Why are you very sad, O my soul? And why do you trouble me? Hope in God; for I will give thanks to him, \add who is\add* the health of my face, \add and\add* my God. 
\c 43 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm for \f + \fr 43:1 \fqa Gr. \ft understanding.\f*instruction, for the sons of Core. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 O God, we have heard with our ears, our fathers have told us, the work which you wroughtest in their days, in the days of old. 
\q1
\v 3 Your hand completely destroyed the nations, and you did plant them: you did afflict the nations, and cast them out. 
\q1
\v 4 For they inherited not the land by their \add own\add* sword, and their \add own\add* arm did not deliver them; but your right hand, and your arm, and the light of your face, because you were well pleased in them. 
\p
\q1
\v 5 You are indeed my King and my God, who commandest deliverances for Jacob. 
\q1
\v 6 In you will we push down our enemies, and in your name will we bring to nought those who rise up against us. 
\q1
\v 7 For I will not trust in my bow, and my sword will not save me. 
\q1
\v 8 For you have saved us from those who afflicted us, and have put to shame those who hated us. 
\q1
\v 9 In God \f + \fr 43:9 \fqa Gr. \ft will be praised etc. See \xt Ps. 106.\f*will we make our boast all the day, and to your name will we give thanks forever. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 10 But now you have cast off, and put us to shame; and you will not go forth with our hosts. 
\q1
\v 11 You have turned us back before our enemies; and those who hated us spoiled for themselves. 
\q1
\v 12 You made us as sheep for food; and you scatteredst us among the nations. 
\q1
\v 13 You have sold your people without price, and there was no profit by their exchange. 
\q1
\v 14 You have made us a reproach to our neighbours, a scorn and derision to those who are all around us. 
\q1
\v 15 You have made us a proverb among the nations, a shaking of the head among the nations. 
\q1
\v 16 All the day my shame is before me, and the confusion of my face has covered me, 
\q1
\v 17 because of the voice of the slanderer and reviler; because of the enemy and avenger. 
\p
\q1
\v 18 All these things have come upon us: but we have not forgotten you, neither have we dealt unrighteously in your covenant. 
\q1
\v 19 Our heart has not gone back; but you have turned aside our paths from your way. 
\q1
\v 20 For you have laid us low in a place of affliction, and the shadow of death has covered us. 
\q1
\v 21 If we have forgotten the name of our God, and if we have spread out our hands to a foreign god; will not God search these things out? 
\q1
\v 22 for he knows the secrets of the heart. 
\q1
\v 23 \x + \xo 43:23 \xt Rom. 8. 36.\x* For, for your sake we are killed all the day long; we are counted as sheep for slaughter. 
\p
\q1
\v 24 Awake, why sleep you, O Lord? Arise, and do not cast \add us\add* off forever. 
\q1
\v 25 Why turnest you your face away, \add and\add* forgettest our poverty and our affliction? 
\q1
\v 26 For our soul has been brought down to the dust; our belly has cleaved to the earth. 
\q1
\v 27 Arise, O Lord, help us, and redeem us for your name's sake. 
\c 44 
\d
\v 1 For the end, for \f + \fr 44:1 \ft See also \xt Ps. 68; 79, \ft titles; \fqa q. d. \ft repeated, see \fqa Hebrew.\f*alternate \add strains\add* by the sons of Core; for instruction, a Song concerning the beloved. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 My heart \f + \fr 44:2 \fqa Lit. \ft eructavit.\f*has uttered a good matter: I declare my works to the king: my tongue is the pen of a quick writer. 
\q1
\v 3 You are more beautiful than the sons of men: grace has been shed forth on your lips: therefore God has blessed you forever. 
\p
\q1
\v 4 Gird your sword upon your thigh, O Mighty One, in your comeliness, and in your beauty; 
\q1
\v 5 and bend \add your bow\add*, and prosper, and reign, because of truth and meekness and righteousness; and your right hand will guide you wonderfully. 
\q1
\v 6 Your weapons are sharpened, Mighty One, (the nations will fall under you) \add they are\add* in the heart of the king's enemies. 
\p
\q1
\v 7 \x + \xo 44:7 \xt Heb. 1. 8-10.\x* Your throne, O God, is forever and ever: the sceptre of your kingdom is a sceptre of righteousness. 
\q1
\v 8 You have loved righteousness, and hated wickedness: therefore God, your God, has anointed you with the oil of gladness beyond your fellows. 
\p
\q1
\v 9 Myrrh, and stacte, and cassia \add are exhaled\add* from your garments, \add and\add* out of the ivory palaces, 
\q1
\v 10 with which kings' daughters have gladdened you for your honour: the queen stood by on your right hand, clothed in vesture worked with gold, \add and\add* arrayed in divers colours. 
\q1
\v 11 Hear, O daughter, and see, and incline your ear; forget also your people, and your father's house. 
\q1
\v 12 Because the king has desired your beauty; for he is your Lord. 
\q1
\v 13 The daughter of Tyre will adore him with gifts; the rich of the people of the land will supplicate your \f + \fr 44:13 \fqa Gr. \ft face.\f*favour. 
\p
\q1
\v 14 All her glory \add is that\add* of the daughter of the king \f + \fr 44:14 \fqa Alex. \ft ἔσωθεν, within, so \fqa Heb.\f*of Esebon, robed \add as she is\add* in golden fringed garments, 
\q1
\v 15 in embroidered \add clothing\add*: virgins will be brought to the king after her: her fellows will be brought to you. 
\q1
\v 16 They will be brought with gladness and exultation: they will be led into the king's temple. 
\q1
\v 17 Instead of your fathers children are born to you: you will make them princes over all the earth. 
\q1
\v 18 They will make mention of your name from generation to generation: therefore will the nations give thanks to you \f + \fr 44:18 \fqa Gr. \ft to the age of the age.\f*forever, even forever and ever. 
\c 45 
\d
\v 1 For the end, for the sons of Core; a Psalm concerning secret things. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 God is our refuge and strength, a help in the afflictions that have come heavily upon us. 
\q1
\v 3 Therefore will we not fear when the earth is troubled, and the mountains are removed into the depths of the seas. 
\q1
\v 4 Their waters have roared and been troubled, the mountains have been troubled by his might. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 5 The flowings of the river gladden the city of God: the Most High has sanctified his tabernacle. 
\q1
\v 6 God is among her; she will not be moved: God will help her \f + \fr 45:6 \fqa Alex. \ft and \fqa Heb. \ft before, \fqa or, \ft toward the morning.\f*with his face. 
\q1
\v 7 The nations were troubled, the kingdoms tottered: he uttered his voice, the earth shook. 
\q1
\v 8 The Lord of hosts is with us; the God of Jacob is our helper. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 9 Come, and behold the works of the Lord, what wonders he has achieved on the earth. 
\q1
\v 10 Putting an end to wars as for the ends of the earth; he will crush the bow, and break in pieces the weapon, and burn the bucklers with fire. 
\q1
\v 11 Be still, and know that I am God: I will be exalted among the nations, I will be exalted in the earth. 
\q1
\v 12 The Lord of hosts is with us; the God of Jacob is our helper. 
\c 46 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm for the sons of Core. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 Clap your hands, all you nations; shout to God with a voice of exultation. 
\q1
\v 3 For the Lord most high is terrible; \add he is\add* a great king over all the earth. 
\q1
\v 4 He has subdued the peoples under us, and the nations under our feet. 
\q1
\v 5 He has chosen out his inheritance for us, the beauty of Jacob which he loved. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 6 God is gone up with a shout, the Lord with a sound of a trumpet. 
\q1
\v 7 Sing praises to our God, sing praises: sing praises to our King, sing praises. 
\q1
\v 8 For God is king of all the earth: sing praises with understanding. 
\q1
\v 9 God reigns over the nations: God sits upon the throne of his holiness. 
\q1
\v 10 The rulers of the people are assembled with the God of Abraham: for God's mighty ones of the earth have been greatly exalted. 
\c 47 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm of \f + \fr 47:1 \ft A song.\f*praise for the sons of Core on the second \add day\add* of the week. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 Great is the Lord, and greatly to be praised in the city of our God, in his holy mountain. 
\q1
\v 3 The city of the great King is well planted \add on\add* the mountains of Zion, with the joy of the whole earth, \add on\add* the sides of the north. 
\q1
\v 4 God is known in her palaces, when he undertakes to help her. 
\p
\q1
\v 5 For, behold, the kings of the earth were assembled, they came together. 
\q1
\v 6 They saw, and so they wondered: they were troubled, they were moved. 
\q1
\v 7 Trembling took hold on them: there were the pangs as of a woman in labor. 
\q1
\v 8 You will break the ships of Tharsis with a vehement wind. 
\q1
\v 9 As we have heard, so have we also seen, in the city of the Lord of hosts, in the city of our God: God has founded it forever. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 10 We have thought of your mercy, O God, among your people. 
\q1
\v 11 According to your name, O God, so is also your praise to the ends of the earth: your right hand is full of righteousness. 
\q1
\v 12 Let mount Zion rejoice, let the daughters of Judæa exult, because of your judgments, O Lord. 
\p
\q1
\v 13 Go all around Zion, and encompass her: tell you her towers. 
\q1
\v 14 Mark you well her strength, and observe her palaces; that you may tell the next generation. 
\q1
\v 15 For this is our God forever and ever: he will be our guide for evermore. 
\c 48 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm for the sons of Core. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 Hear these words, all you nations, listen, all you who dwell upon the earth: 
\q1
\v 3 both the \f + \fr 48:3 \fqa Gr. \ft earth-born.\f*sons of mean men, and sons of \add great\add* men; the rich and poor \add man\add* together. 
\q1
\v 4 My mouth will speak of wisdom; and the meditation of my heart will bring \add forth\add* understanding. 
\q1
\v 5 I will incline my ear to a parable: I will open my \f + \fr 48:5 \fqa Gr. \ft problem.\f*riddle on the harp. 
\p
\q1
\v 6 Wherefore \f + \fr 48:6 \fqa Gr. \ft shall.\f*should I fear in the evil day? The wickedness of my heel will compass me. 
\q1
\v 7 Those who trust in their strength, and boast themselves in the multitude of their wealth— 
\q1
\v 8 A brother does not redeem, will a man redeem? He will not give to God a ransom for himself, 
\q1
\v 9 or the price of the redemption of his soul, though he labour forever, 
\q1
\v 10 and live to the end, \add so\add* that he should not see corruption. 
\p
\q1
\v 11 When he will see wise men dying, the fool and the senseless one will perish together; and they will leave their wealth to strangers. 
\q1
\v 12 Their sepulchres are their houses forever, \add even\add* their tents to all generations: they have called their lands after their own names. 
\q1
\v 13 Man being in honour, understands not: he is compared to the senseless cattle, and is like to them. 
\q1
\v 14 This their way is an offence to them: yet afterwards men will commend their sayings. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 15 They have laid \add them\add* as sheep in Hades; death will feed on them; and the upright will have dominion over them in the morning, and their help will fail in Hades from their glory. 
\q1
\v 16 But God will deliver my soul from the power of Hades, when he will receive me. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 17 Don't be afraid when a man is enriched, and when the glory of his house is increased. 
\q1
\v 18 For he will take nothing when he dies; neither will his glory descend with him. 
\q1
\v 19 For his soul will be blessed in his life: he will give thanks to you when you do well to him. 
\q1
\v 20 \add Yet\add* he will go in \f + \fr 48:20 \fqa Gr. \ft as far as.\f*to the generation of his fathers; he will never see light. 
\q1
\v 21 Man that is in honour, understands not: he is compared to the senseless cattle, and is like them. 
\c 49 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm \f + \fr 49:1 \fqa Or, \ft of.\f*for Asaph. 
\p The God of gods, the Lord, has spoken, and called the earth from the rising of the sun to the going down \add of it\add*. 
\q1
\v 2 Out of Zion \add comes\add* the excellence of his beauty. 
\q1
\v 3 God, our God, will come manifestly, and will not keep silence: a fire will be kindled before him, and all around him there will be a very great tempest. 
\q1
\v 4 He will summon the heaven above, and the earth, that he may \x + \xo 49:4 \xt Heb. 10. 30.\x* judge his people. 
\q1
\v 5 Assemble you his saints to him, those that have engaged in a covenant with him upon sacrifices. 
\q1
\v 6 The heavens will declare his righteousness: for God is judge. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 7 Hear, my people, and I will speak to you, O Israel: and I will testify to you: I am God, your God. 
\q1
\v 8 I will not reprove you on account of your sacrifices; for your whole-burnt-offerings are before me continually. 
\q1
\v 9 I will take no bullocks out of your house, nor he-goats out of your flocks. 
\q1
\v 10 For all the wild beasts of the thicket are mine, the cattle on the mountains, and oxen. 
\q1
\v 11 I know all the birds of the sky; and the beauty of the field is mine. 
\q1
\v 12 If I should be hungry, I will not tell you: for the world is mine, and the fulness of it. 
\q1
\v 13 Will I eat the flesh of bulls, or drink the blood of goats? 
\q1
\v 14 Offer to God the sacrifice of praise; and pay your vows to the Most High. 
\q1
\v 15 Call upon me in the day of affliction; and I will deliver you, and you will glorify me. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 16 But to the sinner God has said, Why do you declare my ordinances, and take up my covenant in your mouth? 
\q1
\v 17 Because you have hated instruction, and have cast my words behind \add you\add*. 
\q1
\v 18 If you saw a thief, you \f + \fr 49:18 \ft See 1 Pe 4. 4.\f*rannest along with him, and have cast in your lot with adulterers. 
\q1
\v 19 Your mouth has multiplied wickedness, and your tongue has framed deceit.\f + \fr 49:19 \ft From these words in \fqa Alex. \ft to \xt Ps. 79. 11, \ft thirty psalms are wanting.\f* 
\q1
\v 20 You did sit and speak against your brother, and did scandalise your mother's son. 
\p
\q1
\v 21 These things you did, and I kept silence: you thoughtest wickedly that I should be like you; \add but\add* I will reprove you, and set \add your offences\add* before you. 
\q1
\v 22 Now consider these things, you who forget God, lest he tear \add you\add*, and there be no deliverer. 
\p
\q1
\v 23 The sacrifice of praise will glorify me: and \f + \fr 49:23 \fqa Gr. \ft there.\f*that is the way wherein I will show to him the salvation of God. 
\c 50 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm of David, 
\q1
\v 2 when Nathan the prophet came to him, when he had gone in to Beersheba. 
\p
\q1
\v 3 Have mercy upon me, O God, according to your great mercy; and according to the multitude of your compassions blot out my transgression. 
\q1
\v 4 Wash me thoroughly from my wickedness, and cleanse me from my sin. 
\p
\q1
\v 5 For I am conscious of my wickedness; and my sin is continually before me. 
\q1
\v 6 Against you only have I sinned, and done evil before you: that you might be justified in your sayings, and might overcome when you are judged. 
\q1
\v 7 For, behold, I was conceived in iniquities, and in sins did my mother conceive me. 
\p
\q1
\v 8 For, behold, you love truth: you have manifested to me the secret and hidden things of your wisdom. 
\q1
\v 9 You will sprinkle me with hyssop, and I will be purified: you will wash me, and I will be made whiter than snow. 
\q1
\v 10 You will cause me to hear gladness and joy: the afflicted bones will rejoice. 
\q1
\v 11 Turn away your face from my sins, and blot out all my iniquities. 
\q1
\v 12 Create in me a clean heart, O God; and renew a right spirit in my inward parts. 
\q1
\v 13 Didn't cast me away from your presence; and remove not your Holy Spirit from me. 
\q1
\v 14 Restore to me the joy of your salvation: establish me with your \f + \fr 50:14 \fqa Gr. \ft governing.\f*directing Spirit. 
\p
\q1
\v 15 \add Then\add* will I teach transgressors your ways; and ungodly men will turn to you. 
\q1
\v 16 Deliver me from blood-guiltiness, O God, the God of my salvation: \add and\add* my tongue will joyfully declare your righteousness. 
\q1
\v 17 O Lord, you will open my lips; and my mouth will declare your praise. 
\q1
\v 18 For if you desiredst sacrifice, I would have given \add it\add*: you will not take pleasure in whole-burnt-offerings. 
\q1
\v 19 Sacrifice to God is a broken spirit: a broken and humbled heart God will not despise. 
\p
\q1
\v 20 Do good, O Lord, to Zion in your good pleasure; and let the walls of Jerusalem be built. 
\q1
\v 21 Then will you be pleased with a sacrifice of righteousness, \f + \fr 50:21 \ft Properly, a heave or wave-offfering.\f*offering, and whole-burnt-sacrifices: then will they offer calves upon your altar. 
\c 51 
\d
\v 1 For the end, \add a Psalm\add* of \f + \fr 51:1 \fqa Gr. \ft governing.\f*instruction by David, 
\q1
\v 2 when Doec the Idumean came and told Saul, and said to him, David is gone to the house of Abimelech. 
\p
\q1
\v 3 Why do you, O mighty man, boast of wickedness in \add your\add* mischief? All the day 
\q1
\v 4 your tongue has devised unrighteousness; like a sharpened razor you have worked deceit. 
\q1
\v 5 You have loved wickedness more than goodness; unrighteousness better than to speak righteousness. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 6 You have loved all words of destruction, \add and\add* a deceitful tongue. 
\p
\q1
\v 7 Therefore may God destroy you forever, may he pluck you up and completely remove you from \add your\add* dwelling, and your root from the land of the living. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 8 The righteous will see, and fear, and will laugh at him, and say, 
\q1
\v 9 Behold the man who made not God his help; but trusted in the abundance of his wealth, and strengthened himself in his vanity. 
\p
\q1
\v 10 But I am as a fruitful olive in the house of God: I have trusted in the mercy of God forever, even for evermore. 
\q1
\v 11 I will give thanks to you forever, for you have done \add it\add*: and I will wait on your name; for \add it is\add* good before your saints. 
\c 52 
\d
\v 1 For the end, \add a Psalm\add* of David upon Maeleth, of instruction. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 The fool has said in his heart, There is no God. They have corrupted \add themselves\add*, and become abominable in iniquities: there is no one that does good. 
\q1
\v 3 God looked down from heaven upon the sons of men, to see if there were any that understood, or sought after God. 
\q1
\v 4 \x + \xo 52:4 \xt Rom. 3. 10-12.\x* They have all gone out of the way, they are together become unprofitable; there is no one that does good, there isn't even one. 
\p
\q1
\v 5 Will none of the workers of wickedness know, who devour my people as they would eat bread? They have not called upon God. There were they greatly afraid, where there was no fear: 
\q1
\v 6 for God has scattered the bones of the men-pleasers; they were ashamed, for God despised them. 
\q1
\v 7 Who will bring the salvation of Israel out of Zion? When the Lord turns the captivity of his people, Jacob will exult, and Israel will be glad. 
\c 53 
\d
\v 1 For the end, among the Hymns of instruction by David, 
\q1
\v 2 when the Ziphites came and said to Saul, Lo, isn't David hid with us? 
\p
\q1
\v 3 Save me, O God, by your name, and judge me by your might. 
\q1
\v 4 O God, hear my prayer; listen to the words of my mouth. 
\q1
\v 5 For strangers have risen up against me, and mighty men have sought my life: they have not set God before them. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 6 For lo! God assists me; and the Lord is the helper of my soul. 
\q1
\v 7 He will return evil to my enemies; completely destroy them in your truth. 
\q1
\v 8 I will willingly sacrifice to you: I will give thanks to your name, O Lord; for \add it is\add* good. 
\q1
\v 9 For you have delivered me out of all affliction, and my eye has seen \add my desire\add* upon my enemies. 
\c 54 
\d
\v 1 For the end, among Hymns of instruction by David. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 Listen, O God, to my prayer; and disregard not my supplication. 
\q1
\v 3 Pay attention to me, and listen to me: I was grieved in my meditation, and troubled; 
\q1
\v 4 because of the voice of the enemy, and because of the oppression of the sinner: for they brought wickedness against me, and were wrathfully angry with me. 
\p
\q1
\v 5 My heart was troubled within me; and the fear of death fell upon me. 
\q1
\v 6 Fear and trembling came upon me, and darkness covered me. 
\q1
\v 7 I said, O that I had wings as \add those\add* of a dove! Then would I flee away, and be at rest. 
\q1
\v 8 Lo! I have fled afar off, and lodged in the wilderness. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 9 I waited for him that should deliver me from distress of spirit and tempest. 
\p
\q1
\v 10 Destroy, O Lord, and divide their tongues: for I have seen wickedness and gainsaying in the city. 
\q1
\v 11 Day and night \f + \fr 54:11 \fqa Or, \ft it, \fqa sc. \ft iniquity.\f*he will go all around it upon its walls: wickedness and sorrow and unrighteousness \add are\add* among it; 
\q1
\v 12 and usury and craft have not failed from its streets. 
\p
\q1
\v 13 For if an enemy had reproached me, I would have endured it; and if one who hated \add me\add* had spoken vauntingly against me, I would have hid myself from him. 
\q1
\v 14 But you, O man likeminded, my guide, and my acquaintance, 
\q1
\v 15 who in companionship with me sweetened \add our\add* food: we walked in the house of God in concord. 
\q1
\v 16 Let death come upon them, and let them go down alive into Hades, for wickedness is in their dwellings, among them. 
\p
\q1
\v 17 I cried to God, and the Lord listened to me. 
\q1
\v 18 Evening, and morning, and at noon I will declare and make known \add my wants\add*: and he will hear my voice. 
\q1
\v 19 He will deliver my soul in peace from those who draw near to me: for they were with me in many \add cases\add*. 
\q1
\v 20 God will hear, and bring them low, \add even\add* he who has existed from eternity. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p \f + \fr 54:20 \fqa Or, \ft they have nothing to give in exchange, \fqa q. d. \ft to redeem their souls. Compare \xt Ps. 48. 7,8; Mark 8. 37.\f*For they suffer no reverse, and \add therefore\add* they have not feared God. 
\q1
\v 21 He has reached forth his hand for retribution; they have profaned his covenant. 
\q1
\v 22 They were scattered at the anger of his face, and his heart drew near \f + \fr 54:22 \ft Compare \fqa Heb. \ft and \fqa A. V.\f*them. His words were smoother than oil, yet are they darts. 
\p
\q1
\v 23 \x + \xo 54:23 \xt 1 Pet. 5. 7.\x* Cast your care upon the Lord, and he will \f + \fr 54:23 \fqa Or, \ft nourish.\f*sustain you; he will never suffer the righteous to be moved. 
\q1
\v 24 But you, O God, will bring them down to the pit of destruction; bloody and crafty men will not live out half their days; but I will hope in you, O Lord. 
\c 55 
\d
\v 1 For the end, concerning the people that were removed from the \f + \fr 55:1 \fqa Or, \ft holy things.\f*sanctuary, by David for a memorial, when the Philistines caught him in Geth. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 Have mercy upon me, O God; for man has trodden me down; all the day long he warring has afflicted me. 
\q1
\v 3 My enemies have trodden me down all the day from the dawning of the day; for there are many warring against me. 
\p
\q1
\v 4 They will be afraid, but I will trust in you. 
\q1
\v 5 In God I will praise my words; all the day have I hoped in God; I will not fear what flesh will do to me. 
\p
\q1
\v 6 All the day long they have abominated my words; all their devices \add are\add* against me for evil. 
\q1
\v 7 They will dwell near and hide \add themselves\add*; they will watch my steps, accordingly as I have waited patiently in my soul. 
\q1
\v 8 You will on no account save them; you will bring down the people in wrath. 
\q1
\v 9 O God, I have declared my life to you; you have set my tears before you, even according to your promise. 
\p
\q1
\v 10 My enemies will be turned back, in the day wherein I will call upon you; behold, I know that you are my God. 
\q1
\v 11 In God will I praise \add his\add* word; in the Lord will I praise \add his\add* saying. 
\q1
\v 12 I have hoped in God; I will not be afraid of what man will do to me. 
\q1
\v 13 The vows of your praise, O God, which I will pay, are upon me. 
\q1
\v 14 For you have delivered my soul from death, and my feet from sliding, that I should be well-pleasing before God in the land of the living. 
\c 56 
\d
\v 1 For the end. Don't destroy: by David, for a memorial, when he fled from the presence of Saul to the cave. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 Have mercy, upon me, O God, have mercy upon me: for my soul has trusted in you: and in the shadow of your wings will I hope, until the wickedness have passed away. 
\q1
\v 3 I will cry to God most high; the God who has benefited me. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 4 He sent from heaven and saved me; he gave to reproach those who trampled on me: God has sent his mercy and his truth; 
\q1
\v 5 and he has delivered my soul from the midst of \add lions'\add* whelps: I lay down to sleep, \add though\add* troubled. \add As for\add* the sons of men, their teeth are arms and \add missile\add* weapons, and their tongue a sharp sword. 
\p
\q1
\v 6 Be exalted, O God, above the heavens; and your glory above all the earth. 
\q1
\v 7 They have prepared snares for my feet, and have bowed down my soul: they have dug a pit before my face, and fallen into it \add themselves\add*. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 8 My heart, O God, \add is\add* ready, my heart \add is\add* ready: I will sing, yes will sing psalms. 
\q1
\v 9 Awake, my glory; awake, psaltery and harp: I will awake early. 
\q1
\v 10 O Lord, I will give thanks to you among the nations: I will sing to you among the nations. 
\q1
\v 11 For your mercy has been magnified even to the heavens, and your truth to the clouds. 
\q1
\v 12 Be exalted, O God, above the heavens; and your glory above all the earth. 
\c 57 
\d
\v 1 For the end. Don't destroy: by David, for a memorial. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 If you do indeed speak righteousness, \add then\add* do you judge rightly, you sons of men. 
\q1
\v 3 For you work iniquities in \add your\add* hearts in the earth: your hands plot unrighteousness. 
\q1
\v 4 Sinners have gone astray from the womb: they go astray from the belly: they speak lies. 
\q1
\v 5 Their venom is like \add that\add* of a snake; as \add that\add* of a deaf asp, and that stops her ears; 
\q1
\v 6 which will not hear the voice of charmers, nor \add heed\add* the \f + \fr 57:6 \fqa Gr. \ft poison.\f*charm prepared skilfully by the wise. 
\p
\q1
\v 7 God has crushed their teeth in their mouth: God has broken the cheek-teeth of the lions. 
\q1
\v 8 They will completely pass away like water running through: he will bend his bow till they will fail. 
\q1
\v 9 They will be destroyed as melted wax: the fire has fallen and they have not seen the sun. 
\q1
\v 10 Before your thorns feel the white thorn, he will swallow you up as living, as in his wrath. 
\p
\q1
\v 11 The righteous will rejoice when he sees the vengeance of the ungodly: he will wash his hands in the blood of the sinner. 
\q1
\v 12 A man will say, Truly then there is \f + \fr 57:12 \fqa Gr. \ft fruit.\f*a reward for the righteous: truly there is a God who judges them in the earth. 
\c 58 
\d
\v 1 For the end. Don't destroy: by David for a memorial, when Saul sent, and watched his house to kill him. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 Deliver me from my enemies, O God; and ransom me from those that rise up against me. 
\q1
\v 3 Deliver me from the workers of wickedness, and save me from bloody men. 
\p
\q1
\v 4 For, behold, they have hunted after my soul; violent men have set upon me: neither \add is it\add* my wickedness, nor my sin, O Lord. 
\q1
\v 5 Without wickedness I ran and directed \add my course aright\add*: awake to help me, and behold. 
\q1
\v 6 You, Lord God of hosts, the God of Israel, draw near to visit all the nations; pity not any that work wickedness. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 7 They will return at evening, and hunger like a dog, and go all around the city. 
\p
\q1
\v 8 Behold, they will utter a voice with their mouth, and a sword is in their lips; for who, \add say they\add*, has heard? 
\q1
\v 9 But you, Lord, will laugh them to scorn; you will completely despise all the nations. 
\q1
\v 10 I will keep my strength, \add looking\add* to you; for you, O God, are my helper. 
\q1
\v 11 \add As for\add* my God, his mercy will go before me: my God will show me \add vengeance\add* on my enemies. 
\p
\q1
\v 12 Kill them not, lest they forget your \f + \fr 58:12 \ft some read λαοῦ 'people'.\f*law; scatter them by your power; and bring them down, O Lord, my defender. 
\q1
\v 13 \add For\add* the sin of their mouth, \add and\add* the word of their lips, let them be even taken in their pride. 
\q1
\v 14 For \add their\add* cursing and falsehood will utter destruction be denounced: \add they will fall\add* by the wrath of utter destruction, and will not be; so will they know that the God of Jacob is Lord of the ends of the earth. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 15 They will return at evening, and be hungry as a dog, and go all around the city. 
\q1
\v 16 They will be scattered here and there for food; and if they don't be satisfied, they will even murmur. 
\p
\q1
\v 17 But I will sing to your strength, and in the morning will I exult \add in\add* your mercy; for you have been my supporter, and my refuge in the day of my affliction. 
\q1
\v 18 \add You are\add* my helper; to you, my God, will I sing; you are my supporter, O my God, \add and\add* my mercy. 
\c 59 
\d
\v 1 For the end, for those who will yet be changed; for an inscription by David for instruction, 
\q1
\v 2 when he \add had\add* burned Mesopotamia of Syria, and Syria Sobal, and Joab \add had\add* returned and struck \add in\add* the valley of salt twelve thousand. 
\p
\q1
\v 3 O God, you have rejected and destroyed us; you have been angry, yet have pitied us. 
\q1
\v 4 You have shaken the earth, and troubled it; heal its breaches, for it has been shaken. 
\q1
\v 5 You have shown your people hard things: you have made us drink the wine of astonishment. 
\q1
\v 6 You have given a token to those who fear you, that they might flee from the bow. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 7 That your beloved ones may be delivered; save with your right hand, and hear me. 
\p
\q1
\v 8 God has spoken in his holiness; I will rejoice, and divide Sicima, and measure out the valley of tents. 
\q1
\v 9 Gilead is mine, and Manasse is mine; and Ephraim is the \f + \fr 59:9 \fqa Or, \ft strengthening.\f*strength of my head; 
\q1
\v 10 Judah is my king; Moab is the caldron of my hope; over Idumea will I stretch out my shoe; the Philistines have been subjected to me. 
\p
\q1
\v 11 Who will lead me into the fortified city? Who will guide me as far as Idumea? 
\q1
\v 12 Will not you, O God, who have cast us off? And will not you, O God, go forth with our forces? 
\q1
\v 13 Give us help from trouble: for vain is the deliverance of man. 
\p
\q1
\v 14 In God will we \f + \fr 59:14 \fqa Gr. \ft work power.\f*do valiantly; and he will bring to nought those who harass us. 
\c 60 
\d
\v 1 For the end, among the Hymns of David. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 O God, listen to my petition; pay attention to my prayer. 
\q1
\v 3 From the ends of the earth have I cried to you, when my heart was in trouble: you liftedst me up on a rock, you did guide me: 
\q1
\v 4 because you were my hope, a tower of strength from the face of the enemy. 
\q1
\v 5 I will dwell in your tabernacle forever; I will shelter myself under the shadow of your wings. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 6 For you, O God, have heard my prayers; you have given an inheritance to those who fear your name. 
\q1
\v 7 You will add days to the days of the king; \add you will lengthen\add* his years to all generations. 
\q1
\v 8 He will endure forever before God: which of them will seek out his mercy and truth? 
\q1
\v 9 So will I sing to your name forever and ever, that I may daily perform my vows. 
\c 61 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm of David for Idithun. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 Will not my soul be subjected to God? For of him is my salvation. 
\q1
\v 3 For he is my God and my Saviour; my helper, I will not be moved \f + \fr 61:3 \fqa Or, \ft any more.\f*very much. 
\q1
\v 4 How long will you assault a man? You are all slaughtering as with a bowed wall and a broken hedge. 
\q1
\v 5 They only took counsel to despise my honour: I ran in thirst: with their mouth they blessed, but with their heart they cursed. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 6 Nevertheless do you, my soul, be subjected to God; for of him \add is\add* my patient hope. 
\q1
\v 7 For he \add is\add* my God and my Saviour; my helper, I will not be moved. 
\q1
\v 8 \f + \fr 61:8 \fqa Gr. \ft on.\f*In God \add is\add* my salvation and my glory: \add he is\add* the God of my help, and my hope is in God. 
\q1
\v 9 Hope in him, all you congregation of the people; pour out your hearts before him, for God is our helper. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 10 But the sons of men are vain; the sons of men are false, so as to be deceitful in the balances; they are \f + \fr 61:10 \fqa Gr. \ft altogether.\f*all alike \add formed\add* out of vanity. 
\q1
\v 11 Don't trust in unrighteousness, and lust not after robberies: if wealth should flow in, set not your heart upon it. 
\q1
\v 12 God has spoken once, \add and\add* I have heard these two things, that power is of God; 
\q1
\v 13 and mercy is yours, O Lord; for you will recompense every one according to his works. 
\c 62 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm of David, when he was in the wilderness of Idumea. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 O God, my God, I cry to you early; my soul has thirsted for you: how often has my flesh \add longed\add* after you, in a barren and trackless and dry land! 
\q1
\v 3 Thus have I appeared before you in the sanctuary, that I might see your power and your glory. 
\q1
\v 4 For your mercy is better than \f + \fr 62:4 \fqa Gr. \ft lives.\f*life: my lips will praise you. 
\q1
\v 5 Thus will I bless you during my life: I will lift up my hands in your name. 
\q1
\v 6 Let my soul be filled as with marrow and fatness; and \add my\add* joyful lips will praise your name. 
\p
\q1
\v 7 \f + \fr 62:7 \fqa Gr. \ft if. See \xt Acts 26. 23.\f*Although I have remembered you on my bed: in the early seasons I have meditated on you. 
\q1
\v 8 For you have been my helper, and in the shelter of your wings will I rejoice. 
\q1
\v 9 My soul has \f + \fr 62:9 \fqa Gr. \ft been glued.\f*kept very close behind you: your right hand has upheld me. 
\q1
\v 10 But they vainly sought after my soul; they will go into the lowest parts of the earth. 
\q1
\v 11 They will be delivered up to the power of the sword; they will be portions for foxes. 
\q1
\v 12 But the king will rejoice in God; every one that swears by him will be praised; for the mouth of those who speak unjust things has been stopped. 
\c 63 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm of David. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 Hear my prayer, O God, when I make my petition to you; deliver my soul from fear of the enemy. 
\q1
\v 3 You have sheltered me from the conspiracy of those who do wickedly; from the multitude of those who work wickedness; 
\q1
\v 4 who have sharpened their tongues as a sword; they have bent their bow maliciously; 
\q1
\v 5 to shoot in secret at the blameless; they will shoot him suddenly, and will not fear. 
\q1
\v 6 They have set up for themselves an evil matter, they have given counsel to hide snares; they have said, Who will see them? 
\q1
\v 7 They have searched out wickedness; they have wearied themselves with searching diligently, a man will approach and the heart is deep, 
\q1
\v 8 and God will be exalted, their wounds were \add caused by\add* the weapon of the foolish children, 
\q1
\v 9 and their tongues have set him at nought, all that saw them were troubled; 
\q1
\v 10 and every man was alarmed, and they related the works of God, and understood his deeds. 
\q1
\v 11 The righteous will rejoice in the Lord, and hope on him, and all the upright in heart will be praised. 
\c 64 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm \add and\add* Song of David. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 Praise becomes you, O God, in Zion; and to you will the vow be performed. 
\q1
\v 3 Hear my prayer; to you all flesh will come. 
\q1
\v 4 The words of transgressors have overpowered us; but do you pardon our sins. 
\q1
\v 5 Blessed \add is he\add* whom you have chosen and adopted; he will dwell in your courts; we will be filled with the good things of your house; your temple is holy. 
\q1
\v 6 \add You are\add* wonderful in righteousness. Listen to us, O God our Saviour; the hope of all the ends of the earth, and of them \add that are\add* on the sea afar off: 
\q1
\v 7 who do \f + \fr 64:7 \fqa Gr. \ft prepare.\f*establish the mountains in your strength, being girded about with power; 
\q1
\v 8 who troublest the depth of the sea, the sounds of its waves. 
\q1
\v 9 The nations will be troubled, and those who inhabit the ends \add of the earth\add* will be afraid of your signs; you will cause the outgoings of morning and evening to rejoice. 
\p
\q1
\v 10 You have visited the earth, and saturated it; you have abundantly enriched it. The river of God is filled with water; you have prepared their food, for thus is the preparation \add of it\add*. 
\q1
\v 11 Saturate her furrows, multiply her fruits; \add the crop\add* springing up will rejoice in its drops. 
\q1
\v 12 You will bless the crown of the year \add because\add* of your goodness; and your plains will be filled with fatness. 
\q1
\v 13 The mountains of the wilderness will be enriched; and the hills will gird themselves with joy. 
\q1
\v 14 The rams of the flock are clothed \add with wool\add*, and the valleys will abound in grain; they will cry aloud, yes they will sing hymns. 
\c 65 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Song of a Psalm of resurrection. 
\p Shout to God, all the earth. 
\q1
\v 2 O sing praises to his name; give glory to his praise. 
\q1
\v 3 Say to God, How awful are your works! Through the greatness of your power your enemies will lie to you. 
\q1
\v 4 Let all the earth worship you, and sing to you; let them sing to your name. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 5 Come and behold the works of God; \add he is\add* terrible in \add his\add* counsels beyond the children of men. 
\q1
\v 6 Who turns the sea into dry land; they will go through the river on foot; there will we rejoice in him, 
\q1
\v 7 who by his power \f + \fr 65:7 \fqa Or, \ft has dominion for ever.\f*is Lord over the age, his eyes look upon the nations; don't let those who provoke \add him\add* be exalted in themselves. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 8 Bless our God, you nations, and make the voice of his praise to be heard; 
\q1
\v 9 who quickens my soul in life, and does not suffer my feet to be moved. 
\q1
\v 10 For you, O God, have proved us; you have tried us with fire as silver is tried. 
\q1
\v 11 You brought us into the snare; you laidest afflictions on our back. 
\q1
\v 12 You did mount men upon our heads; we went through fire and water; but you brought us out into \add a place of\add* refreshment. 
\p
\q1
\v 13 I will go into your house with whole-burnt-offerings; I will pay you my vows, 
\q1
\v 14 which my lips framed, and my mouth uttered in my affliction. 
\q1
\v 15 I will offer to you whole-burnt-sacrifices full of marrow, with incense and rams; I will sacrifice to you oxen with goats. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 16 Come, hear, and I will tell, all you who fear God, how great things he has done for my soul. 
\q1
\v 17 I cried to him with my mouth, and exalted him with my tongue. 
\q1
\v 18 If I have regarded wickedness in my heart, don't let the Lord listen \add to me\add*. 
\q1
\v 19 Therefore God has listened to me; he has attended to the voice of my prayer. 
\q1
\v 20 Blessed be God, who has not turned away my prayer, nor his mercy from me. 
\c 66 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm of David among the Hymns. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 God be merciful to us, and bless us; \add and\add* cause his face to shine upon us. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 3 That \add men\add* may know your way on the earth, your salvation among all nations. 
\q1
\v 4 Let the nations, O God, give thanks to you; let all the nations give thanks to you. 
\q1
\v 5 Let the nations rejoice and exult, for you will judge the peoples in equity, and will guide the nations on the earth. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 6 Let the peoples, O God, give thanks to you; let all the peoples give thanks to you. 
\q1
\v 7 The earth has yielded her fruit; let God, our God, bless us. 
\q1
\v 8 Let God bless us; and let all the ends of the earth fear him. 
\c 67 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm of a Song by David. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 Let God arise, and let his enemies be scattered; and let those who hate him flee from before him. 
\q1
\v 3 As smoke vanishes, let them vanish: as wax melts before the fire, so let the sinners perish from before God. 
\q1
\v 4 But let the righteous rejoice; let them exult before God: let them be delighted with joy. 
\p
\q1
\v 5 Sing to God, sing praises to his name: make a way for him that rides upon the west (the Lord is his name) and exult before him. They will be troubled before the face of him, 
\q1
\v 6 \add who is\add* the father of the orphans, and judge of the widows: \add such is\add* God in his holy place. 
\q1
\v 7 God settles the solitary in a house; leading forth prisoners mightily, also those who act provokingly, \add even\add* those who dwell in tombs. 
\p
\q1
\v 8 O God, when you went forth before your people, when you went through the wilderness; Pause: 
\q1
\v 9 the earth quaked, yes, the heavens dropped \add water\add* at the presence of the God of Sina, at the presence of the God of Israel. 
\q1
\v 10 O God, you will grant to your inheritance a gracious rain; for it was weary, but you did refresh it. 
\p
\q1
\v 11 Your \f + \fr 67:11 \ft See the \fqa Hebrew.\f*creatures dwell in it: you have in your goodness prepared for the poor. 
\q1
\v 12 The Lord God will give a word to those who preach \add it\add* in a great company. 
\q1
\v 13 The king of the forces of the beloved, of the beloved, \add will\add* even \add grant them\add* for the beauty of the house to divide the spoils. 
\q1
\v 14 Even if you should lie among the lots, \add you will have\add* the wings of a dove covered with silver, and her breast with \f + \fr 67:14 \fqa Lit. \ft greenness of gold.\f*yellow gold. 
\q1
\v 15 When the heavenly One scatters kings upon it, they will be made snow-white in Selmon. 
\q1
\v 16 The mountain of God is a rich mountain; a \f + \fr 67:16 \fqa Gr. \ft curdled like cheese.\f*swelling mountain, a rich mountain. 
\q1
\v 17 Why do you conceive \add evil\add*, you swelling mountains? \add this is\add* the mountain which God has delighted to dwell in; yes, the Lord will dwell \add in it\add* forever. 
\p
\q1
\v 18 The chariots of God are ten thousand fold, thousands of rejoicing ones: the Lord is among them, in Sina, in the holy place. 
\q1
\v 19 \f + \fr 67:19 \fqa Gr. \ft having gone up.\f*You are gone up on high, you have led captivity captive, you have received gifts for man, yes, for \add they were\add* rebellious, that you might dwell among them. 
\p
\q1
\v 20 Blessed be the Lord God, blessed be the Lord daily; and the God of our salvation will prosper us. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 21 Our God is the God of salvation; and to the Lord belong the issues from death. 
\q1
\v 22 But God will crush the heads of his enemies; the hairy crown of those who go on in their trespasses. 
\q1
\v 23 The Lord said, I will bring again from Basan, I will bring \add my people\add* again through the depths of the sea. 
\q1
\v 24 That your foot may be dipped in blood, \add and\add* the tongue of your dogs \add be stained\add* with that of \add yours\add* enemies. 
\p
\q1
\v 25 Your goings, O God, have been seen; the goings of my God, the king, in the sanctuary. 
\q1
\v 26 The princes went first, next before the players on instruments, among damsels playing on timbrels. 
\q1
\v 27 Praise God in the congregations, the Lord from the fountains of Israel. 
\q1
\v 28 There is Benjamin the younger \add one\add* in ecstasy, the princes of Judah their rulers, the princes of Zebulun, the princes of Nephthali. 
\p
\q1
\v 29 O God, command you your strength: strengthen, O God, this which you have worked in us. 
\q1
\v 30 Because of your temple at Jerusalem will kings bring presents to you. 
\q1
\v 31 Rebuke the wild beasts of the reed: let the crowd of bulls with the heifers of the nations \add be rebuked\add*, so that they who have been proved with silver may not be shut out: scatter you the nations that wish for wars. 
\q1
\v 32 Ambassadors will arrive out of Egypt; Ethiopia will hasten \add to stretch out\add* her hand readily to God. 
\p
\q1
\v 33 Sing to God, you kingdoms of the earth; sing psalms to the Lord. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 34 Sing to God who \f + \fr 67:34 \fqa Gr. \ft mounts, \fqa or, \ft has mounted.\f*rides on the heaven of heaven, eastward: lo, he will utter a mighty sound with his voice. 
\q1
\v 35 Give glory to God: his excellency is over Israel, and his power is in the clouds. 
\q1
\v 36 God is wonderful \f + \fr 67:36 \fqa Or, \ft among his holy ones.\f*in his holy \add places\add*, the God of Israel: he will give power and strength to his people: blessed be God. 
\c 68 
\d
\v 1 For the end, \add a Psalm\add* of David, for \f + \fr 68:1 \ft See \xt Ps. 44. \ft title.\f*alternate \add strains\add*. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 Save me, O God; for the waters have come in to my soul. 
\q1
\v 3 I am stuck fast in deep mud, and there is no standing: I have come in to the depths of the sea, and a storm has overwhelmed me. 
\q1
\v 4 I am weary \add of\add* crying, my throat has become hoarse; my eyes have failed by my waiting on my God. 
\q1
\v 5 Those who hate me without a cause are more than the hairs of my head: my enemies that persecute me unrighteously are strengthened: then I \f + \fr 68:5 \fqa Or, \ft paid for, \fqa or, \ft made up for.\f*restored that which I didn't take away. 
\p
\q1
\v 6 O God, you know my foolishness; and my transgressions are not hidden from you. 
\q1
\v 7 Don't let those who wait on you, O Lord of hosts, be ashamed on my account: don't let those who seek you, be ashamed on my account, O God of Israel. 
\q1
\v 8 For I have suffered reproach for your sake; shame has covered my face. 
\q1
\v 9 I became foreign to my brothers, and a stranger to my mother's children. 
\q1
\v 10 \x + \xo 68:10 \xt John 2. 17; Rom. 15. 3.\x* For the zeal of your house has eaten me up; and the reproaches of those who reproached you are fallen upon me. 
\q1
\v 11 I bowed down my soul with fasting, and that was made my reproach. 
\q1
\v 12 I put on sackcloth for my covering; and I became a proverb to them. 
\q1
\v 13 Those who sit in the gate talked against me, and those who drank wine sang against me. 
\p
\q1
\v 14 But I \add will cry\add* to you, O Lord, in my prayer; O God, it is a propitious time: in the multitude of your mercy hear me, in the truth of your salvation. 
\q1
\v 15 Save me from the mud, that I stick not \add in it\add*: let me be delivered from those who hate me, and from the deep waters. 
\q1
\v 16 Don't let the waterflood drown me, nor let the deep swallow me up; neither let the well shut its mouth upon me. 
\q1
\v 17 Hear me, O Lord; for your mercy is good: according to the multitude of your compassions look upon me. 
\q1
\v 18 Don't turn away your face from your \f + \fr 68:18 \fqa Or, \ft son.\f*servant; for I am afflicted: hear me speedily. 
\q1
\v 19 Draw near to my soul and redeem it: deliver me because of my enemies. 
\p
\q1
\v 20 For you know my reproach, and my shame, and my confusion; all that afflict me are before you. 
\q1
\v 21 My soul has waited for reproach and misery; and I waited for one to grieve with me, but there was none; and for one to comfort me, but I found none. 
\q1
\v 22 They gave \add me\add* also gall for my food, and made me drink vinegar for my thirst. 
\q1
\v 23 \x + \xo 68:23 \xt Rom. 11. 9,10.\x* Let their table before them be for a snare, and for a recompence, and for a stumbling-block. 
\q1
\v 24 Let their eyes be darkened that they should not see; and bow down their back continually. 
\q1
\v 25 Pour out your wrath upon them, and let the fury of your anger take hold on them. 
\q1
\v 26 \x + \xo 68:26 \xt Acts 1. 20.\x* Let their habitation be made desolate; and let there be no inhabitant in their tents: 
\q1
\v 27 because they persecuted him whom you have struck; and they have added to the grief of my wounds. 
\q1
\v 28 Add wickedness to their wickedness; and don't let them come into your righteousness. 
\q1
\v 29 Let them be blotted out of the book of the living, and don't let them be written with the righteous. 
\p
\q1
\v 30 I am poor and sorrowful; but the salvation of your face has helped me. 
\q1
\v 31 I will praise the name of my God with a song, I will magnify him with praise; 
\q1
\v 32 and \add this\add* will please God more than a young calf having horns and hoofs. 
\q1
\v 33 Let the poor see and rejoice; seek the Lord diligently, and you will live. 
\q1
\v 34 For the Lord hears the poor, and does not despise his fettered ones. 
\q1
\v 35 Let the heavens and the earth praise him, the sea, and all things moving in them. 
\q1
\v 36 For God will save Zion, and the cities of Judea will be built; and \add men\add* will dwell there, and inherit it. 
\q1
\v 37 The seed of his servants will possess it, and those who love his name will dwell therein. 
\c 69 
\d
\v 1 For the end, by David for a remembrance, that the Lord may save me. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 Draw near, O God, to my help. 
\q1
\v 3 Let them be ashamed and greatly agitated that seek my soul: let them be turned backward and put to shame, that wish me evil. 
\q1
\v 4 Let those who say to me, Aha, aha, be turned back and put to shame immediately. 
\q1
\v 5 Let all that seek you exult and be glad in you: and let those that love your salvation say continually, Let God be magnified. 
\q1
\v 6 But I am poor and needy; O God, help me: you are my helper and deliverer, O Lord, don't delay. 
\c 70 
\d
\v 1 By David, \add a Psalm sung by\add* the sons of Jonadab, and the first that were taken captive. 
\p O Lord, I have hoped in you: let me never be put to shame. 
\q1
\v 2 In your righteousness deliver me and rescue me: incline your ear to me, and save me. 
\q1
\v 3 Be to me a protecting God, and a strong hold to save me: for you are my fortress and my refuge. 
\q1
\v 4 Deliver me, O my God, from the hand of the sinner, from the hand of the transgressor and unjust man. 
\q1
\v 5 For you are my support, O Lord; O Lord, \add you are\add* my hope from my youth. 
\q1
\v 6 On you have I been stayed from the womb: from the belly of my mother you are my protector: of you is my \f + \fr 70:6 \fqa Gr. \ft hymn singing.\f*praise continually. 
\p
\q1
\v 7 I have become as it were a wonder to many; but you are \add my\add* strong helper. 
\q1
\v 8 Let my mouth be filled with praise, that I may hymn your glory, \add and\add* your majesty all the day. 
\q1
\v 9 Didn't cast me off at the time of old age; don't forsake me when my strength fails. 
\q1
\v 10 For my enemies have spoken against me; and those who lay wait for my soul have taken counsel together, 
\q1
\v 11 saying, God has forsaken him: persecute you and take him; for there is no one to deliver \add him\add*. 
\q1
\v 12 O God, don't go far from me, O my God, draw near to my help. 
\q1
\v 13 Let those that plot against my soul be ashamed and completely fail: let those that seek my hurt be clothed with shame and dishonour. 
\p
\q1
\v 14 But I will hope continually, and will praise you more and more. 
\q1
\v 15 My mouth will declare your righteousness openly, \add and\add* your salvation all the day; for I am not acquainted with the affairs \add of men\add*. 
\q1
\v 16 I will go on in the might of the Lord: O Lord, I will make mention of your righteousness only. 
\q1
\v 17 O God, you have taught me from my youth, and until now will I declare your wonders; 
\q1
\v 18 even until I am old and advanced in years. O God, don't forsake me; until I will have declared your arm to all the generation that is to come: 
\q1
\v 19 even your power and your righteousness, O God, up to the highest \add heavens, even\add* the mighty works which you have done: O God, who is like to you? 
\p
\q1
\v 20 What afflictions many and sore have you showed me! Yet you did turn and quicken me, and brought me again from the depths of the earth. 
\q1
\v 21 You did multiply your righteousness, and did turn and comfort me, and brought me again out of the depths of the earth. 
\q1
\v 22 I will also therefore give thanks to you, O God, \add because of\add* your truth, on an instrument of psalmody: I will sing psalms to you on the harp, O Holy One of Israel. 
\q1
\v 23 My lips will rejoice when I sing to you; and my soul, which you have redeemed. 
\q1
\v 24 Moreover also my tongue will \f + \fr 70:24 \fqa Lit. \ft meditate.\f*dwell all the day upon your righteousness; when they will be ashamed and greatly agitated that seek my hurt. 
\c 71 
\d
\v 1 For Solomon. 
\p O God, give your judgment to the king, and your righteousness to the king's son; 
\q1
\v 2 \add that he may\add* judge your people with righteousness, and your poor with judgment. 
\p
\q1
\v 3 Let the mountains and the hills raise peace to your people: 
\q1
\v 4 he will judge the poor of the people in righteousness, and save the children of the needy; and will bring low the false accuser. 
\q1
\v 5 He will continue as long as the sun, and before the moon forever. 
\q1
\v 6 He will come down as rain upon a fleece; and as drops falling upon the earth. 
\q1
\v 7 In his days will righteousness spring up; and abundance of peace till the moon be removed. 
\q1
\v 8 He will have dominion from sea to sea, and from the river to the ends of the earth. 
\q1
\v 9 The Ethiopians will fall down before him; and his enemies will lick the dust. 
\q1
\v 10 The kings of Tharsis, and the isles, will bring presents: the kings of the Arabs and Saba will offer gifts. 
\q1
\v 11 All kings will worship him; all the nations will serve him. 
\q1
\v 12 For he has delivered the poor from the oppressor; and the needy who had no helper. 
\q1
\v 13 He will spare the poor and needy, and will deliver the souls of the needy. 
\q1
\v 14 He will redeem their souls from usury and injustice: and their name \add will be\add* precious before him. 
\q1
\v 15 He will live, and there will be given him of the gold of Arabia: and \add men\add* will pray for him continually; \add and\add* all the day will they praise him. 
\q1
\v 16 There will be an establishment on the earth on the tops of the mountains: the fruit of it will be exalted above Lebanon, and they of the city will flourish as grass of the earth. 
\p
\q1
\v 17 Let his name be blessed forever: his name will endure \f + \fr 71:17 \fqa Gr. \ft before.\f*longer than the sun: and all the tribes of the earth will be blessed in him: all nations will call him blessed. 
\p
\q1
\v 18 Blessed is the Lord God of Israel, who alone does wonders. 
\q1
\v 19 Blessed is his glorious name forever, even forever and ever: and all the earth will be filled with his glory. So be it, so be it. 
\d
\v 20 The hymns of David the son of Jessæ are ended. 
\c 72 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm for Asaph. 
\p How good is God to Israel, to the upright in heart! 
\q1
\v 2 But my feet were almost overthrown; my goings very nearly slipped. 
\q1
\v 3 For I was zealous of the transgressors, beholding the tranquillity of sinners. 
\p
\q1
\v 4 For there is no sign of reluctance in their death: and \add they have\add* firmness under their affliction. 
\q1
\v 5 They are not in the troubles of \add other\add* men; and they will not be scourged with \add other\add* men. 
\q1
\v 6 Therefore pride has possessed them; they have clothed themselves with their injustice and ungodliness. 
\q1
\v 7 Their injustice will go forth as out of fatness: they have fulfilled their intention. 
\q1
\v 8 They have taken counsel and spoken in wickedness: they have uttered unrighteousness loftily. 
\q1
\v 9 They have set their mouth against heaven, and their tongue has gone through upon the earth. 
\q1
\v 10 Therefore will my people return here: and full days will be found \f + \fr 72:10 \fqa Gr. \ft in.\f*with them. 
\q1
\v 11 They said, How does God know? And \f + \fr 72:11 \fqa Gr. \ft if there is.\f*is there knowledge in the Most High? 
\q1
\v 12 Behold, these \add are\add* the sinners, and those who prosper always: they have possessed wealth. 
\p
\q1
\v 13 I said, Truly in vain have I justified my heart, and washed my hands in innocency. 
\q1
\v 14 For I was plagued all the day, and my reproof \add was\add* every morning. 
\q1
\v 15 If I said, I will speak thus; behold, I \add should\add* have broken covenant with the generation of your children. 
\q1
\v 16 I undertook to understand this, \add but\add* it is too hard for me, 
\q1
\v 17 until I go into the sanctuary of God; \add and so\add* understand the latter end. 
\p
\q1
\v 18 Surely you have appointed \add judgments\add* to them because of their crafty dealings: you have cast them down when they were lifted up. 
\q1
\v 19 How have they become desolate! Suddenly they have failed: they have perished because of their wickedness. 
\q1
\v 20 As the dream of one awakening, O Lord, in your city you will despise their image. 
\p
\q1
\v 21 For my heart has rejoiced, and my reins have been \f + \fr 72:21 \fqa Gr. \ft changed.\f*gladdened. 
\q1
\v 22 But I \add was\add* vile and didn't know: I became brutish before you. 
\q1
\v 23 Yet I am continually with you: you have holden my right hand. 
\q1
\v 24 You have guided me by your counsel, and you have taken me to yourself with glory. 
\q1
\v 25 For what have I in heaven \add but you\add*? And what have I desired upon the earth beside you? 
\q1
\v 26 My heart and my flesh have failed: \add but\add* God \add is the strength\add* of my heart, and God is my portion forever. 
\p
\q1
\v 27 For, behold, those who remove themselves far from you will perish: you have destroyed every one that goes a whoring from you. 
\q1
\v 28 But it is good for me to cling close to God, to put my trust in the Lord; that I may proclaim all your praises in the gates of the daughter of Zion. 
\c 73 
\d
\v 1 \add A Psalm\add* of \f + \fr 73:1 \fqa Gr. \ft understanding.\f*instruction for Asaph. 
\p Why have you rejected \add us\add*, O God, forever? \add why\add* is your wrath kindled against the sheep of your pasture? 
\q1
\v 2 Remember your congregation which you have purchased from the beginning; you did ransom the rod of your inheritance; this mount Zion wherein you have dwelt. 
\q1
\v 3 Lift up your hands against their pride continually; \add because of\add* all that the enemy has done wickedly in your holy places. 
\p
\q1
\v 4 Those who hate you have boasted among your feast; they have set up their standards for signs, 
\q1
\v 5 ignorantly as it were in the entrance above; 
\q1
\v 6 they cut down its doors at once with axes as in a wood of trees; they have broken it down with hatchet and stone cutter. 
\q1
\v 7 They have burnt your sanctuary with fire to the ground; they have profaned the \f + \fr 73:7 \fqa Gr. \ft tabernacle.\f*habitation of your name. 
\q1
\v 8 They have said in their heart, \add even\add* all their kindred together, Come, let us abolish the feasts of the Lord from the earth. 
\q1
\v 9 We have not seen our signs; there is no longer a prophet; and \add God\add* will not know us any more. 
\p
\q1
\v 10 How long, O God, will the enemy reproach? Will the enemy provoke your name forever? 
\q1
\v 11 Why turnest you away your hand, and your right hand from the midst of your bosom forever? 
\q1
\v 12 But God is our King \f + \fr 73:12 \fqa Gr. \ft before the age.\f*of old; he has worked salvation among the earth. 
\q1
\v 13 You did establish the sea, in your might, you did break to pieces the heads of the \f + \fr 73:13 \fqa Or, \ft serpents.\f*dragons in the water. 
\q1
\v 14 You did break to pieces the heads of the dragon; you did give him \add for\add* food to the Ethiopian nations. 
\q1
\v 15 You did cling fountains and torrents; you driedst up \f + \fr 73:15 \fqa Heb. \ft rivers of Etham.\f*mighty rivers. 
\q1
\v 16 The day is yours, and the night is yours; you have prepared the sun and the moon. 
\q1
\v 17 You have made all the borders of the earth; you have made summer and spring. 
\p
\q1
\v 18 Remember this your creation: an enemy has reproached the Lord, and a foolish people has provoked your name. 
\q1
\v 19 Don't deliver to the wild beasts a soul that gives praise to you: forget not forever the souls of your poor. 
\q1
\v 20 Look upon your covenant: for the dark \add places\add* of the earth are filled with the habitations of wickedness. 
\q1
\v 21 Don't let the afflicted and shamed one be rejected: the poor and needy will praise your name. 
\q1
\v 22 Arise, O God, plead your cause: remember your reproaches that come from the foolish one all the day. 
\q1
\v 23 Forget not the voice of your petitioners: let the pride of those who hate you continually ascend before you. 
\c 74 
\d
\v 1 For the end, Don't destroy, a Psalm of a Song for Asaph. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 We will give thanks to you, O God, we will give thanks, and call upon your name: I will declare all your wonderful works. 
\q1
\v 3 When I will take a set time, I will judge righteously. 
\q1
\v 4 The earth is dissolved, and all that dwell in it: I have strengthened its pillars. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 5 I said to the transgressors, Do not transgress; and to the sinners, Lift not up the horn. 
\q1
\v 6 Lift not up your horn on high; don't speak unrighteousness against God. 
\q1
\v 7 For \add good comes\add* neither from the east, nor from the west, nor from the desert mountains. 
\q1
\v 8 For God is the judge; he puts down one, and raises up another. 
\q1
\v 9 For \add there is\add* a cup in the hand of the Lord, full of unmingled wine; and he has \f + \fr 74:9 \fqa Gr. \ft from this into that.\f*turned \add it\add* from side to side, but its dregs have not been wholly poured out; all the sinners of the earth will drink \add them\add*. 
\p
\q1
\v 10 But I will exult forever: I will sing praises to the God of Jacob. 
\q1
\v 11 I will break all the horns of sinners; but the horns of the righteous one will be exalted. 
\c 75 
\d
\v 1 For the end, among the Hymns, a Psalm for Asaph; a Song for the Assyrian. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 God is known in Judea; his name is great in Israel. 
\q1
\v 3 His place has been in \f + \fr 75:3 \fqa Or, \ft Salem, see the Hebrew.\f*peace, and his dwelling-place in Zion. 
\q1
\v 4 There he broke the power of the bows, the shield, and the sword, and the battle. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 5 You do wonderfully shine forth from the everlasting mountains. 
\q1
\v 6 All the simple ones in heart were troubled; all the men of wealth have slept their sleep, and have found nothing in their hands. 
\q1
\v 7 At your rebuke, O God of Jacob, the riders on horses slumbered. 
\q1
\v 8 You are terrible; and who will withstand you, because of your anger? 
\q1
\v 9 You did cause judgment to be heard from heaven; the earth feared, and was still, 
\q1
\v 10 when God arose to judgment, to save all the meek in heart. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 11 For the inward thought of man will give thanks to you: and the memorial of his inward thought will keep a feast to you. 
\q1
\v 12 Vow, and pay \add your vows\add* to the Lord our God; all that are all around him will bring gifts, \add even\add* to him that is terrible, 
\q1
\v 13 and that takes away the spirits of princes; to him that is terrible among the kings of the earth. 
\c 76 
\d
\v 1 For the end, for Idithun, a Psalm of Asaph. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 I cried to the Lord with my voice, yes, my voice \add was addressed\add* to God; and he gave heed to me. 
\q1
\v 3 In the day of my affliction I earnestly sought the Lord; \add even\add* with my hands by night before him, and I was not deceived; my soul refused to be comforted. 
\q1
\v 4 I remembered God, and rejoiced; I poured out my complaint, and my soul fainted. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 5 All my enemies set a watch \add against me\add*: I was troubled, and didn't speak. 
\p
\q1
\v 6 I considered the days of old, and remembered ancient years. 
\q1
\v 7 I meditated; I communed with my heart by night, and diligently searched my spirit, \add saying\add*, 
\q1
\v 8 Will the Lord cast off forever? And will he be well pleased no more? 
\q1
\v 9 Will he cut off his mercy forever, even forever and ever? 
\q1
\v 10 Will God forget to pity? Or will he shut up his compassions in his wrath? \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 11 I said, Now I have begun; this is the change of the right hand of the Most High. 
\q1
\v 12 I remembered the works of the Lord; for I will remember your wonders from the beginning. 
\q1
\v 13 I will meditate on all your works, and will consider your doings. 
\p
\q1
\v 14 O God, your way is in the sanctuary; who is a great God as our God? 
\q1
\v 15 You are the God who do wonders; you have made known your power among the nations. 
\q1
\v 16 You have with your arm redeemed your people, the sons of Jacob and Joseph. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 17 The waters saw you, O God, the waters saw you, and feared; and the depths were troubled. 
\q1
\v 18 \add There was\add* an abundant sound of waters: the clouds uttered a voice; for your arrows went abroad. 
\q1
\v 19 The voice of your thunder was abroad, and around your lightnings appeared to the world; the earth trembled and quaked. 
\q1
\v 20 Your way is in the sea, and your paths in many waters, and your footsteps cannot be known. 
\q1
\v 21 You did guide your people as sheep by the hand of Moses and Aaron. 
\c 77 
\d
\v 1 \add A Psalm\add* of \f + \fr 77:1 \fqa Gr. \ft understanding.\f*instruction for Asaph. 
\p Give heed, O my people, to my law: incline your ear to the words of my mouth. 
\q1
\v 2 \x + \xo 77:2 \xt Mat. 13. 35.\x* I will open my mouth in parables: I will utter dark sayings \add which have been\add* from the beginning. 
\q1
\v 3 All which we have heard and known, and our fathers have declared to us. 
\q1
\v 4 They were not hid from their children to a second generation; \add the fathers\add* declaring the praises of the Lord, and his mighty acts, and his wonders which he worked. 
\p
\q1
\v 5 He raised up a testimony in Jacob, and appointed a law in Israel, which he commanded our fathers, to make it known to their children: 
\q1
\v 6 that another generation might know, even the sons which should be born; and they should arise and declare them to their children. 
\q1
\v 7 That they might set their hope on God, and not forget the works of God, but diligently seek his commandments. 
\q1
\v 8 That they should not be as their fathers, a perverse and provoking generation; a generation which set not its heart aright, and its spirit was not \f + \fr 77:8 \fqa Or, \ft faithfully secured.\f*steadfast with God. 
\p
\q1
\v 9 The children of Ephraim, bending and shooting \add with\add* the bow, turned \add back\add* in the day of battle. 
\q1
\v 10 They didn't keep the covenant of God, and would not walk in his law. 
\q1
\v 11 They forgot his benefits, and his miracles which he \add had\add* showed them; 
\q1
\v 12 the miracles which he worked before their fathers, in the land of Egypt, in the plain of Tanes. 
\q1
\v 13 He clave the sea, and led them through: he made the waters to stand as \add in\add* a bottle. 
\q1
\v 14 He guided them with a cloud by day, and all the night with a light of fire. 
\q1
\v 15 He clave a rock in the wilderness, and made them drink as in a great deep. 
\q1
\v 16 He brought water out of the rock, and caused waters to flow down as rivers. 
\p
\q1
\v 17 They sinned yet more against him; they provoked the Most High in the wilderness. 
\q1
\v 18 They tempted God in their hearts, in asking food for \add the desire of\add* their souls. 
\q1
\v 19 They spoke also against God, and said, Will God be able to prepare a table in the wilderness? 
\q1
\v 20 Although he struck the rock, and the waters flowed, and the torrents ran abundantly; will he be able also to give bread, or prepare a table for his people? 
\p
\q1
\v 21 Therefore the Lord heard, and was provoked: and fire was kindled in Jacob, and wrath went up against Israel. 
\q1
\v 22 Because they didn't believe in God, and didn't trust in his salvation. 
\q1
\v 23 Yet he commanded the clouds from above, and opened the doors of heaven, 
\q1
\v 24 and rained upon them manna to eat, and gave them the bread of heaven. 
\q1
\v 25 Man ate angels' bread; \x + \xo 77:25 \xt Mat. 6. 31.\x* he sent them provision to the full. 
\p
\q1
\v 26 He removed the south wind from heaven; and by his might he brought in the south-west wind. 
\q1
\v 27 He rained upon them flesh like dust, and feathered birds like the sand of the seas. 
\q1
\v 28 They fell into the midst of their camp, all around their tents. 
\q1
\v 29 So they ate, and were completely filled; and he gave them their desire. 
\p
\q1
\v 30 They were not disappointed of their desire: \add but\add* when their food was yet in their mouth, 
\q1
\v 31 then the indignation of God rose up against them, and killed the fattest of them, and overthrew the choice men of Israel. 
\p
\q1
\v 32 Among all this they sinned yet more, and didn't believe his miracles. 
\q1
\v 33 Their days were consumed in vanity, and their years with anxiety. 
\p
\q1
\v 34 When he killed them, they sought him: and they returned and called betimes upon God. 
\q1
\v 35 They remembered that God was their helper, and the most high God was their redeemer. 
\q1
\v 36 Yet they loved him \add only\add* with their mouth, and lied to him with their tongue. 
\q1
\v 37 For their heart \add was\add* not right with him, neither were they steadfast in his covenant. 
\p
\q1
\v 38 But he is compassionate, and will \f + \fr 77:38 \fqa Gr. \ft be propitious, \fqa or, \ft merciful to.\f*forgive their sins, and will not destroy \add them\add*: yes, he will frequently turn away his wrath, and will not kindle all his anger. 
\q1
\v 39 He remembered that they are flesh; a wind that passes away, and returns not. 
\p
\q1
\v 40 How often did they provoke him in the wilderness, \add and\add* anger him in a dry land! 
\q1
\v 41 Yes, they turned back, and tempted God, and provoked the Holy One of Israel. 
\q1
\v 42 They didn't remember his hand, the day in which he delivered them from the hand of the oppressor. 
\q1
\v 43 How he had worked his signs in Egypt, and his wonders in the field of Tanes: 
\q1
\v 44 and had changed their rivers into blood; and their \f + \fr 77:44 \fqa Gr. \ft rains, \fqa or, \ft showers.\f*streams, that they should not drink. 
\q1
\v 45 He sent against them the dog-fly, and it devoured them; and the frog, and it spoiled them. 
\q1
\v 46 He gave their fruit to the canker worm, and their labours to the locust. 
\q1
\v 47 He killed their vines with hail, and their sycamores with frost. 
\q1
\v 48 He gave up their cattle to hail, and their substance to the fire. 
\q1
\v 49 He sent out against them the fury of his anger, wrath, and indignation, and affliction, a message by evil angels. 
\q1
\v 50 He made a way for his wrath; he spared not their souls from death, but consigned their cattle to death; 
\q1
\v 51 and struck every first-born in the land of Egypt; the first-fruits of their labours in the tents of Cham. 
\q1
\v 52 He removed his people like sheep; he led them as a flock in the wilderness. 
\q1
\v 53 He guided them with hope, and they didn't fear: but the sea covered their enemies. 
\q1
\v 54 He brought them in to the mountain of his sanctuary, this mountain which his right hand had purchased. 
\q1
\v 55 He cast out the nations from before them, and made them to inherit by a line of inheritance, and made the tribes of Israel to dwell in their tents. 
\p
\q1
\v 56 Yet they tempted and provoked the most high God, and didn't keep his testimonies. 
\q1
\v 57 They turned back, and broke covenant, even as also their fathers: they became like a crooked bow. 
\q1
\v 58 They provoked him with their high places, and moved him to zeal with their graven images. 
\p
\q1
\v 59 God heard and \f + \fr 77:59 \fqa Lit. \ft overlooked them. See \xt Acts 17. 30.\f*lightly regarded \add them\add*, and greatly despised Israel. 
\q1
\v 60 He rejected the tabernacle of Selom, his tent where he dwelt among men. 
\q1
\v 61 He gave their strength into captivity, and their beauty into the enemy's hand. 
\q1
\v 62 He \f + \fr 77:62 \fqa Gr. \ft shut up.\f*gave his people to the sword; and disdained his inheritance. 
\q1
\v 63 Fire devoured their young men; and their virgins mourned not. 
\q1
\v 64 Their priests fell by the sword; and their widows will not be wept for. 
\p
\q1
\v 65 So the Lord awoke as one out of sleep, \add and\add* as a mighty man who has been heated with wine. 
\q1
\v 66 He struck his enemies in the hinder parts: he brought on them a perpetual reproach. 
\p
\q1
\v 67 He rejected the tabernacle of Joseph, and chose not the tribe of Ephraim; 
\q1
\v 68 but chose the tribe of Judah, the mount Zion which he loved. 
\q1
\v 69 He built his sanctuary as \add the place\add* of unicorns; he founded it forever on the earth. 
\q1
\v 70 He chose David also his servant, and took him up from the flocks of sheep. 
\q1
\v 71 He took him from following the ewes great with young, to be the shepherd of Jacob his servant, and Israel his inheritance. 
\q1
\v 72 So he tended them in the innocency of his heart; and guided them by the skilfulness of his hands. 
\c 78 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm for Asaph. 
\p O God, the nations have come into your inheritance; they have polluted your holy temple; they have made Jerusalem a storehouse of fruits. 
\q1
\v 2 They have given the dead bodies of your servants \add to be\add* food for the birds of the sky, the flesh of your holy ones for the wild beasts of the earth. 
\q1
\v 3 They have shed their blood as water, all around Jerusalem; and there was none to bury \add them\add*. 
\q1
\v 4 We have become a reproach to our neighbours, a scorn and derision to them \add that are\add* all around us. 
\p
\q1
\v 5 How long, O Lord? Will you be angry forever? Will your zeal burn like fire? 
\q1
\v 6 Pour out your wrath upon the nations that have not known you, and upon the kingdoms which have not called upon your name. 
\q1
\v 7 For they have devoured Jacob, and laid his place waste. 
\p
\q1
\v 8 Don't remember our old transgressions; let your tender mercies speedily prevent us; for we are greatly impoverished. 
\q1
\v 9 Help us, O God our Saviour; for the glory of your name, O Lord, deliver us; and be merciful to our sins, for your name's sake. 
\q1
\v 10 Lest haply they should say among the nations, Where is their God? And let the avenging of your servants' blood that has been shed be known among the nations before our eyes. 
\p
\q1
\v 11 Let the groaning of the prisoners come in before you; according to the greatness of your arm preserve the \f + \fr 78:11 \fqa i. e. \ft men appointed to die.\f*sons of the killed ones. 
\q1
\v 12 Repay to our neighbours sevenfold into their bosom their reproach, with which they have reproached you, O Lord. 
\q1
\v 13 For we are your people and the sheep of your pasture; we will give you thanks forever; we will declare your praise throughout all generations. 
\c 79 
\d
\v 1 For the \f + \fr 79:1 \ft See \xt Ps. 44, \ft and \xt 68, \ft titles.\f*end, for alternate \add strains\add*, a testimony for Asaph, a Psalm concerning the Assyrian. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 Pay attention, O Shepherd of Israel, who guidest Joseph like a flock; you who sits upon the cherubs, manifest yourself; 
\q1
\v 3 before Ephraim and Benjamin and Manasse, stir up your power, and come to deliver us. 
\q1
\v 4 Turn us, O God, and cause your face to shine; and we will be delivered. 
\p
\q1
\v 5 O Lord God of hosts, how long are you angry with the prayer of your servant? 
\q1
\v 6 You will feed us with bread of tears; and will cause us to drink tears by measure. 
\q1
\v 7 You have made us a strife to our neighbours; and our enemies have mocked at us. 
\q1
\v 8 Turn us, O Lord God of hosts, and cause your face to shine; and we will be saved. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 9 You have transplanted a vine out of Egypt: you have cast out the nations, and planted it. 
\q1
\v 10 You made a way before it, and did cause its roots to strike, and the land was filled \add with it\add*. 
\q1
\v 11 Its shadow covered the mountains, and its shoots \add equalled\add* the \f + \fr 79:11 \fqa Gr. \ft Cedars of God, see \xt Gen. 30. 8; Jon. 3. 3; Acts 7. 20.\f*goodly cedars. 
\q1
\v 12 It sent its branches to the sea, and its shoots to the river. 
\q1
\v 13 Why have you broken down its hedge, while all that pass by the way pluck it? 
\q1
\v 14 The boar out of the wood has laid it waste, and the wild beast has devoured it. 
\p
\q1
\v 15 O God of hosts, turn, we pray you: look on \add us\add* from heaven, and behold and visit this vine; 
\q1
\v 16 and restore that which your right hand has planted: and look on the son of man whom you did strengthen for yourself. 
\q1
\v 17 \add It is\add* burnt with fire and dug up: they will perish at the rebuke of your \f + \fr 79:17 \fqa Gr. \ft See \xt Ps. 20. 9.\f*presence. 
\q1
\v 18 Let your hand be upon the man of your right hand, and upon the son of man whom you did strengthen for yourself. 
\p
\q1
\v 19 So will we not depart from you: you will quicken us, and we will call upon your name. 
\q1
\v 20 Turn us, O Lord God of hosts, and make your face to shine; and we will be saved. 
\c 80 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm for \f + \fr 80:1 \fqa Alex. \ft David.\f*Asaph, concerning the wine-presses. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 Rejoice in God our helper; shout aloud to the God of Jacob. 
\q1
\v 3 Take a psalm, and produce the timbrel, the pleasant psaltery with the harp. 
\q1
\v 4 Blow the trumpet at the new moon, in the glorious day of \f + \fr 80:4 \fqa Alex. \ft our.\f*your feast. 
\p
\q1
\v 5 For \add this\add* is an ordinance for Israel, and a statute of the God of Jacob. 
\q1
\v 6 He made \f + \fr 80:6 \fqa Gr. \ft him, \fqa sc. \ft Israel.\f*it \add to be\add* a testimony in Joseph, when he came forth out of the land of Egypt: he heard a language which he didn't understand. 
\p
\q1
\v 7 He removed his back from burdens: his hands slaved in making the baskets. 
\q1
\v 8 You did call upon me in trouble, and I delivered you; I heard you in the secret place of the storm: I proved you at the water of \f + \fr 80:8 \fqa Lit. \ft contradiction.\f*Strife. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 9 Hear, my people, and I will speak to you, O Israel; and I will testify to you: if you will listen to me; 
\q1
\v 10 there will be no new god in you; neither will you worship a foreign god. 
\q1
\v 11 For I am the Lord your God, that brought you out of the land of Egypt: open your mouth wide, and I will fill it. 
\q1
\v 12 But my people didn't listen to my voice; and Israel gave no heed to me. 
\q1
\v 13 So I let them go after the ways of their own hearts: they will go on in their own ways. 
\p
\q1
\v 14 If my people had listened to me, if Israel had walked in my ways, 
\q1
\v 15 I should have put down their enemies very quickly, and should have laid my hand upon those that afflicted them. 
\q1
\v 16 The Lord's enemies \add should have\add* lied to him: but \f + \fr 80:16 \fqa sc. \ft of the others.\f*their time will be forever. 
\q1
\v 17 He fed them with the fat of wheat; and satisfied them with honey out of the rock. 
\c 81 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm for Asaph. 
\p God stands in the assembly of gods; and in the midst \add of them\add* will judge gods. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 How long will you judge unrighteously, and accept the persons of sinners? \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 3 Judge the orphan and poor: \f + \fr 81:3 \fqa Gr. \ft justify.\f*do justice to the low and needy. 
\q1
\v 4 Rescue the needy, and deliver the poor out of the hand of the sinner. 
\p
\q1
\v 5 They don't know, nor understand; they walk on in darkness: all the foundations of the earth will are shaken. 
\q1
\v 6 I have said, You are gods; and all \add of you\add* children of the Most High. 
\q1
\v 7 But you die as men, and fall as one of the princes. 
\p
\q1
\v 8 Arise, O God, judge the earth: for you will inherit all nations. 
\c 82 
\d
\v 1 A Song of a Psalm for Asaph. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 O God, who will be compared to you? Don't be silent, neither be still, O God. 
\p
\q1
\v 3 For behold, your enemies have made a noise; and those who hate you have lifted up the head. 
\q1
\v 4 Against your people they have craftily imagined a device, and have taken counsel against your saints. 
\q1
\v 5 They have said, Come, and let us completely destroy them out of the nation; and let the name of Israel be remembered no more at all. 
\q1
\v 6 For they have taken counsel together with one consent: they have made a confederacy against you; 
\q1
\v 7 even the tents of the Idumeans, and the Ismaelites; Moab, and the Agarenes; 
\q1
\v 8 Gebal, and Ammon, and Amalec; the Philistines also, with those who dwell at Tyre. 
\q1
\v 9 Yes, Assur too has come with them: they have become a help to the children of Lot. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 10 Do you to them as to Midian, and to Sisera; as to Jabin at the brook of Kison. 
\q1
\v 11 They were completely destroyed at Aendor: they became as dung for the earth. 
\q1
\v 12 Make their princes as Oreb and Zeb, and Zebee and Salmana; \add even\add* all their princes: 
\q1
\v 13 who said, Let us take to ourselves the \f + \fr 82:13 \fqa Alex. \ft sanctuary.\f*altar of God as an inheritance. 
\q1
\v 14 O my God, make them as a wheel; as stubble before the face of the wind. 
\q1
\v 15 As fire which will burn up a wood, as the flame may consume the mountains; 
\q1
\v 16 so will you persecute them with your tempest, and trouble them in your anger. 
\q1
\v 17 Fill their faces with dishonour; so will they seek your name, O Lord. 
\q1
\v 18 Let them be ashamed and troubled for evermore; yes, let them be greatly agitated and destroyed. 
\q1
\v 19 Let them know that your name is Lord; that you alone are Most High over all the earth. 
\c 83 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm for the sons of Core, concerning the wine-presses. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 How amiable are your tents, O Lord of hosts! 
\q1
\v 3 My soul longs, and faints for the courts of the Lord: my heart and my flesh have exulted in the living God. 
\q1
\v 4 Yes, the sparrow has found himself a home, and the turtle-dove a nest for herself, where she may lay her young, \add even\add* your altars, O Lord of hosts, my King, and my God. 
\p
\q1
\v 5 Blessed are those who dwell in your house: they will praise you evermore. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 6 Blessed is the man whose help is of you, O Lord; in his heart he has purposed to go up 
\q1
\v 7 the valley of weeping, to the place which he has appointed, for \add there\add* the law-giver will grant blessings. 
\q1
\v 8 They will go from strength to strength: the God of gods will be seen in Zion. 
\p
\q1
\v 9 O Lord God of hosts, hear my prayer: listen, O God of Jacob. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 10 Behold, O God our defender, and look upon the face of your anointed. 
\q1
\v 11 For one day in your courts is better than thousands. I would rather be an abject in the house of God, than dwell in the tents of sinners. 
\q1
\v 12 For the Lord loves mercy and truth: God will give grace and glory: the Lord will not withhold good things from those who walk in innocence. 
\q1
\v 13 O Lord of hosts, blessed is the man who trusts in you. 
\c 84 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm for the sons of Core. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 O Lord, you have taken pleasure in your land: you have turned back the captivity of Jacob. 
\q1
\v 3 You have forgiven your people their transgressions; you have covered all their sins. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 4 You have caused all your wrath to cease: you have turned from your fierce anger. 
\p
\q1
\v 5 Turn us, O God of our salvation, and turn your anger away from us. 
\q1
\v 6 Would you be angry with us forever? Or will you continue your wrath from generation to generation? 
\q1
\v 7 O God, you will turn and quicken us; and your people will rejoice in you. 
\q1
\v 8 Show us your mercy, O Lord, and grant us your salvation. 
\p
\q1
\v 9 I will hear what the Lord God will say concerning me: for he will speak peace to his people, and to his saints, and to those that turn their heart toward him. 
\q1
\v 10 Moreover his salvation is near those who fear him; that glory may dwell in our land. 
\q1
\v 11 Mercy and truth are met together: righteousness and peace have kissed \add each other\add*. 
\q1
\v 12 Truth has sprung out of the earth; and righteousness has looked down from heaven. 
\q1
\v 13 For the Lord will give goodness; and our land will yield her fruit. 
\q1
\v 14 Righteousness will go before him; and will set his steps in the way. 
\c 85 
\d
\v 1 A Prayer of David. 
\p O Lord, incline your ear, and listen to me; for I am poor and needy. 
\q1
\v 2 Preserve my soul, for I am holy; save your servant, O God, who hopes in you. 
\q1
\v 3 Pity me, O Lord: for to you will I cry all the day. 
\q1
\v 4 Rejoice the soul of your servant: for to you, O Lord, have I lifted up my soul. 
\q1
\v 5 For you, O Lord, are kind, and gentle; and plenteous in mercy to all that call upon you. 
\q1
\v 6 Give ear to my prayer, O Lord; and pay attention to the voice of my supplication. 
\q1
\v 7 In the day of my trouble I cried to you: for you did hear me. 
\p
\q1
\v 8 There is no one like to you, O Lord, among the gods; and there are no \add works\add* like to your works. 
\q1
\v 9 All nations whom you have made will come, and will worship before you, O Lord; and will glorify your name. 
\q1
\v 10 For you are great, and do wonders: you are the only \add and\add* the great God. 
\q1
\v 11 Guide me, O Lord, in your way, and I will walk in your truth: let my heart rejoice, that I may fear your name. 
\q1
\v 12 I will give you thanks, O Lord my God, with all my heart; and I will glorify your name forever. 
\q1
\v 13 For your mercy is great toward me; and you have delivered my soul from the lowest hell. 
\p
\q1
\v 14 O God, transgressors have risen up against me, and an assembly of violent \add men\add* have sought my life; and have not set you before them. 
\q1
\v 15 But you, O Lord God, are compassionate and merciful, long-suffering, and abundant in mercy and true. 
\q1
\v 16 Look you upon me, and have mercy upon me: give your strength to your servant, and save the son of your handmaid. 
\q1
\v 17 Establish with me a token for good; and let those who hate me see \add it\add* and be ashamed; because you, O Lord, have helped me, and comforted me. 
\c 86 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm of a Song for the sons of Core. 
\p His foundations are in the holy mountains. 
\q1
\v 2 The Lord loves the gates of Zion, more than all the tents of Jacob. 
\q1
\v 3 Glorious things have been spoken of you, O city of God. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 4 I will make mention of Raab and Babylon to those who know me: behold also the Philistines, and Tyre, and the people of the Ethiopians: these were born there. 
\q1
\v 5 A man will say, Zion \add is my\add* mother; and \add such\add* a man was born in her; and the Highest himself has founded her. 
\q1
\v 6 The Lord will recount \add it\add* in the writing of the people, and of these princes that \f + \fr 86:6 \fqa Gr. \ft have been in her.\f*were born in her. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 7 The dwelling of all within you is as \add the dwelling\add* of those that rejoice. 
\c 87 
\d
\v 1 A song of a Psalm for the sons of Core for the end, upon Maeleth for responsive \add strains\add*, of \f + \fr 87:1 \fqa Gr. \ft understanding.\f*instruction for Æman the Israelite. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 O Lord God of my salvation, I have cried by day and in the night before you. 
\q1
\v 3 Let my prayer come in before you; incline your ear to my supplication, O Lord. 
\p
\q1
\v 4 For my soul is filled with troubles, and my life has drawn near to Hades. 
\q1
\v 5 I have been reckoned with those who go down to the pit; I became as a man without help; 
\q1
\v 6 free among the dead, as the killed ones \f + \fr 87:6 \fqa Alex. \ft om. ἐῤῥιμμένοι, cast out.\f*cast out, who sleep in the tomb; whom you rememberest no more; and they are rejected from your hand. 
\q1
\v 7 They laid me in the lowest pit, in dark \add places\add*, and in the shadow of death. 
\q1
\v 8 Your wrath has pressed heavily upon me, and you have brought upon me all your billows. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 9 You have removed my acquaintance far from me; they have made me an abomination to themselves; I have been delivered up, and have not gone forth. 
\q1
\v 10 My eyes are dimmed from poverty; but I cried to you, O Lord, all the day; I spread forth my hands to you. 
\p
\q1
\v 11 Will you work wonders for the dead? Or will \f + \fr 87:11 \ft See \fqa Heb.\f*physicians raise \add them\add* up, that they will praise you? 
\q1
\v 12 Will any one declare your mercy in the tomb? And your truth in destruction? 
\q1
\v 13 Will your wonders be known in darkness? And your righteousness in a forgotten land? 
\q1
\v 14 But I cried to you, O Lord; and in the morning will my prayer prevent you. 
\p
\q1
\v 15 Wherefore, O Lord, do you reject my \f + \fr 87:15 \fqa Heb. \ft and \fqa Alex. \ft soul.\f*prayer, \add and\add* turn your face away from me? 
\q1
\v 16 I am poor and in troubles from my youth; and having been exalted, I was brought low and into \f + \fr 87:16 \ft See \xt 2 Cor. 4. 8.\f*despair. 
\q1
\v 17 Your wrath has passed over me; and your terrors have greatly disquieted me. 
\q1
\v 18 They compassed me like water; all the day they beset me together. 
\q1
\v 19 You have put far from me \f + \fr 87:19 \fqa Alex. \ft friend and neighbour.\f*\add every\add* friend, and my acquaintances because of \add my\add* wretchedness. 
\c 88 
\d
\v 1 \add A Psalm\add* of instruction for Ætham the Israelite. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 I will sing of your mercies, O Lord, forever: I will declare your truth with my mouth to all generations. 
\q1
\v 3 For you have said, Mercy will be built up forever: your truth will be established in the heavens. 
\q1
\v 4 I made a covenant with my chosen ones, I swore to David my servant. 
\q1
\v 5 I will \f + \fr 88:5 \fqa Gr. \ft prepare.\f*establish your seed forever, and build up your throne to all generations. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 6 The heavens will declare your wonders, O Lord; and your truth in the assembly of the saints. 
\q1
\v 7 For who in the \f + \fr 88:7 \fqa Gr. \ft clouds.\f*heavens will be compared to the Lord? And who will be likened to the Lord among the sons of God? 
\q1
\v 8 God is glorified in the council of the saints; great and terrible toward all that are all around him. 
\q1
\v 9 O Lord God of hosts, who is like to you? You are mighty, O Lord, and your truth is all around you. 
\q1
\v 10 You rulest the power of the sea; and you calmest the tumult of its waves. 
\q1
\v 11 You have brought down the proud as one that is killed; and with the arm of your power you have scattered your enemies. 
\q1
\v 12 The heavens are yours, and the earth is yours: you have founded the world, and the fulness of it. 
\q1
\v 13 You have created the north and the \f + \fr 88:13 \fqa Gr. \ft sea.\f*west: Thabor and Hermon will rejoice in your name. 
\q1
\v 14 Your is the mighty arm: let your hand be strengthened, let your right hand be exalted. 
\q1
\v 15 Justice and judgment are the establishment of your throne: mercy and truth will go before your face. 
\p
\q1
\v 16 Blessed is the people that knows the joyful sound: they will walk, O Lord, in the light of your face. 
\q1
\v 17 In your name will they rejoice all the day: and in your righteousness they will be exalted. 
\q1
\v 18 For you are the boast of their strength; and in your good pleasure will our horn be exalted, 
\q1
\v 19 for \add our\add* help is of the Lord; and of the Holy One of Israel, our king. 
\p
\q1
\v 20 Then you spokest in vision to your children, and said, I have laid help on a mighty one; I have exalted one chosen out of my people. 
\q1
\v 21 \x + \xo 88:21 \xt Acts 13. 22.\x* I have found David my servant; I have anointed him by \add my\add* holy \f + \fr 88:21 \fqa Heb. \ft and \fqa Alex. \ft oil, see \xt Ps. 91. 10.\f*mercy. 
\q1
\v 22 For my hand will support him; and my arm will strengthen him. 
\q1
\v 23 The enemy will have no advantage against him; and the son of transgression will not hurt him again. 
\q1
\v 24 I will hew down his foes before him, and put to flight those that hate him. 
\q1
\v 25 But my truth and my mercy will be with him; and in my name will his horn be exalted. 
\q1
\v 26 I will set his hand in the sea, and his right hand in the rivers. 
\q1
\v 27 He will call upon me, \add saying\add*, You are my Father, my God, and the helper of my salvation. 
\q1
\v 28 I will make him \add my\add* first-born, higher than the kings of the earth. 
\q1
\v 29 I will keep my mercy for him forever, and my covenant \add will be\add* firm with him. 
\q1
\v 30 I will establish his seed forever and ever, and his throne as the days of heaven. 
\p
\q1
\v 31 If his children should forsake my law, and don't walk in my judgments; 
\q1
\v 32 if they should profane my ordinances, and not keep my commandments; 
\q1
\v 33 I will visit their transgressions with a rod, and their sins with scourges. 
\q1
\v 34 But my mercy I will not completely remove from him, nor wrong my truth. 
\q1
\v 35 Neither will I by any means profane my covenant; and I will not make void the things that proceed out of my lips. 
\q1
\v 36 Once have I sworn by my holiness, that I will not lie to David. 
\q1
\v 37 His seed will endure forever, and his throne as the sun before me; 
\q1
\v 38 and as the moon \add that is\add* established forever, and as the faithful witness in heaven. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 39 But you have cast off and despise, you have rejected your anointed. 
\q1
\v 40 You have overthrown the covenant of your servant; you have profaned his sanctuary, \add casting it\add* to the ground. 
\q1
\v 41 You have broken down all his hedges; you have made his strong holds a terror. 
\q1
\v 42 All that go by the way have spoiled him: he is become a reproach to his neighbours. 
\q1
\v 43 You have exalted the right hand of his enemies; you have made all his enemies to rejoice. 
\q1
\v 44 You have turned back the help of his sword, and have not helped him in the battle. 
\q1
\v 45 You have deprived him of \f + \fr 88:45 \fqa Gr. \ft purification.\f*glory: you have broken down his throne to the ground. 
\q1
\v 46 You have shortened the days of his \f + \fr 88:46 \fqa Alex. \ft time.\f*throne: you have poured shame upon him. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 47 How long, O Lord, will you turn away, forever? Will your anger flame out as fire? 
\q1
\v 48 Remember what my being is: for have you created all the sons of men in vain? 
\q1
\v 49 What man is there who will live, and not see death? Will \add any one\add* deliver his soul from the hand of Hades? \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 50 Where are your ancient mercies, O Lord, which you swore to David in your truth? 
\q1
\v 51 Remember, O Lord, the reproach of your servants, which I have borne in my bosom, \add even the reproach\add* of many nations; 
\q1
\v 52 with which your enemies have reviled, O Lord: with which they have reviled the recompence of your anointed. 
\q1
\v 53 Blessed be the Lord forever. So be it, so be it. 
\c 89 
\d
\v 1 A Prayer of Moses the man of God. 
\p Lord, you have been our refuge in all generations. 
\q1
\v 2 Before the mountains existed, and \add before\add* the earth and the world were formed, even from age to age, You are. 
\q1
\v 3 Don't turn man back to \add his\add* low place, because you said, Return, you sons of men? 
\q1
\v 4 For a thousand years in your sight are as the yesterday which is past, and as a watch in the night. 
\q1
\v 5 Years will be \f + \fr 89:5 \fqa Gr. \ft their vanities or rejections.\f*vanity to them: let the morning pass away as grass. 
\q1
\v 6 In the morning let it flower, and pass away: in the evening let it droop, let it be withered and dried up. 
\q1
\v 7 For we have perished in your anger, and in your wrath we have been troubled. 
\q1
\v 8 You have set our transgressions before you: our age is in the light of your face. 
\q1
\v 9 For all our days have gone, and we have passed away in your wrath: our years have \f + \fr 89:9 \fqa Gr. \ft mediated.\f*spun out their tale as a spider. 
\q1
\v 10 \add As for\add* the days of our years, in them are seventy years; and if \add men should be\add* in strength, eighty years: and \f + \fr 89:10 \fqa Or, \ft what is more than these.\f*the greater part of them would be labour and trouble; for weakness overtakes us, and we will be chastened. 
\q1
\v 11 Who knows the power of your wrath? 
\q1
\v 12 and \add who knows how\add* to number \add his days\add* because of the fear of your wrath? So manifest your right hand, and those that are instructed in wisdom in the heart. 
\p
\q1
\v 13 Return, O Lord, how long? And be asked concerning your servants. 
\q1
\v 14 We have been satisfied in the morning with your mercy; and we did exult and rejoice: 
\q1
\v 15 let us rejoice in all our days, in return for the days wherein you did afflict us, the years wherein we saw evil. 
\q1
\v 16 Look upon your servants, and upon your works; and guide their children. 
\q1
\v 17 Let the brightness of the Lord our God be upon us: and do you \f + \fr 89:17 \fqa Or, \ft prosper.\f*direct for us the works of our hands.\f + \fr 89:17 \fqa Alex. \ft + yea, prosper thou the work of our hands.\f* 
\c 90 
\d
\v 1 Praise of a Song, by David. 
\p He who dwells in the help of the Highest, will sojourn under the shelter of the God of heaven. 
\q1
\v 2 He will say to the Lord, You are my helper and my refuge: my God; I will hope in him. 
\q1
\v 3 For he will deliver you from the snare of the hunters, from \add every\add* troublesome matter. 
\q1
\v 4 He will overshadow you with his shoulders, and you will trust under his wings: his truth will cover you with a shield. 
\q1
\v 5 You will not be afraid of terror by night; nor of the arrow flying by day; 
\q1
\v 6 \add nor\add* of the \add evil\add* \f + \fr 90:6 \ft See ver 3.\f*thing that walks in darkness; \add nor\add* of calamity, and the evil spirit at noon-day. 
\q1
\v 7 A thousand will fall at your side, and ten thousand at your right hand; but it will not come near you. 
\q1
\v 8 Only with your eyes will you observe and see the reward of sinners. 
\p
\q1
\v 9 For you, O Lord, are my hope: you, my soul, have made the Most High your refuge. 
\q1
\v 10 No evils will come upon you, and no scourge will draw near to your dwelling. 
\q1
\v 11 For he will give his angels charge concerning you, to keep you in all your ways. 
\q1
\v 12 \x + \xo 90:12 \xt Mat. 4. 6.\x* They will bear you up on their hands, lest at any time you dash your foot against a stone. 
\q1
\v 13 You will tread on the asp and basilisk: and you will trample on the lion and dragon. 
\p
\q1
\v 14 For he has hoped in me, and I will deliver him: I will protect him, because he has known my name. 
\q1
\v 15 He will call upon me, and I will listen to him: I am with him in affliction; and I will deliver him, and glorify him. 
\q1
\v 16 I will satisfy him with length of days, and show him my salvation. 
\c 91 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm of a Song for the Sabbath-day. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 It is a good thing to give thanks to the Lord, and to sing praises to your name, O you Most High; 
\q1
\v 3 to proclaim your mercy in the morning, and your truth by night, 
\q1
\v 4 on a psaltery of ten strings, with a song on the harp. 
\q1
\v 5 For you, O Lord, have made me glad with your work: and in the operations of your hands will I exult. 
\p
\q1
\v 6 How have your works been magnified, O Lord! Your thoughts are very deep. 
\q1
\v 7 A foolish man will not know, and a senseless man will not understand this. 
\q1
\v 8 When the sinners spring up as the grass, and all the workers of wickedness \f + \fr 91:8 \ft Perhaps, 'come to light'.\f*have watched; \add it is\add* so they may be completely destroyed forever. 
\q1
\v 9 But you, O Lord, are most high forever. 
\p
\q1
\v 10 \f + \fr 91:10 \fqa Alex. \ft + for behold thine enemies, O Lord, as in \fqa Heb.\f*For, behold, your enemies will perish; and all the workers of wickedness will be scattered. 
\q1
\v 11 But my horn will be exalted as \add the horn\add* of a unicorn; and my old age with rich \f + \fr 91:11 \fqa Alex. \ft oil. See \xt Ps. 88. 20.\f*mercy. 
\q1
\v 12 My eye has seen my enemies, and my ear will hear the wicked that rise up against me. 
\p
\q1
\v 13 The righteous will flourish as a palm-tree: he will be increased as the cedar in Lebanon. 
\q1
\v 14 Those who are planted in the house of the Lord will flourish in the courts of our God. 
\q1
\v 15 Then they will be increased in a \f + \fr 91:15 \fqa Gr. \ft fat.\f*fine old age; and they will be prosperous; so they may declare 
\q1
\v 16 that the Lord my God is righteous, and there is no wickedness in him. 
\c 92 
\d
\v 1 For \f + \fr 92:1 \fqa Alex. \ft the sabbath-day.\f*the day before the Sabbath, when the land was \add first\add* inhabited, the praise of a Song by David. 
\p The Lord reigns; he has clothed himself with honour: the Lord has clothed and girded himself with strength; for he has established the world, which will not be moved. 
\q1
\v 2 Your throne is prepared of old: you are from everlasting. 
\q1
\v 3 The rivers have lifted up, O Lord, the rivers have lifted up their voices,\f + \fr 92:3 \fqa Alex. \ft + the floods will lift up their waves. See \fqa Heb.\f* 
\q1
\v 4 at \f + \fr 92:4 \fqa q. d. \ft in answer to.\f*the voices of many waters: the billows of the sea are wonderful: the Lord is wonderful in high places. 
\q1
\v 5 Your testimonies are made very sure: holiness becomes your house, O Lord, \f + \fr 92:5 \fqa Gr. \ft to length of days.\f*forever. 
\c 93 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm of David for the fourth \add day\add* of the week. 
\p The Lord is a God of vengeance; the God of vengeance \f + \fr 93:1 \fqa Gr. \ft plural, \fqa bis.\f*has declared himself. 
\q1
\v 2 Be exalted, you who judgest the earth: give a reward to the proud. 
\p
\q1
\v 3 How long will sinners, O Lord, how long will sinners boast? 
\q1
\v 4 They will utter and speak unrighteousness; all the workers of wickedness will speak \add so\add*. 
\q1
\v 5 They have afflicted your people, O Lord, and hurt your heritage. 
\q1
\v 6 They have killed the widow and fatherless, and murdered the stranger. 
\q1
\v 7 They said, The Lord will not see, neither will the God of Jacob understand. 
\p
\q1
\v 8 Understand now, you simple among the people; and you fools, at length be wise. 
\q1
\v 9 He who planted the ear, does he not hear? Or he who formed the eye, does not he perceive? 
\q1
\v 10 He who chastises the nations, will not he punish, \add even\add* he who teaches man knowledge? 
\q1
\v 11 \x + \xo 93:11 \xt 1 Cor. 3. 20.\x* The Lord knows the thoughts of men, that they are vain. 
\p
\q1
\v 12 Blessed is the man whoever you will chasten, O Lord, and will teach him out of your law; 
\q1
\v 13 to give him rest from evil days, until a pit be digged for the sinful one. 
\q1
\v 14 For the Lord will not cast off his people, neither will he forsake his inheritance; 
\q1
\v 15 until righteousness return to judgment, and all the upright in heart will follow it. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 16 Who will rise up for me against the transgressors? Or who will stand up with me against the workers of wickedness? 
\q1
\v 17 If the Lord had not helped me, my soul had almost sojourned in Hades. 
\q1
\v 18 If I said, My foot has been moved; 
\q1
\v 19 your mercy, O Lord, helped me. O Lord, according to the multitude of my griefs within my heart, your consolations have \f + \fr 93:19 \fqa Lit. \ft 'have loved'. \fqa Alex. \ft ἠὺφπαναν, 'have gladdened'.\f*soothed my soul. 
\p
\q1
\v 20 Will the throne of wickedness have fellowship with you, which frames mischief by an ordinance? 
\q1
\v 21 They will hunt for the soul of the righteous, and condemn innocent blood. 
\q1
\v 22 But the Lord was my refuge; and my God the helper of my hope. 
\q1
\v 23 He will recompense to them their wickedness and their wickedness: the Lord our God will completely destroy them. 
\c 94 
\d
\v 1 The praise of a Song by David. 
\p Come, let us exult \f + \fr 94:1 \fqa Gr. \ft unto.\f*in the Lord; let us make a joyful noise to God our Saviour. 
\q1
\v 2 Let us come before his presence with thanksgiving, and make a joyful noise to him with psalms. 
\q1
\v 3 For the Lord is a great God, and a great king over all gods: \f + \fr 94:3 \fqa Heb. \ft and \fqa Alex. \ft omit this clause. See \xt Ps. 93. 14.\f*for the Lord will not cast off his people. 
\q1
\v 4 For the ends of the earth are in his hands; and the heights of the mountains are his. 
\q1
\v 5 For the sea is his, and he made it: and his hands formed the dry land. 
\p
\q1
\v 6 Come, let us worship and fall down before him; and weep before the Lord who made us. 
\q1
\v 7 For he is our God; and we are the people of his pasture, and the sheep of his hand. 
\q1
\v 8 \x + \xo 94:8 \xt Heb. 3. 7-12.\x* Today, if you will hear his voice, harden not your hearts, as in the provocation, according to the day of \f + \fr 94:8 \ft Note, πειρασμοῦ is the reading of several editions.\f*irritation in the wilderness: 
\q1
\v 9 where your fathers tempted me, proved me, and saw my works. 
\q1
\v 10 Forty years was I grieved with this generation, and said, They do always err in their heart, and they have not known my ways. 
\q1
\v 11 So I swore in my wrath, They will not enter into my rest. 
\c 95 
\d
\v 1 When the house was built after the Captivity, a Song by David. 
\p Sing to the Lord a new song; sing to the Lord, all the earth. 
\q1
\v 2 Sing to the Lord, bless his name: proclaim his salvation from day to day. 
\q1
\v 3 Publish his glory among the nations, his wonderful works among all people. 
\p
\q1
\v 4 For the Lord is great, and greatly to be praised: he is terrible above all gods. 
\q1
\v 5 For all the gods of the nations are devils: but the Lord made the heavens. 
\q1
\v 6 Thanksgiving and beauty are before him: holiness and majesty are in his sanctuary. 
\p
\q1
\v 7 Bring to the Lord, you families of the nations, bring to the Lord glory and honour. 
\q1
\v 8 Bring to the Lord the glory \add becoming\add* his name: take offerings, and go into his courts. 
\q1
\v 9 Worship the Lord in his holy court: let all the earth tremble before him. 
\q1
\v 10 Say among the nations, The Lord reigns: for he has established the world so that it will not be moved: he will judge the people in righteousness. 
\q1
\v 11 Let the heavens rejoice, and the earth exult; let the sea be moved, and the fulness of it. 
\q1
\v 12 The plains will rejoice, and all things in them: then will all the trees of the wood exult before the presence of the Lord: 
\q1
\v 13 for he comes, for he comes to judge the earth; he will judge the world in righteousness, and the people with his truth. 
\c 96 
\d
\v 1 For David, when his land is established. 
\p The Lord reigns, let the earth exult, let many islands rejoice. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 Cloud and darkness are all around him; righteousness and judgment are the establishment of his throne. 
\q1
\v 3 Fire will go before him, and burn up his enemies all around. 
\q1
\v 4 His lightnings appeared to the world; the earth saw, and trembled. 
\q1
\v 5 The mountains melted like wax at the presence of the Lord, at the presence of the Lord of the whole earth. 
\q1
\v 6 The heavens have declared his righteousness, and all the people have seen his glory. 
\p
\q1
\v 7 Let all that worship graven images be ashamed, who boast of their idols; \x + \xo 96:7 \xt Heb. 1. 6.\x* worship him, all you his angels. 
\p
\q1
\v 8 Zion heard and rejoiced; and the daughters of Judea exulted, because of your judgments, O Lord. 
\q1
\v 9 For you are Lord most high over all the earth; you are greatly exalted above all gods. 
\p
\q1
\v 10 You who love the Lord, hate evil; the Lord preserves the souls of his saints; he will deliver them from the hand of sinners. 
\q1
\v 11 Light is sprung up for the righteous, and gladness for the upright in heart. 
\q1
\v 12 Rejoice in the Lord, you righteous; and give thanks for a remembrance of his holiness. 
\c 97 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm of David. 
\p Sing to the Lord a new song; for the Lord has worked wonderful works, his right hand, and his holy arm, have worked salvation for him. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 The Lord has made known his salvation, he has revealed his righteousness in the sight of the nations. 
\q1
\v 3 He has remembered his mercy to Jacob, and his truth to the house of Israel; all the ends of the earth have seen the salvation of our God. 
\p
\q1
\v 4 Shout to God, all the earth; sing, and exult, and sing psalms. 
\q1
\v 5 Sing to the Lord with a harp, with a harp, and the voice of a psalm. 
\q1
\v 6 With trumpets of metal, and the sound of a trumpet of horn make a joyful noise to the Lord before the king. 
\q1
\v 7 Let the sea be moved, and the fulness of it; the world, and those who dwell in it. 
\q1
\v 8 The rivers will clap their hands together; the mountains will exult.\f + \fr 97:8 \fqa Alex. \ft + before the Lord, for he comes.\f* 
\q1
\v 9 For he has come to judge the earth; he will judge the world in righteousness, and the nations in uprightness. 
\c 98 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm of David. 
\p The Lord reigns;—let the people rage; \add it is he\add* that sits upon the cherubs, let the earth be moved. 
\q1
\v 2 The Lord is great in Zion, and is high over all the people. 
\q1
\v 3 Let them give thanks to your great name; for it is terrible and holy. 
\q1
\v 4 The king's honour loves judgment; you have prepared \f + \fr 98:4 \fqa Gr. \ft equities.\f*equity, you have worked judgment and justice in Jacob. 
\q1
\v 5 Exalt you the Lord our God, and worship \add at\add* his footstool; for he is holy. 
\p
\q1
\v 6 Moses and Aaron among his priests, and Samuel among those who call upon his name; they called upon the Lord, and he heard them. 
\q1
\v 7 He spoke to them in a pillar of cloud; they kept his testimonies, and the ordinances which he gave them. 
\q1
\v 8 O Lord our God, you heard them; O God, you became propitious to them, though you did take vengeance on all their devices. 
\q1
\v 9 Exalt you the Lord our God, and worship at his holy mountain; for the Lord our God is holy. 
\c 99 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm for Thanksgiving. 
\p Make a joyful noise to the Lord, all the earth. 
\q1
\v 2 Serve the Lord with gladness; come before his presence with exultation. 
\q1
\v 3 Know that the Lord he is God; he made us, and not we ourselves; \add we are\add* his people, and the sheep of his pasture. 
\q1
\v 4 Enter into his gates with thanksgiving, and his courts with hymns; give thanks to him, praise his name. 
\q1
\v 5 For the Lord is good, his mercy is forever; and his truth \add endures\add* to generation and generation. 
\c 100 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm of David. 
\p I will sing to you, O Lord, of mercy and judgment; I will sing a psalm, 
\q1
\v 2 and I will be wise in a blameless way. When will you come to me? I walked in the innocence of my heart, among my house. 
\q1
\v 3 I have not set before my eyes any unlawful thing; I have hated transgressors. 
\q1
\v 4 A perverse heart has not cleaved to me; I have not known an evil man, because he turns away from me. 
\q1
\v 5 Him that privily speaks against his neighbour, him have I driven from \add me\add*: he who is proud in look and insatiable in heart,—with him I have not eaten. 
\q1
\v 6 My eyes \add will be\add* upon the faithful of the land, so they may dwell with me: he who walked in a perfect way, the same ministered to me. 
\q1
\v 7 The proud doer didn't dwell among my house; the unjust speaker prospered not in my sight. 
\q1
\v 8 Early did I kill all the sinners of the land, that I might destroy out of the city of the Lord all that work wickedness. 
\c 101 
\d
\v 1 A Prayer for the Poor; when he is deeply afflicted, and pours out his supplication before the Lord. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 Hear my prayer, O Lord, and let my cry come to you. 
\q1
\v 3 Don't turn away your face from me: in the day \add when\add* I am afflicted, incline your ear to me: in the day \add when\add* I will call upon you, speedily hear me. 
\p
\q1
\v 4 For my days have vanished like smoke, and my bones have been parched like a stick. 
\q1
\v 5 I am blighted like grass, and my heart is dried up; for I have forgotten to eat my bread. 
\q1
\v 6 Because of the voice of my groaning, my bone has cleaved to my flesh. 
\q1
\v 7 I have become like a pelican of the wilderness; 
\q1
\v 8 I have become like an owl in a ruined house. I have watched, and am become as a sparrow dwelling alone on a roof. 
\q1
\v 9 All the day long my enemies have reproached me; and those who praised me have sworn against me. 
\q1
\v 10 For I have eaten ashes as it were bread, and mingled my drink with weeping; 
\q1
\v 11 because of your anger and your wrath: for you have lifted me up, and dashed me down. 
\p
\q1
\v 12 My days have declined like a shadow; and I am withered like grass. 
\q1
\v 13 But you, Lord, endurest forever, and your memorial to generation and generation. 
\q1
\v 14 You will arise, and have mercy upon Zion: for \add it is\add* time to have mercy upon her, for the set time has come. 
\q1
\v 15 For your servants have taken pleasure in her stones, and they will pity her dust. 
\q1
\v 16 So the nations will fear your name, O Lord, and all kings your glory. 
\p
\q1
\v 17 For the Lord will build up Zion, \f + \fr 101:17 \fqa Or, \ft then shall be.\f*and will appear in his glory. 
\q1
\v 18 He has had regard to the prayer of the lowly, and has not despised their petition. 
\q1
\v 19 Let this be written for another generation; and the people that will be created will praise the Lord. 
\q1
\v 20 For he has looked out from the height of his sanctuary; the Lord looked upon the earth from heaven; 
\q1
\v 21 to hear the groaning of the fettered ones, to loosen the sons of the killed; 
\q1
\v 22 to proclaim the name of the Lord in Zion, and his praise in Jerusalem; 
\q1
\v 23 when the people are gathered together, and the kings, to serve the Lord. 
\p
\q1
\v 24 He answered him in the way of his strength: tell me the fewness of my days. 
\q1
\v 25 Don't take me away among my days: your years \add are\add* \x + \xo 101:25 \xt Heb. 1. 11,13.\x* through all generations. 
\q1
\v 26 In the \f + \fr 101:26 \fqa Gr. \ft plural.\f*beginning you, O Lord, did lay the foundation of the earth; and the heavens are the works of your hands. 
\q1
\v 27 They will perish, but you remainest: and \add they all\add* will wax old as a garment; and as a vesture will you fold them, and they will be changed. 
\q1
\v 28 But you are the same, and your years will not fail. 
\q1
\v 29 The children of your servants will dwell \add securely\add*, and their seed will \f + \fr 101:29 \fqa Or, \ft be directed aright.\f*prosper forever. 
\c 102 
\d
\v 1 \add A Psalm\add* of David. 
\p Bless the Lord, O my soul; and all \add that is\add* within me, \add bless\add* his holy name. 
\q1
\v 2 Bless the Lord, O my soul, and forget not all his praises: 
\q1
\v 3 who forgives all your transgressions, who heals all your diseases; 
\q1
\v 4 who redeems your life from corruption; who crowns you with mercy and compassion; 
\q1
\v 5 who satisfies your desire with good things: \add so that\add* your youth will be renewed like \add that\add* of the eagle. 
\p
\q1
\v 6 The Lord executes mercy and judgment for all that are injured. 
\q1
\v 7 He made known his ways to Moses, his will to the children of Israel. 
\q1
\v 8 The Lord is compassionate and pitiful, long-suffering, and full of mercy. 
\q1
\v 9 He will not be always angry; neither will he be wrathful forever. 
\q1
\v 10 He has not dealt with us according to our sins, nor recompensed us according to our iniquities. 
\q1
\v 11 For as the heaven is high above the earth, the Lord has \add so\add* increased his mercy toward those who fear him. 
\q1
\v 12 As far as the east is from the west, \add so far\add* has he removed our transgressions from us. 
\q1
\v 13 As a father pities \add his\add* children, the Lord pities those who fear him. 
\q1
\v 14 For he knows our frame: remember that we are dust. 
\p
\q1
\v 15 \add As for\add* man, his days are as grass; as a flower of the field, so he will flourish. 
\q1
\v 16 For the wind passes over it, and it will not be; and it will know its place no more. 
\q1
\v 17 But the mercy of the Lord is from generation to generation upon those who fear him, and his righteousness to children's children; 
\q1
\v 18 to those who keep his covenant, and remember his commandments to do them. 
\p
\q1
\v 19 The Lord has prepared his throne in the heaven; and his kingdom rules over all. 
\q1
\v 20 Bless the Lord, all you his angels, mighty in strength, who perform his bidding, \add ready\add* to listen to the voice of his words. 
\q1
\v 21 Bless the Lord, all you his hosts; \add you\add* ministers of his that do his will. 
\q1
\v 22 Bless the Lord, all his works, in every place of his dominion: bless the Lord, O my soul. 
\c 103 
\d
\v 1 \add A Psalm\add* of David. 
\p Bless the Lord, O my soul. O Lord my God, you are very great; you have clothed yourself with praise and honour: 
\q1
\v 2 who do robe yourself with light as with a garment; spreading out the heaven as a curtain. 
\q1
\v 3 Who covers his chambers with waters; who makes the clouds his chariot; who walks on the wings of the wind. 
\q1
\v 4 \x + \xo 103:4 \xt Heb. 1. 7.\x* Who makes his angels spirits, and his ministers a flaming fire. 
\p
\q1
\v 5 Who establishes the earth on her sure foundation: it will not be moved forever. 
\q1
\v 6 The deep, as it were a garment, is his covering: the waters will stand \f + \fr 103:6 \fqa Or, \ft above.\f*on the hills. 
\q1
\v 7 At your rebuke they will flee; at the voice of your thunder they will be alarmed. 
\q1
\v 8 They go up to the mountains, and down to the plains, to the place which you have founded for them. 
\q1
\v 9 You have set a bound which they will not pass, neither will they turn again to cover the earth. 
\p
\q1
\v 10 He sends forth his fountains among the valleys: the waters will run between the mountains. 
\q1
\v 11 They will give drink to all the wild beasts of the field: the wild donkeys will take \add of them\add* to \add quench\add* their thirst. 
\q1
\v 12 By them will the birds of the sky lodge: they will utter a voice out of the midst of the rocks. 
\q1
\v 13 He waters the mountains from his chambers: the earth will be satisfied with the fruit of your works. 
\p
\q1
\v 14 He makes grass to grow for the cattle, and green herb for the service of men, to bring bread out of the earth; 
\q1
\v 15 and wine makes glad the heart of man, to make his face cheerful with oil: and bread strengthens man's heart. 
\q1
\v 16 The trees of the plain will be full \add of sap; even\add* the cedars of Lebanon which he has planted. 
\q1
\v 17 There the sparrows will build their nests; and the house of the heron takes the lead among them. 
\q1
\v 18 The high mountains are a refuge for the stags, \add and\add* the rock for the rabbits. 
\p
\q1
\v 19 He appointed the moon for seasons: the sun knows his going down. 
\q1
\v 20 You did make darkness, and it was night; in it all the wild beasts of the forest will be abroad: 
\q1
\v 21 \add even\add* young lions roaring for prey, and to seek food for themselves from God. 
\q1
\v 22 The sun arises, and they will be gathered together, and will lie down in their dens. 
\q1
\v 23 Man will go forth to his work, and to his labour till evening. 
\p
\q1
\v 24 How great are your works, O Lord! In wisdom have you worked them all: the earth is filled with your creation. 
\q1
\v 25 \add So is\add* this great and wide sea: there are things creeping innumerable, small animals and great. 
\q1
\v 26 There go the ships; \add and\add* this dragon whom you have made to play in it. 
\q1
\v 27 All wait upon you, to give them \add their\add* food in due season. 
\q1
\v 28 When you have given \add it\add* them, they will gather \add it\add*; and when you have opened your hand, they will all be filled with good. 
\q1
\v 29 But when you have turned away your face, they will be troubled: you will take away their breath, and they will fail, and return to their dust. 
\q1
\v 30 You will send forth your Spirit, and they will be created; and you will renew the face of the earth. 
\p
\q1
\v 31 Let the glory of the Lord be forever: the Lord will rejoice in his works; 
\q1
\v 32 who looks upon the earth, and makes it tremble; who touches the mountains, and they smoke. 
\q1
\v 33 I will sing to the Lord while I live; I will sing praise to my God while I exist. 
\q1
\v 34 Let my meditation be sweet to him: and I will rejoice in the Lord. 
\q1
\v 35 Let the sinners fail from off the earth, and transgressors, so that they will be no more. Bless the Lord, O my soul. 
\c 104 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\p Give thanks to the Lord, and call upon his name; declare his works among the nations. 
\q1
\v 2 Sing to him, yes, sing praises to him: tell forth all his wonderful works. 
\q1
\v 3 Glory in his holy name: let the heart of those who seek the Lord rejoice. 
\q1
\v 4 Seek the Lord, and be strengthened; seek his face continually. 
\q1
\v 5 Remember his wonderful works that he has done; his wonders, and the judgments of his mouth; 
\q1
\v 6 \add you\add* seed of Abraham, his servants, \add you\add* children of Jacob, his chosen ones. 
\p
\q1
\v 7 He is the Lord our God; his judgments are in all the earth. 
\q1
\v 8 He has remembered his covenant forever, the word which he commanded for a thousand generations: 
\q1
\v 9 which he established as a covenant to Abraham, and \add he remembered\add* his oath to Isaac. 
\q1
\v 10 He established it to Jacob for an ordinance, and to Israel for an everlasting covenant; 
\q1
\v 11 saying, To you I will give the land of Canaan, the line of your inheritance: 
\q1
\v 12 when they were few in number, very few, and sojourners in it. 
\q1
\v 13 They went from nation to nation, and from \add one\add* kingdom to another people. 
\q1
\v 14 He suffered no man to wrong them; and he rebuked kings for their sakes: 
\q1
\v 15 \add saying\add*, Don't touch my anointed ones; and do my prophets no harm. 
\q1
\v 16 Moreover he called for a famine upon the land; he broke the whole support of bread. 
\p
\q1
\v 17 He sent a man before them; Joseph was sold for a slave. 
\q1
\v 18 They \f + \fr 104:18 \fqa Gr. \ft humbled.\f*hurt his feet with fetters; \f + \fr 104:18 \fqa Or, \ft his body, see \fqa Heb.\f*his soul passed into iron, 
\q1
\v 19 until the time that his cause came on; the word of the Lord tried him as fire. 
\q1
\v 20 The king sent and loosed him; \add even\add* the prince of the people, and let him go free. 
\q1
\v 21 He made him lord over his house, and ruler of all his substance; 
\q1
\v 22 to chastise his rulers at his pleasure, and to teach his elders wisdom. 
\p
\q1
\v 23 Israel also came into Egypt, and Jacob sojourned in the land of Cham. 
\q1
\v 24 He increased his people greatly, and made them stronger than their enemies. 
\q1
\v 25 He turned their heart to hate his people, to deal craftily with his servants. 
\q1
\v 26 He sent Moses his servant, \add and\add* Aaron whom he had chosen. 
\p
\q1
\v 27 He established among them his signs, and \add his\add* wonders in the land of Cham. 
\q1
\v 28 He sent darkness, and made it dark; yet they \f + \fr 104:28 \fqa Gr. \ft embittered.\f*rebelled against his words. 
\q1
\v 29 He turned their waters into blood, and killed their fish. 
\q1
\v 30 Their land produced frogs abundantly, in the chambers of their kings. 
\q1
\v 31 He spoke, and the dog-fly came, and lice in all their coasts. 
\q1
\v 32 He turned their rain into hail, \add and sent\add* flaming fire in their land. 
\q1
\v 33 He struck their vines and their fig-trees; and broke every tree of their coast. 
\q1
\v 34 He spoke, and the locust came, and caterpillars innumerable, 
\q1
\v 35 and devoured all the grass in their land, and devoured the fruit of their ground. 
\q1
\v 36 He struck also every first-born of their land, the first-fruits of all their labour. 
\q1
\v 37 He brought them out with silver and gold; and there was not a feeble one among their tribes. 
\q1
\v 38 Egypt rejoiced at their departing; for the fear of them fell upon them. 
\q1
\v 39 He spread out a cloud for a covering to them, and fire to give them light by night. 
\q1
\v 40 They asked, and the quail came, and he satisfied them with the bread of heaven. 
\q1
\v 41 He clave the rock, and the waters flowed; rivers ran in dry places. 
\p
\q1
\v 42 For he remembered his holy word, which \add he promised\add* to Abraham his servant. 
\q1
\v 43 He brought out his people with exultation, and his chosen with joy; 
\q1
\v 44 and gave them the lands of the nations; and they inherited the labours of the people; 
\q1
\v 45 that they might keep his ordinances, and diligently seek his law. 
\c 105 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\p Give thanks to the Lord; for he is good: for his mercy \add endures\add* forever. 
\q1
\v 2 Who will tell the mighty acts of the Lord? \add who\add* will cause all his praises to be heard? 
\q1
\v 3 Blessed are those who keep judgment, and do righteousness at all times. 
\p
\q1
\v 4 Remember us, O Lord, with the favour \add you have\add* to your people: visit us with your salvation; 
\q1
\v 5 that we may behold the good of your elect, that we may rejoice in the gladness of your nation, that we may glory with your inheritance. 
\p
\q1
\v 6 We have sinned with our fathers, we have transgressed, we have done unrighteously. 
\q1
\v 7 Our fathers in Egypt didn't understand your wonders, and didn't remember the multitude of your mercy; but provoked \add him\add* as they went up by the Red Sea. 
\q1
\v 8 Yet he saved them for his name's sake, that he might cause his mighty power to be known. 
\q1
\v 9 He rebuked the Red Sea, and it was dried up: so he led them through the deep as through the wilderness. 
\q1
\v 10 He saved them out of the hand of those who hated \add them\add*, and redeemed them out of the hand of the enemy. 
\q1
\v 11 The water covered those that oppressed them: there was not one of them left. 
\q1
\v 12 Then they believed his words, and celebrated his praise. 
\q1
\v 13 They made haste, they forgot his works; they waited not for his counsel. 
\q1
\v 14 They lusted exceedingly in the wilderness, and tempted God in the dry \add land\add*. 
\q1
\v 15 He gave them their request, and sent fulness into their souls. 
\p
\q1
\v 16 They provoked Moses also in the camp, and Aaron the holy one of the Lord. 
\q1
\v 17 The earth opened and swallowed up Dathan, and closed upon the congregation of Abiron. 
\q1
\v 18 A fire was kindled in their congregation, and a flame burnt up the sinners. 
\p
\q1
\v 19 They made a calf in Horeb, and worshipped the graven image, 
\q1
\v 20 and they changed their glory into the similitude of a calf that feeds on grass. 
\q1
\v 21 They forgot God who saved them, who had worked great deeds in Egypt; 
\q1
\v 22 wondrous \add works\add* in the land of Cham, and terrible things at the Red Sea. 
\q1
\v 23 So he said that he would have destroyed them, had not Moses his chosen stood before him in the breach, to turn \add him\add* away from the fierceness of his anger, so that he should not destroy them. 
\p
\q1
\v 24 Moreover they despise the desirable land, and didn't believe his word. 
\q1
\v 25 They murmured in their tents: they didn't listen to the voice of the Lord. 
\q1
\v 26 So he lifted up his hand against them, to cast them down in the wilderness; 
\q1
\v 27 and to cast down their seed among the nations, and to scatter them in the lands. 
\p
\q1
\v 28 They were joined also to Beelphegor, and ate the sacrifices of the dead. And they provoked him with their devices; 
\q1
\v 29 and destruction was multiplied among them. 
\q1
\v 30 Then Phinees stood up, and made atonement: and the plague ceased. 
\q1
\v 31 It was counted to him for righteousness, to all generations forever. 
\p
\q1
\v 32 They provoked him also at the water of Strife, and Moses was hurt for their sakes; 
\q1
\v 33 for they provoked his spirit, and he \f + \fr 105:33 \fqa Or, \ft gave commandment.\f*spoke \add unadvisedly\add* with his lips. 
\p
\q1
\v 34 They destroyed not the nations which the Lord told them \add to destroy\add*; 
\q1
\v 35 but were mingled with the nations, and learned their works. 
\q1
\v 36 They served their graven images; and it became an offence to them. 
\q1
\v 37 They sacrificed their sons and their daughters to devils, 
\q1
\v 38 and shed innocent blood, the blood of their sons and daughters, whom they sacrificed to the idols of Canaan; and the land was \f + \fr 105:38 \fqa Or, \ft murderously defiled.\f*defiled with blood, 
\q1
\v 39 and was polluted with their works; and they went a whoring with their own devices. 
\p
\q1
\v 40 So the Lord was very angry with his people, and he abhorred his inheritance. 
\q1
\v 41 He delivered them into the hands of \add their\add* enemies; and those who hated them ruled over them. 
\q1
\v 42 Their enemies oppressed them, and they were brought down under their hands. 
\q1
\v 43 Many a time he delivered them; but they provoked him by their counsel, and they were brought low by their iniquities. 
\q1
\v 44 Yet the Lord looked upon their affliction, when he heard their petition. 
\q1
\v 45 He remembered his covenant, and repented according to the multitude of his mercy. 
\q1
\v 46 He caused them to be pitied in the sight of all who carried them captive. 
\p
\q1
\v 47 Save us, O Lord our God, and gather us from among the nations, that we may give thanks to your holy name, that we may glory in your praise. 
\q1
\v 48 Blessed be the Lord God of Israel from everlasting and to everlasting; and all the people will say, Amen, Amen. 
\c 106 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\p Give thanks to the Lord, for he is good; for his mercy \add endures\add* forever. 
\q1
\v 2 Let them say \add so\add* who have been redeemed by the Lord, whom he has redeemed from the hand of the enemy; 
\q1
\v 3 and gathered them out of the lands, from the east, and west, and north, and \f + \fr 106:3 \fqa Gr. \ft sea.\f*south. 
\p
\q1
\v 4 They wandered in the wilderness in a dry land; they found no way to a city of habitation. 
\q1
\v 5 Hungry and thirsty, their soul fainted in them. 
\q1
\v 6 Then they cried to the Lord in their affliction, and he delivered them out of their distresses. 
\q1
\v 7 He guided them into a straight path, that they might go to a city of habitation. 
\p
\q1
\v 8 Let them acknowledge to the Lord his mercies, and his wonderful works to the children of men. 
\q1
\v 9 For he satisfies the empty soul, and fills the hungry \add soul\add* with good things, 
\q1
\v 10 \add even\add* those who sit in darkness and the shadow of death, fettered in poverty and iron; 
\q1
\v 11 because they \f + \fr 106:11 \fqa Gr. \ft embittered the oracles.\f*rebelled against the words of God, and provoked the counsel of the Most High. 
\q1
\v 12 So their heart was brought low with troubles; they were weak, and there was no helper. 
\q1
\v 13 Then they cried to the Lord in their affliction, and he saved them out of their distresses. 
\q1
\v 14 He brought them out of darkness and the shadow of death, and broke their bonds asunder. 
\p
\q1
\v 15 Let them acknowledge to the Lord his mercies, and his wonders to the children of men. 
\q1
\v 16 For he broke to pieces the bronze gates, and crushed the iron bars. 
\p
\q1
\v 17 \f + \fr 106:17 \ft see the Hebrew.\f*He helped them out of the way of their wickedness; for they were brought low because of their iniquities. 
\q1
\v 18 Their soul abhorred all food; and they drew near to the gates of death. 
\q1
\v 19 Then they cried to the Lord in their affliction, and he saved them out of their distresses. 
\q1
\v 20 He sent his word, and healed them, and delivered them out of their destructions. 
\p
\q1
\v 21 Let them acknowledge to the Lord his mercies, and his wonderful works to the children of men. 
\q1
\v 22 Let them offer to him the sacrifice of praise, and proclaim his works with exultation. 
\p
\q1
\v 23 Those who go down to the sea in ships, doing business in many waters; 
\q1
\v 24 these \add men\add* have seen the works of the Lord, and his wonders in the deep. 
\q1
\v 25 He speaks, and the stormy wind arises, and its waves are lifted up. 
\q1
\v 26 They go up to the heavens, and go down to the depths; their soul melts because of troubles. 
\q1
\v 27 They are troubled, they stagger as a drunkard, and all their wisdom is swallowed up. 
\q1
\v 28 Then they cry to the Lord in their affliction, and he brings them out of their distresses. 
\q1
\v 29 He commands the storm, and it is calmed into a gentle breeze, and its waves are still. 
\q1
\v 30 They are glad, because they are quiet; and he guides them to their desired haven. 
\p
\q1
\v 31 Let them acknowledge to the Lord his mercies, and his wonderful works to the children of men. 
\q1
\v 32 Let them exalt him in the congregation of the people, and praise him in the seat of the elders. 
\p
\q1
\v 33 He turns rivers into a desert, and streams of \f + \fr 106:33 \fqa Gr. \ft waters.\f*water into \f + \fr 106:33 \fqa Gr. \ft thirst.\f*a dry land; 
\q1
\v 34 a fruitful land into saltness, for the wickedness of those who dwell in it. 
\q1
\v 35 He turns a wilderness into pools of water, and a dry land into streams of water. 
\q1
\v 36 There he causes the hungry to dwell, and they establish for themselves cities of habitation. 
\q1
\v 37 They sow fields, and plant vineyards, and they yield fruit of increase. 
\q1
\v 38 He blesses them, and they multiply exceedingly, and he diminishes not the number of their cattle. 
\q1
\v 39 Again they become few, and are brought low, by the pressure of evils and pain. 
\q1
\v 40 Contempt is poured upon their princes, and he causes them to wander in a desert and trackless land. 
\q1
\v 41 But he helps the poor out of poverty, and makes \add him\add* families as a flock. 
\q1
\v 42 The upright will see and rejoice; and all wickedness will stop her mouth. 
\q1
\v 43 Who is wise, and will observe these things, and understand the mercies of the Lord? 
\c 107 
\d
\v 1 Song of a Psalm by David. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 O God, my heart is ready, my heart is ready; I will sing and sing psalms with my glory. 
\q1
\v 3 Awake, psaltery and harp; I will awake early. 
\q1
\v 4 I will give thanks to you, O Lord, among the people; I will sing praise to you among the nations. 
\q1
\v 5 For your mercy is great above the heavens, and your truth \add reaches\add* to the clouds. 
\q1
\v 6 Be exalted, O God, above the heavens; and your glory above all the earth. 
\q1
\v 7 That your beloved \add ones\add* may be delivered, save with your right hand, and hear me. God has spoken in his sanctuary; 
\q1
\v 8 I will be exalted, and will divide Sicima, and will measure out the valley of tents. 
\q1
\v 9 Gilead is mine; and Manasseh is mine; and Ephraim is the help of my head; Judah is my king; 
\q1
\v 10 Moab is the caldron of my hope; over Idumea will I cast my sandal; the Philistines are made subject to me. 
\p
\q1
\v 11 Who will bring me into the fortified city? Or who will guide me to Idumea? 
\q1
\v 12 Will not you, O God, who have rejected us? And will not you, O God, go forth with our hosts? 
\q1
\v 13 Give us help from tribulation: for vain is the help of man. 
\q1
\v 14 Through God we will \f + \fr 107:14 \fqa Gr. \ft work power.\f*do valiantly; and he will bring to nought our enemies. 
\c 108 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm of David. 
\p O God, pass not over my praise in silence; 
\q1
\v 2 for the mouth of the sinner and the mouth of the crafty \add man\add* have been opened against me: they have spoken against me with a crafty tongue. 
\q1
\v 3 They have compassed me with words of hatred; and fought against me without a cause. 
\q1
\v 4 \f + \fr 108:4 \fqa Or, \ft in return for my love.\f*Instead of loving me, they falsely accused me: but I continued to pray. 
\q1
\v 5 They rewarded me evil for good, and hatred for my love. 
\p
\q1
\v 6 Set you a sinner against him; and let \f + \fr 108:6 \fqa Or, \ft the accuser.\f*the devil stand at his right hand. 
\q1
\v 7 When he is judged, let him go forth condemned: and let his prayer become sin. 
\q1
\v 8 Let his days be few: and \x + \xo 108:8 \xt Acts 1. 20.\x* let another take his office of overseer. 
\q1
\v 9 Let his children be orphans, and his wife a widow. 
\q1
\v 10 Let his children wander without a dwelling-place, and beg: let them be cast out of their habitations. 
\q1
\v 11 Let \add his\add* creditor exact all that belongs to him: and let strangers spoil his labours. 
\q1
\v 12 Let him have no helper; neither let there be any one to have compassion on his fatherless children. 
\q1
\v 13 Let his children be \add given up\add* to utter destruction: in one generation let his name be blotted out. 
\q1
\v 14 Let the wickedness of his fathers be remembered before the Lord; and don't let the sin of his mother be blotted out. 
\q1
\v 15 Let them be before the Lord continually; and let their memorial be blotted out from the earth. 
\p
\q1
\v 16 Because he didn't remember to show mercy, but persecuted the needy and poor man, and \add that\add* to kill him that was pricked in the heart. 
\q1
\v 17 He loved cursing also, and it will come upon him; and he didn't take pleasure in blessing, so it will be removed far from him. 
\q1
\v 18 Yes, he put on cursing as a garment, and it has come as water into his bowels, and as oil into his bones. 
\q1
\v 19 Let it be to him as a garment which he puts on, and as a girdle with which he girds himself continually. 
\q1
\v 20 This is the dealing of the Lord with those who falsely accuse me, and of those who speak evil against my soul. 
\p
\q1
\v 21 But you, O Lord, Lord, deal \add mercifully\add* with me, for your name's sake: for your mercy is good. 
\q1
\v 22 Deliver me, for I am poor and needy; and my heart is troubled within me. 
\q1
\v 23 I am removed as a shadow in its going down: I am tossed up and down like locusts. 
\q1
\v 24 My knees are weakened through fasting, and my flesh is changed because of \add the want of\add* oil. 
\q1
\v 25 I became also a reproach to them: \add when\add* they saw me they shook their heads. 
\p
\q1
\v 26 Help me, O Lord my God; and save me according to your mercy. 
\q1
\v 27 Let them know that this is your hand; and \add that\add* you, Lord, have worked it. 
\q1
\v 28 Let them curse, but you will bless: let those who rise up against me be ashamed, but let your servant rejoice. 
\q1
\v 29 Let those that falsely accuse me be clothed with shame, and let them cover themselves with their shame as with a mantle. 
\q1
\v 30 I will give thanks to the Lord abundantly with my mouth; and among many I will praise him. 
\q1
\v 31 For he stood on the right hand of the poor, to save \add me\add* from those who persecute my soul. 
\c 109 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm of David. 
\p \x + \xo 109:1 \xt Mat. 22. 44.\x* The Lord said to my Lord, Sit you on my right hand, until I make your enemies your footstool. 
\q1
\v 2 The Lord will send out a rod of power for you out of Zion: rule you among your enemies. 
\q1
\v 3 With you is dominion in the day of your power, in the splendours of \f + \fr 109:3 \fqa Or, \ft holiness, \fqa i. e. \ft holy things.\f*your saints: I have begotten you from the womb before the morning. 
\q1
\v 4 The Lord swore, and will not repent, You are a priest forever, after the order of Melchisedec. 
\q1
\v 5 The Lord at your right hand has dashed in pieces kings in the day of his wrath. 
\q1
\v 6 He will judge among the nations, he will fill up \add the number of\add* corpses, he will crush the heads of many on the earth. 
\q1
\v 7 He will drink of the brook in the way; therefore he will lift up the head. 
\c 110 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\p I will give you thanks, O Lord, with my whole heart, in the council of the upright, and \add in\add* the congregation. 
\q1
\v 2 The works of the Lord are great, sought out \f + \fr 110:2 \ft Comp. \fqa Gr. \ft with \fqa Heb.\f*according to all his will. 
\q1
\v 3 His work is \add worthy of\add* thanksgiving and honour: and his righteousness endures forever and ever. 
\q1
\v 4 He has caused his wonderful works to be remembered: the Lord is merciful and compassionate. 
\q1
\v 5 He has given food to those who fear him: he will remember his covenant forever. 
\q1
\v 6 He has declared to his people the power of his works, to give them the inheritance of the nations. 
\q1
\v 7 The works of his hands are truth and judgment: all his commandments are sure: 
\q1
\v 8 established forever and ever, done in truth and uprightness. 
\q1
\v 9 He sent redemption to his people: he commanded his covenant forever: holy and fearful is his name. 
\q1
\v 10 The fear of the Lord is the \f + \fr 110:10 \fqa Or, \ft sum.\f*beginning of wisdom, and all that act accordingly have a good understanding; his praise endures forever and ever. 
\c 111 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\p Blessed is the man who fears the Lord: he will delight greatly in his commandments. 
\q1
\v 2 His seed will be mighty in the earth: the generation of the upright will be blessed. 
\q1
\v 3 Glory and riches will be in his house; and his righteousness endures for evermore. 
\q1
\v 4 To the upright light has sprung up in darkness: he is pitiful, and merciful, and righteous. 
\q1
\v 5 The good man is he who pities and lends: he will direct his affairs with judgment. 
\q1
\v 6 For he will not be moved forever; the righteous will be in everlasting remembrance. 
\q1
\v 7 He will not be afraid of \add any\add* evil report: his heart is ready to trust in the Lord. 
\q1
\v 8 His heart is established, he will not fear, till he will see \add his desire\add* upon his enemies. 
\q1
\v 9 \x + \xo 111:9 \xt 2 Cor. 9. 9.\x* He has dispersed abroad; he has given to the poor; his righteousness endures for evermore: his horn will be exalted with honour. 
\q1
\v 10 The sinner will see and be angry, he will gnash his teeth, and consume away: the desire of the sinner will perish. 
\c 112 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\p Praise the Lord, you servants \add of his\add*, praise the name of the Lord. 
\q1
\v 2 Let the name of the Lord be blessed, from this present time and forever. 
\q1
\v 3 From the rising of the sun to his setting, the name of the Lord is to be praised. 
\q1
\v 4 The Lord is high above all the nations; his glory is above the heavens. 
\q1
\v 5 Who is as the Lord our God? Who dwells in the high places, 
\q1
\v 6 and \add yet\add* looks upon the low things in heaven, and on the earth: 
\q1
\v 7 who lifts up the poor from the earth, and raises up the needy from the dunghill; 
\q1
\v 8 to set him with princes, \add even\add* with the princes of his people: 
\q1
\v 9 who settles the barren \add woman\add* in a house, \add as\add* a mother rejoicing over children. 
\c 113 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\p At the going forth of Israel from Egypt, of the house of Jacob from a barbarous people, 
\q1
\v 2 Judea became his \f + \fr 113:2 \fqa Or, \ft consecrated thing.\f*sanctuary, \add and\add* Israel his dominion. 
\q1
\v 3 The sea saw and fled: Jordan was turned back. 
\q1
\v 4 The mountains skipped like rams, and the hills like lambs. 
\p
\q1
\v 5 What \add ailed\add* you, O sea, that you fleddest? And you Jordan, that you were turned back? 
\q1
\v 6 \add You\add* mountains, that you skipped like rams, and \add you\add* hills, like lambs? 
\q1
\v 7 The earth trembled at the presence of the Lord, at the presence of the God of Jacob; 
\q1
\v 8 who turned the rock into pools of water, and the \f + \fr 113:8 \fqa Gr. \ft sharp rock.\f*flint into fountains of water. 
\p
\q1
\v 9 Not to us, O Lord, not to us, but to your name give glory, because of your mercy and your truth; 
\q1
\v 10 lest at any time the nations should say, Where is their God? 
\q1
\v 11 But our God has done in heaven and on earth, whatever he has pleased. 
\p
\q1
\v 12 The idols of the nations are silver and gold, the works of men's hands. 
\q1
\v 13 They have a mouth, but they \f + \fr 113:13 \fqa Gr. \ft will not.\f*cannot speak; they have eyes, but they cannot see: 
\q1
\v 14 they have ears, but they cannot hear; they have noses, but they cannot smell; 
\q1
\v 15 they have hands, but they cannot handle; they have feet, but they cannot walk: they cannot speak through their throat. 
\q1
\v 16 Let those that make them become like to them, and all who trust in them. 
\p
\q1
\v 17 The house of Israel trusts in the Lord: he is their helper and defender. 
\q1
\v 18 The house of Aaron trusts in the Lord: he is their helper and defender. 
\q1
\v 19 Those who fear the Lord trust in the Lord: he is their helper and defender. 
\p
\q1
\v 20 The Lord has remembered us, and blessed us: he has blessed the house of Israel, he has blessed the house of Aaron. 
\q1
\v 21 He has blessed those who fear the Lord, both small and great. 
\q1
\v 22 The Lord \f + \fr 113:22 \fqa Or, \ft increase you.\f*add \add blessings\add* to you and to your children. 
\q1
\v 23 Blessed are you of the Lord, who made the heaven and the earth. 
\p
\q1
\v 24 The heaven of \f + \fr 113:24 \fqa Gr. \ft sing.\f*heavens \add belongs\add* to the Lord: but he has given the earth to the sons of men. 
\q1
\v 25 The dead will not praise you, O Lord, nor any that go down to Hades. 
\q1
\v 26 But we, the living, will bless the Lord, from now on and forever. 
\c 114 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\p I am well pleased, because the Lord will listen to the voice of my supplication. 
\q1
\v 2 Because he has inclined his ear to me, therefore will I call upon him while I live. 
\q1
\v 3 The pangs of death compassed me; the dangers of hell found me: I found affliction and sorrow. 
\q1
\v 4 Then I called on the name of the Lord: O Lord, deliver my soul. 
\p
\q1
\v 5 The Lord is merciful and righteous; yes, our God has pity. 
\q1
\v 6 The Lord preserves \f + \fr 114:6 \fqa Gr. \ft infants.\f*the simple: I was brought low, and he delivered me. 
\p
\q1
\v 7 Return to your rest, O my soul; for the Lord has dealt bountifully with you. 
\q1
\v 8 For he has delivered my soul from death, my eyes from tears, and my feet from falling. 
\q1
\v 9 I will be well-pleasing before the Lord in the land of the living. 
\c 115 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\p \x + \xo 115:1 \xt 2 Cor. 4. 13.\x* I believed, wherefore I have spoken: but I was greatly afflicted. 
\q1
\v 2 I said in my amazement, Every man is a liar. 
\p
\q1
\v 3 What will I give to the Lord for all the things wherein he has rewarded me? 
\q1
\v 4 I will take the cup of salvation, and call upon the name of the Lord. 
\q1
\v 4a I will pay my vows to the Lord, in the presence of all his people. 
\p
\q1
\v 6 Precious in the sight of the Lord is the death of his saints. 
\q1
\v 7 O Lord, I am your servant; I am your servant, and the son of your handmaid: you have burst my bonds asunder. 
\q1
\v 8 I will offer to you the sacrifice of praise, and will call upon the name of the Lord. 
\q1
\v 9 I will pay my vows to the Lord, in the presence of all his people, 
\q1
\v 10 in the courts of the Lord's house, among you, Jerusalem. 
\c 116 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\p \x + \xo 116:1 \xt Rom. 15. 11.\x* Praise the Lord, all you nations: praise him, all you peoples. 
\q1
\v 2 For his mercy has been abundant toward us: and the truth of the Lord endures forever. 
\c 117 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\p Give thanks to the Lord; for \add he is\add* good: for his mercy \add endures\add* forever. 
\q1
\v 2 Let now the house of Israel say, that \add he is\add* good: for his mercy \add endures\add* forever. 
\q1
\v 3 Let now the house of Aaron say, that \add he is\add* good: for his mercy \add endures\add* forever. 
\q1
\v 4 Let now all that fear the Lord say, that \add he is\add* good: for his mercy \add endures\add* forever. 
\p
\q1
\v 5 I called on the Lord out of affliction: and he listened to me, \add so as to bring me\add* into a wide place. 
\q1
\v 6 \x + \xo 117:6 \xt Heb. 13. 6.\x* The Lord is my helper; and I will not fear what man will do to me. 
\q1
\v 7 The Lord is my helper; and I will see \add my desire\add* upon my enemies. 
\q1
\v 8 \add It is\add* better to trust in the Lord than to trust in man. 
\q1
\v 9 \add It is\add* better to hope in the Lord, than to hope in princes. 
\p
\q1
\v 10 All nations surrounded me: but in the name of the Lord I repulsed them. 
\q1
\v 11 They completely surrounded me: but in the name of the Lord I repulsed them. 
\q1
\v 12 They surrounded me as bees \add do\add* a honeycomb, and they burst into flame as fire among thorns: but in the name of the Lord I repulsed them. 
\q1
\v 13 I was thrust, and sorely shaken, that I might fall: but the Lord helped me. 
\p
\q1
\v 14 The Lord is my strength and my song, and is become my salvation. 
\q1
\v 15 The voice of exultation and salvation is in the tents of the righteous: the right hand of the Lord has worked mightily. 
\q1
\v 16 The right hand of the Lord has exalted me: the right hand of the Lord has worked powerfully. 
\q1
\v 17 I will not die, but live, and recount the works of the Lord. 
\q1
\v 18 The Lord has chastened me sore: but he has not given me up to death. 
\p
\q1
\v 19 Open to me the gates of righteousness: I will go into them, and give praise to the Lord. 
\q1
\v 20 This is the gate of the Lord: the righteous will enter by it. 
\q1
\v 21 I will give thanks to you; because you have heard me, and are become my salvation. 
\q1
\v 22 \x + \xo 117:22 \xt Mat. 21. 42.\x* The stone which the builders rejected, the same is become the head of the corner. 
\q1
\v 23 This has been done of the Lord; and it is wonderful in our eyes. 
\q1
\v 24 This is the day which the Lord has made: let us exult and rejoice in it. 
\q1
\v 25 O Lord, save now: O Lord, send now prosperity. 
\q1
\v 26 \x + \xo 117:26 \xt Mat. 21. 9.\x* Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord: we have blessed you out of the house of the Lord. 
\p
\q1
\v 27 God is the Lord, and he has shined upon us: celebrate the feast with \f + \fr 117:27 \ft Possibly, the multitude, \fqa q. d. \ft cœtu frequenti.\f*thick \add branches, binding the victims\add* even to the horns of the altar. 
\q1
\v 28 You are my God, and I will give you thanks: you are my God, and I will exalt you. I will give thanks to you, for you have heard me, and are become my salvation. 
\q1
\v 29 Give thanks to the Lord; for he is good: for his mercy \add endures\add* forever. 
\c 118 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\p Blessed are the blameless in the way, who walk in the law of the Lord. 
\q1
\v 2 Blessed are those who search out his testimonies: they will diligently seek him with the whole heart. 
\q1
\v 3 For those who work wickedness have not walked in his ways. 
\q1
\v 4 You have commanded \add us\add* diligently to keep your precepts. 
\q1
\v 5 O that my ways were directed to keep your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 6 Then I will not be ashamed, when I have respect to all your commandments. 
\q1
\v 7 I will give you thanks with uprightness of heart, when I have learnt the judgments of your righteousness. 
\q1
\v 8 I will keep your ordinances: O don't forsake me greatly. 
\p
\q1
\v 9 With which will a young man direct his way? By keeping your words. 
\q1
\v 10 With my whole heart have I diligently sought you: didn't cast me away from your commandments. 
\q1
\v 11 I have hidden your oracles in my heart, that I might not sin against you. 
\q1
\v 12 You are blessed, O Lord: teach me your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 13 With my lips have I declared all the judgments of your mouth. 
\q1
\v 14 I have delighted in the way of your testimonies, \add as much\add* as in all riches. 
\q1
\v 15 I will meditate on your commandments, and consider your ways. 
\q1
\v 16 I will meditate on your ordinances: I will not forget your words. 
\p
\q1
\v 17 Give a recompence to your servant: \add so\add* I will live, and keep your words. 
\q1
\v 18 Unveil you my eyes, and I will perceive wondrous things out of your law. 
\q1
\v 19 I am a stranger in the earth: hide not your commandments from me. 
\q1
\v 20 My soul has longed exceedingly for your judgments at all times. 
\q1
\v 21 You have rebuked the proud: cursed are those who turn aside from your commandments. 
\q1
\v 22 Remove from me reproach and contempt; for I have sought out your testimonies. 
\q1
\v 23 For princes sat and spoke against me: but your servant was meditating on your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 24 For your testimonies are my meditation, and your ordinances are my counsellors. 
\p
\q1
\v 25 My soul has cleaved to the ground; quicken you me according to your word. 
\q1
\v 26 I declared my ways, and you did hear me; teach me your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 27 Instruct me in the way of your ordinances; and I will meditate on your wondrous works. 
\q1
\v 28 My soul has slumbered for sorrow; strengthen you me with your words. 
\q1
\v 29 Remove from me the way of wickedness; and be merciful to me \f + \fr 118:29 \fqa q. d. \ft in teaching me thy law.\f*by your law. 
\q1
\v 30 I have chosen the way of truth; and have not forgotten your judgments. 
\q1
\v 31 I have cleaved to your testimonies, O Lord; put me not to shame. 
\q1
\v 32 I ran the way of your commandments, when you did enlarge my heart. 
\p
\q1
\v 33 \f + \fr 118:33 \fqa sc. \ft as a lawgiver.\f*Teach me, O Lord, the way of your ordinances, and I will seek it out continually. 
\q1
\v 34 Instruct me, and I will search out your law, and will keep it with my whole heart. 
\q1
\v 35 Guide me in the path of your commandments; for I have delighted in it. 
\q1
\v 36 Incline my heart to your testimonies, and not to covetousness. 
\q1
\v 37 Turn away my eyes that I may not behold vanity: quicken you me in your way. 
\q1
\v 38 Confirm your oracle to your servant, that he may fear you. 
\q1
\v 39 Take away my reproach which I have feared: for your judgments are good. 
\q1
\v 40 Behold, I have desired your commandments: quicken me in your righteousness. 
\p
\q1
\v 41 Let your mercy come upon me, O Lord; \add even\add* your salvation, according to your word. 
\q1
\v 42 And \add so\add* I will give an answer to those who reproach me: for I have trusted in your words. 
\q1
\v 43 Don't take the word of truth completely out of my mouth; for I have hoped in your judgments. 
\q1
\v 44 So I will keep your law continually, forever and ever. 
\q1
\v 45 I walked also at large: for I sought out your commandments. 
\q1
\v 46 I spoke of your testimonies before kings, and was not ashamed. 
\q1
\v 47 I \f + \fr 118:47 \fqa Or, \ft exercised myself in.\f*meditated on your commandments, which I loved exceedingly. 
\q1
\v 48 I lifted up my hands to your commandments which I loved; and I meditated in your ordinances. 
\p
\q1
\v 49 Remember your words to your servant, wherein you have made me hope. 
\q1
\v 50 This has comforted me in my affliction: for your oracle has quickened me. 
\q1
\v 51 The proud have transgressed exceedingly; but I swerved not from your law. 
\q1
\v 52 I remembered your judgments of old, O Lord; and was comforted. 
\q1
\v 53 Despair took hold upon me, because of the sinners who forsake your law. 
\q1
\v 54 Your ordinances were my songs in the place of my sojourning. 
\q1
\v 55 I remembered your name, O Lord, in the night, and kept your law. 
\q1
\v 56 This I had, because I diligently sought your ordinances. 
\p
\q1
\v 57 You are my portion, O Lord: I said that I would keep your law. 
\q1
\v 58 I besought your \f + \fr 118:58 \fqa Gr. \ft presence, \fqa or, \ft countenance.\f*favour with my whole heart: have mercy upon me according to your word. 
\q1
\v 59 I thought on your ways, and turned my feet to your testimonies. 
\q1
\v 60 I prepared myself, (and was not terrified,) to keep your commandments. 
\q1
\v 61 The snares of sinners entangled me: but I forgot not your law. 
\q1
\v 62 At midnight I arose, to give thanks to you for the judgments of your righteousness. 
\q1
\v 63 I am a companion of all those who fear you, and of those who keep your commandments. 
\q1
\v 64 O Lord, the earth is full of your mercy: teach me your ordinances. 
\p
\q1
\v 65 You have worked kindly with your servant, O Lord, according to your word. 
\q1
\v 66 Teach me kindness, and instruction, and knowledge: for I have believed your commandments. 
\q1
\v 67 Before I was afflicted, I transgressed; therefore have I kept your word. 
\q1
\v 68 Good are you, O Lord; therefore in your goodness teach me your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 69 The injustice of the proud has been multiplied against me: but I will search out your commandments with all my heart. 
\q1
\v 70 Their heart has been curdled like milk; but I have meditated on your law. 
\q1
\v 71 \add It is\add* good for me that you have afflicted me; that I might learn your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 72 The law of your mouth is better to me than thousands of gold and silver. 
\p
\q1
\v 73 Your hands have made me, and fashioned me: instruct me, that I may learn your commandments. 
\q1
\v 74 Those who fear you will see me and rejoice: for I have hoped in your words. 
\q1
\v 75 I know, O Lord, that your judgments are righteousness, and \add that\add* you in truthfulness have afflicted me. 
\q1
\v 76 Let, I pray you, your mercy be to comfort me, according to your word to your servant. 
\q1
\v 77 Let your compassions come to me, that I may live: for your law is my meditation. 
\q1
\v 78 Let the proud be ashamed; for they transgressed against me unjustly: but I will meditate in your commandments. 
\q1
\v 79 Let those that fear you, and those that know your testimonies, turn to me. 
\q1
\v 80 Let my heart be blameless in your ordinances, that I may not be ashamed. 
\p
\q1
\v 81 My soul faints for your salvation: I have hoped in your words. 
\q1
\v 82 My eyes failed \add in waiting\add* for your word, saying, When will you comfort me? 
\q1
\v 83 For I have become as a bottle in the frost: \add yet\add* I have not forgotten your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 84 How many are the days of your servant? When will you execute judgment for me on those who persecute me? 
\q1
\v 85 Transgressors told me \add idle tales\add*; but not according to your law, O Lord. 
\q1
\v 86 All your commandments are truth; they persecuted me unjustly; help you me. 
\q1
\v 87 They nearly made an end of me in the earth; but I forsook not your commandments. 
\q1
\v 88 Quicken me according to your mercy; so I will keep the testimonies of your mouth. 
\p
\q1
\v 89 Your word, O Lord, abides in heaven forever. 
\q1
\v 90 Your truth \add endures\add* to all generations; you have founded the earth, and it abides. 
\q1
\v 91 The day continues by your arrangement; for all things are your servants. 
\q1
\v 92 Were it not that your law is my meditation, then I should have perished in my affliction. 
\q1
\v 93 I will never forget your ordinances; for with them you have quickened me. 
\q1
\v 94 I am yours, save me; for I have sought out your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 95 Sinners laid wait for me to destroy me; \add but\add* I understood your testimonies. 
\q1
\v 96 I have seen an end of all perfection; \add but\add* your commandment is very broad. 
\p
\q1
\v 97 How I have loved your law, O Lord! It is my meditation all the day. 
\q1
\v 98 You have made me wiser than my enemies \add in\add* your commandment; for it is mine forever. 
\q1
\v 99 I have more understanding than all my teachers; for your testimonies are my meditation. 
\q1
\v 100 I understand more than the aged; because I have sought out your commandments. 
\q1
\v 101 I have kept back my feet from every evil way, that I might keep your words. 
\q1
\v 102 I have not declined from your judgments; for you have \f + \fr 118:102 \ft That is, as a lawgiver.\f*instructed me. 
\p
\q1
\v 103 How sweet are your oracles to my throat! More so than honey to my mouth! 
\q1
\v 104 I gain understanding by your commandments: therefore I have hated every way of unrighteousness. 
\p
\q1
\v 105 Your law is a lamp to my feet, and a light to my paths. 
\q1
\v 106 I have sworn and determined to keep the judgments of your righteousness. 
\q1
\v 107 I have been very greatly afflicted, O Lord: quicken me, according to your word. 
\q1
\v 108 Accept, I pray you, O Lord, the freewill-offerings of my mouth, and teach me your judgments. 
\q1
\v 109 My soul is continually in \f + \fr 118:109 \fqa Heb. \ft and \fqa Alex. \ft my.\f*your hands; and I have not forgotten your law. 
\q1
\v 110 Sinners spread a snare for me; but I erred not from your commandments. 
\q1
\v 111 I have inherited your testimonies forever; for they are the joy of my heart. 
\q1
\v 112 I have inclined my heart to perform your ordinances forever, \f + \fr 118:112 \ft See \fqa Heb.\f*in return \add for your mercies\add*. 
\p
\q1
\v 113 I have hated transgressors; but I have loved your law. 
\q1
\v 114 You are my helper and my supporter; I have hoped in your words. 
\q1
\v 115 Depart from me, you evil-doers; for I will search out the commandments of my God. 
\q1
\v 116 Uphold me according to your word, and quicken me; and don't make me ashamed of my expectation. 
\q1
\v 117 Help me, and I will be saved; and I will meditate in your ordinances continually. 
\q1
\v 118 You have brought to nothing all that depart from your ordinances; for their inward thought is unrighteous. 
\q1
\v 119 I have reckoned all the sinners of the earth as transgressors; therefore have I loved your testimonies. 
\q1
\v 120 Penetrate my flesh with your fear; for I am afraid of your judgments. 
\p
\q1
\v 121 I have done judgment and justice; don't deliver me up to those who injure me. 
\q1
\v 122 Receive your servant for good: don't let the proud accuse me falsely. 
\q1
\v 123 My eyes have failed for your salvation, and for the word of your righteousness. 
\q1
\v 124 Deal with your servant according to your mercy, and teach me your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 125 I am your servant; instruct me, and I will know your testimonies. 
\q1
\v 126 \add It is\add* time for the Lord to work: they have completely broken your law. 
\q1
\v 127 Therefore have I loved your commandments more than gold, or the topaz. 
\q1
\v 128 Therefore I directed myself \add according\add* to all your commandments: I have hated every unjust way. 
\p
\q1
\v 129 Your testimonies are wonderful: therefore my soul has sought them out. 
\q1
\v 130 The manifestation of your words will enlighten, and instruct the simple. 
\q1
\v 131 I opened my mouth, and drew breath: for I earnestly longed after your commandments. 
\q1
\v 132 Look upon me and have mercy upon me, after the manner of those who love your name. 
\q1
\v 133 Order my steps according to your word: and don't let any wickedness have dominion over me. 
\q1
\v 134 Deliver me from the false accusation of men: so will I keep your commandments. 
\q1
\v 135 Cause your face to shine upon your servant: and teach me your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 136 My eyes have been bathed in streams of water, because I didn't keep your law. 
\p
\q1
\v 137 Righteous are you, O Lord, and upright are your judgments. 
\q1
\v 138 You have commanded righteousness and perfect truth, \add as\add* your testimonies. 
\q1
\v 139 Your zeal has quite wasted me: because my enemies have forgotten your words. 
\q1
\v 140 Your word \add has been\add* very fully tried; and your servant loves it. 
\q1
\v 141 I am young and despised: \add yet\add* I have not forgotten your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 142 Your righteousness is an everlasting righteousness, and your law is truth. 
\q1
\v 143 Afflictions and distresses found me: \add but\add* your commandments \add were\add* my meditation. 
\q1
\v 144 Your testimonies \add are\add* an everlasting righteousness: instruct me, and I will live. 
\p
\q1
\v 145 I cried with my whole heart; hear me, O Lord: I will search out your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 146 I cried to you; save me, and I will keep your testimonies. 
\q1
\v 147 I arose before the dawn, and cried: I hoped in your words. 
\q1
\v 148 My eyes prevented the dawn, that I might meditate on your oracles. 
\q1
\v 149 Hear my voice, O Lord, according to your mercy; quicken me according to your judgment. 
\q1
\v 150 They have drawn near who persecuted me unlawfully; and they are far removed from your law. 
\q1
\v 151 You are near, O Lord; and all your \f + \fr 118:151 \fqa Alex. \ft ἐντολαί, commands.\f*ways are truth. 
\q1
\v 152 I have known of old \f + \fr 118:152 \fqa Gr. \ft of.\f*concerning your testimonies, that you have founded them forever. 
\p
\q1
\v 153 Look upon my affliction, and rescue me; for I have not forgotten your law. 
\q1
\v 154 Plead my cause, and ransom me: quicken me because of your word. 
\q1
\v 155 Salvation is far from sinners: for they have not searched out your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 156 Your mercies, O Lord, are many: quicken me according to your judgment. 
\q1
\v 157 Many are those who persecute me and oppress me: \add but\add* I have not declined from your testimonies. 
\q1
\v 158 I beheld men acting foolishly, and I pined away; for they didn't keep your oracles. 
\q1
\v 159 Behold, I have loved your commandments, O Lord: quicken me in your mercy. 
\q1
\v 160 The beginning of your words is truth; and all the judgments of your righteousness \add endure\add* forever. 
\p
\q1
\v 161 Princes persecuted me without a cause, but my heart feared because of your words. 
\q1
\v 162 I will exult because of your oracles, as one that finds much spoil. 
\q1
\v 163 I hate and abhor unrighteousness; but I love your law. 
\q1
\v 164 Seven times in a day have I praised you because of the judgments of your righteousness. 
\q1
\v 165 Great peace have those who love your law: and there is no stumbling-block to them. 
\q1
\v 166 I waited for your salvation, O Lord, and have loved your commandments. 
\q1
\v 167 My soul has kept your testimonies, and loved them exceedingly. 
\q1
\v 168 I have kept your commandments and your testimonies; for all my ways are before you, O Lord. 
\p
\q1
\v 169 Let my supplication come near before you, O Lord; instruct me according to your oracle. 
\q1
\v 170 Let my petition come in before you, O Lord; deliver me according to your oracle. 
\q1
\v 171 Let my lips utter a hymn, when you will have taught me your ordinances. 
\q1
\v 172 Let my tongue utter your oracles; for all your commandments are righteous. 
\q1
\v 173 Let your hand be \add prompt\add* to save me; for I have chosen your commandments. 
\q1
\v 174 I have longed after your salvation, O Lord; and your law is my meditation. 
\q1
\v 175 My soul will live, and will praise you; and your judgments will help me. 
\q1
\v 176 I have gone astray like a lost sheep; seek your servant; for I have not forgotten your commandments. 
\c 119 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Degrees. 
\p In my affliction I cried to the Lord, and he listened to me. 
\q1
\v 2 Deliver my soul, O Lord, from unjust lips, and from a deceitful tongue. 
\p
\q1
\v 3 What should be given to you, and what should be added to you, for \add your\add* crafty tongue? 
\q1
\v 4 Sharpened weapons of the mighty, with coals of the desert. 
\p
\q1
\v 5 Woe is me, that my sojourning is \f + \fr 119:5 \fqa Heb. \ft משך.\f*prolonged; I have tabernacled among the tents of Kedar. 
\q1
\v 6 My soul has long been a sojourner; 
\q1
\v 7 I was peaceable among those who hated peace; when I spoke to them, they warred against me without a cause. 
\c 120 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Degrees. 
\p I lifted up my eyes to the mountains, where my help will come. 
\q1
\v 2 My help \add will come\add* from the Lord, who made the heaven and the earth. 
\q1
\v 3 Don't let your foot be moved; and don't let your keeper slumber. 
\q1
\v 4 Behold, he who keeps Israel will not slumber nor sleep. 
\q1
\v 5 The Lord will keep you: the Lord is your shelter upon your right hand. 
\q1
\v 6 The sun will not burn you by day, neither the moon by night. 
\q1
\v 7 May the Lord preserve you from all evil: the Lord will keep your soul. 
\q1
\v 8 The Lord will keep your coming in, and your going out, from now on and even forever. 
\c 121 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Degrees. 
\p I was glad when they said to me, Let us go into the house of the Lord. 
\q1
\v 2 Our feet stood in your courts, O Jerusalem. 
\q1
\v 3 Jerusalem is built as a city whose fellowship is complete. 
\q1
\v 4 For there the tribes went up, the tribes of the Lord, as a testimony for Israel, to give thanks to the name of the Lord. 
\q1
\v 5 For there are set thrones for judgment, \add even\add* thrones for the house of David. 
\p
\q1
\v 6 \f + \fr 121:6 \fqa Or, \ft ask Jerusalem how it is with her.\f*Pray now for the peace of Jerusalem: and \add let there be\add* prosperity to those who love you. 
\q1
\v 7 Let peace, I pray, be within your host, and prosperity in your palaces. 
\q1
\v 8 For the sake of my brothers and my neighbours, I have indeed spoken peace concerning you. 
\q1
\v 9 Because of the house of the Lord our God, I have diligently sought your good. 
\c 122 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Degrees. 
\p To you who dwell in heaven have I lifted up my eyes. 
\q1
\v 2 Behold, as the eyes of servants \add are directed\add* to the hands of their masters, \add and\add* as the eyes of a maiden-servant to the hands of her mistress; so our eyes \add are directed\add* to the Lord our God, until he have mercy upon us. 
\q1
\v 3 Have pity upon us, O Lord, have pity upon us: for we are exceedingly filled with contempt. 
\q1
\v 4 \add Yes\add*, our soul has been exceedingly filled \add with it\add*: \f + \fr 122:4 \fqa Or, \ft we are the reproach of them that are at ease.\f*\add let\add* the reproach \add be\add* to those who are at ease, and contempt to the proud. 
\c 123 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Degrees. 
\p If it had not been that the Lord was among us, let Israel now say; 
\q1
\v 2 if it had not been that the Lord was among us, when men rose up against us; 
\q1
\v 3 truly they would have swallowed us up alive, when their wrath was kindled against us: 
\q1
\v 4 truly the water would have drowned us, our soul would have gone under the torrent. 
\q1
\v 5 Yes, our soul would have gone under the overwhelming water. 
\p
\q1
\v 6 Blessed be the Lord, who has not given us for a prey to their teeth. 
\q1
\v 7 Our soul has been delivered as a sparrow from the snare of the bird-catchers: the snare is broken, and we are delivered. 
\q1
\v 8 Our help is in the name of the Lord, who made heaven and earth. 
\c 124 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Degrees. 
\p Those who trust in the Lord \add will be\add* as mount Zion: he who dwells in Jerusalem will never be moved. 
\q1
\v 2 The mountains are all around her, and \add so\add* the Lord is all around his people, from now on and even forever. 
\q1
\v 3 For the Lord will not allow the rod of sinners to be upon the lot of the righteous; lest the righteous should stretch forth their hands to wickedness. 
\p
\q1
\v 4 Do good, O Lord, to them \add that are\add* good, and to them \add that are\add* upright in heart. 
\q1
\v 5 But those who turn aside to crooked ways the Lord will lead away with the workers of wickedness: \f + \fr 124:5 \fqa Or, \ft let peace be.\f*\add but\add* peace \add will be\add* upon Israel. 
\c 125 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Degrees. 
\p When the Lord turned the captivity of Zion, we became as comforted ones. 
\q1
\v 2 Then was our mouth filled with joy, and our tongue with exultation: then would they say among the nations, 
\q1
\v 3 The Lord has done great things among them. The Lord has done great things for us, we became joyful. 
\p
\q1
\v 4 Turn, O Lord, our captivity, as the streams in the south. 
\q1
\v 5 Those who sow in tears will reap in joy. 
\q1
\v 6 They went on and wept as they cast their seeds; but they will surely come with exultation, bringing their sheaves \add with them\add*. 
\c 126 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Degrees. 
\p Except the Lord build the house, those who build labour in vain: except the Lord keep the city, the watchman watches in vain. 
\q1
\v 2 It is vain for you to rise early: you rise up after resting, you who eat the bread of grief; while he gives sleep to his beloved. 
\p
\q1
\v 3 Behold, the inheritance of the Lord, children, the reward of the fruit of the womb. 
\q1
\v 4 As arrows in the hand of a mighty man; so are the children of those who were outcasts. 
\q1
\v 5 Blessed is the man who will satisfy his desire with them: they will not be ashamed when they will speak to their enemies in the gates. 
\c 127 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Degrees. 
\p Blessed are all those who fear the Lord; who walk in his ways. 
\q1
\v 2 You will eat the \f + \fr 127:2 \fqa Alex. \ft fruits of thy labours.\f*labours of your hands: you are blessed, and it will be well with you. 
\q1
\v 3 Your wife will be as a fruitful vine on the sides of your house: your children as young olive-plants all around your table. 
\p
\q1
\v 4 Behold, thus will the man be blessed that fears the Lord. 
\q1
\v 5 May the Lord bless you out of Zion; and may you see the prosperity of Jerusalem all the days of your life. 
\q1
\v 6 May you see your children's children. Peace be upon Israel. 
\c 128 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Degrees. 
\p Many a time have they warred against me from my youth, let Israel now say: 
\q1
\v 2 Many a time have they warred against me from my youth: and yet they didn't prevail against me. 
\q1
\v 3 The sinners worked upon my back: they prolonged their \f + \fr 128:3 \ft שיך iniquity, easily read for שוכה a furrow.\f*wickedness. 
\q1
\v 4 The righteous Lord has cut asunder the necks of sinners. 
\p
\q1
\v 5 Let all that hate Zion be put to shame and turned back. 
\q1
\v 6 Let them be as the grass of the house-tops, which withers before it is plucked up. 
\q1
\v 7 With which the reaper fills not his hand, nor he who makes up the sheaves, his bosom. 
\q1
\v 8 Neither do those who go by say, The blessing of the Lord be upon you: we have blessed you in the name of the Lord. 
\c 129 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Degrees. 
\p Out of the depths have I cried to you, O Lord. 
\q1
\v 2 O Lord, listen to my voice; let your ears be attentive to the voice of my supplication. 
\q1
\v 3 If you, O Lord, should mark iniquities, O Lord, who will stand? 
\q1
\v 4 For with you is \f + \fr 129:4 \fqa Or, \ft propitiation.\f*forgiveness: for your \f + \fr 129:4 \ft See \xt Gen. 31. 53.\f*name's sake 
\q1
\v 5 have I waited for you, O Lord, my soul has waited for your word. 
\q1
\v 6 My soul has hoped in the Lord; from the morning watch till night. 
\q1
\v 7 Let Israel hope in the Lord: for with the Lord is mercy, and with him is plenteous redemption. 
\q1
\v 8 He will redeem Israel from all his iniquities. 
\c 130 
\d
\v 1 \f + \fr 130:1 \fqa Alex. \ft + 'for David.'\f*A Song of Degrees. 
\p O Lord, my heart isn't exalted, neither have my eyes been \add haughtily\add* raised: neither have I exercised myself in great \add matters\add*, nor in things too wonderful for me. 
\q1
\v 2 \add I will have sinned\add* if I have not been humble, but have exalted my soul: according to \add the relation of\add* a weaned child to his mother, so will you recompense my soul. 
\q1
\v 3 Let Israel hope in the Lord, from now on and forever. 
\c 131 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Degrees. 
\p Lord, remember David, and all his meekness: 
\q1
\v 2 how he swore to the Lord, \add and\add* vowed to the God of Jacob, \add saying\add*, 
\q1
\v 3 \f + \fr 131:3 \fqa Gr. \ft if I shall, etc. \fqa Hebraism.\f*I will not go into the tabernacle of my house; I will not go up to the couch of my bed; 
\q1
\v 4 I will not give sleep to my eyes, nor slumber to my eyelids, nor rest to my temples, 
\q1
\v 5 until I find a place for the Lord, a tabernacle for the God of Jacob. 
\q1
\v 6 Behold, we heard of it in Ephratha; we found it in the fields of the wood. 
\q1
\v 7 Let us enter into his tents: let us worship at the place where his feet stood. 
\p
\q1
\v 8 Arise, O Lord, into your rest; you, and the ark of your holiness. 
\q1
\v 9 Your priests will clothe themselves with righteousness; and your saints will exult. 
\q1
\v 10 For the sake of your servant David don't turn away the face of your anointed. 
\p
\q1
\v 11 The Lord swore \add in\add* truth to David, and he will not annul it, \add saying\add*, Of the fruit of your body will I set \add a king\add* upon your throne. 
\q1
\v 12 If your children will keep my covenant, and these my testimonies which I will teach them, their children also will sit upon your throne forever. 
\q1
\v 13 For the Lord has elected Zion, he has chosen her for a habitation for himself, \add saying\add*, 
\q1
\v 14 This is my rest forever: here will I dwell; for I have chosen it. 
\q1
\v 15 I will surely bless her provision: I will satisfy her poor with bread. 
\q1
\v 16 I will clothe her priests with salvation; and her saints will greatly exult. 
\q1
\v 17 There will I cause to spring up a horn to David: I have prepared a lamp for my anointed. 
\q1
\v 18 His enemies will I clothe with shame; but upon himself will my \f + \fr 131:18 \ft See \xt Ps. 88. 39.\f*holiness flourish. 
\c 132 
\d
\v 1 \f + \fr 132:1 \fqa Alex. \ft + 'for David.'\f*A Song of Degrees. 
\p See now! What is so good, or what so pleasant, as for brothers to dwell together? 
\q1
\v 2 \add It is\add* as ointment on the head, that ran down to the beard, \add even\add* the beard of Aaron; that ran down to the fringe of his clothing. 
\q1
\v 3 As the dew of Aermon, that comes down on the mountains of Zion: for there the Lord commanded the blessing, \add even\add* life forever. 
\c 133 
\d
\v 1 A Song of Degrees. 
\p Behold now, bless the Lord, all the servants of the Lord, who stand in the house of the Lord, in the courts of the house of our God. 
\q1
\v 2 Lift up your hands by night \f + \fr 133:2 \fqa Or, \ft to the holy places.\f*in the sanctuaries, and bless the Lord. 
\q1
\v 3 May the Lord, who made heaven and earth, bless you out of Zion. 
\c 134 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\p Praise you the name of the Lord; praise the Lord, \add you his\add* servants, 
\q1
\v 2 who stand in the house of the Lord, in the courts of the house of our God. 
\q1
\v 3 Praise you the Lord; for the Lord is good: sing praises to his name; for \add it is\add* good. 
\p
\q1
\v 4 For the Lord has chosen Jacob for himself, \add and\add* Israel for his peculiar treasure. 
\q1
\v 5 For I know that the Lord is great, and our Lord is above all gods; 
\q1
\v 6 all that the Lord willed, he did in heaven, and on the earth, in the sea, and in all deeps. 
\q1
\v 7 Who brings up clouds from the extremity of the earth: he has made lightnings for the rain: he brings winds out of his treasures. 
\q1
\v 8 Who struck the first-born of Egypt, both of man and beast. 
\q1
\v 9 He sent signs and wonders into the midst of you, O Egypt, on Pharaoh, and on all his servants. 
\q1
\v 10 Who struck many nations, and killed mighty kings; 
\q1
\v 11 Seon king of the Amorites, and Og king of Basan, and all the kingdoms of Canaan: 
\q1
\v 12 and gave their land \add for\add* an inheritance, an inheritance to Israel his people. 
\p
\q1
\v 13 O Lord, your name \add endures\add* forever, and your memorial to all generations. 
\q1
\v 14 For the Lord will judge his people, and comfort himself concerning his servants. 
\q1
\v 15 The idols of the nations are silver and gold, the works of men's hands. 
\q1
\v 16 They have a mouth, but they cannot speak; they have eyes, but they cannot see; 
\q1
\v 17 they have ears, but they cannot hear; for there is no breath in their mouth. 
\q1
\v 18 Let those who make them be made like to them; and all those who trust in them. 
\p
\q1
\v 19 O house of Israel, bless you the Lord: O house of Aaron, bless you the Lord: 
\q1
\v 20 O house of Levi, bless the Lord: you who fear the Lord, bless the Lord. 
\q1
\v 21 Blessed in Zion be the Lord, who dwells in Jerusalem. 
\c 135 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\p Give thanks to the Lord: for he is good: for his mercy \add endures\add* forever. 
\q1
\v 2 Give thanks to the God of gods: for his mercy \add endures\add* forever. 
\q1
\v 3 Give thanks to the Lord of lords: for his mercy \add endures\add* forever. 
\p
\q1
\v 4 To him who alone has worked great wonders: for his mercy \add endures\add* forever. 
\q1
\v 5 To him who made the heavens by understanding; for his mercy \add endures\add* forever. 
\q1
\v 6 To him who established the earth on the waters; for his mercy \add endures\add* forever. 
\q1
\v 7 To him who alone made great lights; for his mercy \add endures\add* forever. 
\q1
\v 8 The sun to rule the day; for his mercy \add endures\add* forever. 
\q1
\v 9 The moon and the stars to rule the night; for his mercy \add endures\add* forever. 
\p
\q1
\v 10 To him who struck Egypt with their first-born; for his mercy \add endures\add* forever. 
\q1
\v 11 Brought Israel out of the midst of them; for his mercy \add endures\add* forever: 
\q1
\v 12 with a strong hand, and a high arm: for his mercy \add endures\add* forever. 
\q1
\v 13 To him who divided the Red Sea into parts: for his mercy \add endures\add* forever: 
\q1
\v 14 and brought Israel through the midst of it: for his mercy \add endures\add* forever: 
\q1
\v 15 and overthrew Pharaoh and his host in the Red Sea: for his mercy endures forever. 
\q1
\v 16 To him who led his people through the wilderness: for his mercy \add endures\add* forever. 
\p
\q1
\v 17 To him who struck great kings: for his mercy \add endures\add* forever: 
\q1
\v 18 and killed mighty kings; for his mercy \add endures\add* forever: 
\q1
\v 19 Seon king of the Amorites: for his mercy \add endures\add* forever: 
\q1
\v 20 and Og king of Basan: for his mercy \add endures\add* forever: 
\q1
\v 21 and gave their land \add for\add* an inheritance: for his mercy \add endures\add* forever: 
\q1
\v 22 even an inheritance to Israel his servant: for his mercy \add endures\add* forever. 
\p
\q1
\v 23 For the Lord remembered us in our low estate; for his mercy \add endures\add* forever: 
\q1
\v 24 and redeemed us from our enemies; for his mercy \add endures\add* forever. 
\q1
\v 25 Who gives food to all flesh; for his mercy \add endures\add* forever. 
\q1
\v 26 Give thanks to the God of heaven; for his mercy \add endures\add* forever. 
\c 136 
\d
\v 1 \f + \fr 136:1 \fqa Alex. \ft omits.\f*For David, \add a Psalm\add* of Jeremiah. 
\p By the rivers of Babylon, there we sat; and wept when we remembered Zion. 
\q1
\v 2 We hung our \f + \fr 136:2 \fqa Gr. \ft organs, \fqa or, \ft instruments.\f*harps on the willows among it. 
\q1
\v 3 For there those who had taken us captive asked of us the words of a song; and those who had carried us away \add asked\add* a hymn, \add saying\add*, Sing us \add one\add* of the songs of Zion. 
\p
\q1
\v 4 How should we sing the Lord's song \f + \fr 136:4 \fqa Gr. \ft on.\f*in a foreign land? 
\q1
\v 5 If I forget you, O Jerusalem, let my right hand forget \add its skill\add*. 
\q1
\v 6 May my tongue cling to my throat, if I do not remember you; if I do not prefer Jerusalem as the chief of my joy. 
\p
\q1
\v 7 Remember, O Lord, the children of Edom in the day of Jerusalem; who said, Rase \add it\add*, \f + \fr 136:7 \fqa Gr. \ft empty, empty.\f*rase \add it\add*, even to its foundations. 
\q1
\v 8 Wretched daughter of Babylon! Blessed \add he will be\add* who will reward you as you have rewarded us. 
\q1
\v 9 Blessed \add he will be\add* who will seize and dash your infants against the rock. 
\c 137 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm for David, of Haggai and Zechariah. 
\p I will give you thanks, O Lord, with my whole heart; and I will sing psalms to you before the angels; for you have heard all the words of my mouth. 
\q1
\v 2 I will worship toward your holy temple, and give thanks to your name, on account of your mercy and your truth; for you have magnified your holy name above every thing. 
\q1
\v 3 In whatever day I will call upon you, hear me speedily; you will abundantly provide me with your power in my soul. 
\q1
\v 4 Let all the kings of the earth, O Lord, give thanks to you; for they have heard all the words of your mouth. 
\q1
\v 5 Let them sing in the ways of the Lord; for great is the glory of the Lord. 
\p
\q1
\v 6 For the Lord is high, and \add yet\add* regards the lowly; and he knows high things from afar off. 
\q1
\v 7 Though I should walk among affliction, you will quicken me; you have stretched forth your hands against the wrath of my enemies, and your right hand has saved me. 
\q1
\v 8 O Lord, you will recompense \add them\add* on my behalf: your mercy, O Lord, \add endures\add* forever: overlook not the works of your hands. 
\c 138 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm of David.\f + \fr 138:1 \fqa Alex. \ft + of Zacharias in the dispersion.\f* 
\p O Lord, you have proved me, and known me. 
\q1
\v 2 You know my down-sitting and my up-rising: you understand my thoughts \f + \fr 138:2 \fqa Gr. \ft from afar.\f*long before. 
\q1
\v 3 You have traced my path and my \f + \fr 138:3 \fqa q. d. \ft of rushes, \fqa lit. \ft rush.\f*bed, and have foreseen all my ways. 
\q1
\v 4 For there is no unrighteous word in my tongue: behold, O Lord, you have known all things, 
\q1
\v 5 the last and the first: you have fashioned me, and laid your hand upon me. 
\p
\q1
\v 6 The knowledge of you is too wonderful for me; it is very difficult, I cannot \add attain\add* to it. 
\q1
\v 7 Where will I go from your Spirit? And where will I flee from your presence? 
\q1
\v 8 If I should go up to heaven, you are there: if I should go down to hell, you are present. 
\q1
\v 9 If I should spread my wings \add to fly\add* \f + \fr 138:9 \fqa Alex. \ft κατ᾿ ὄρθον, toward the dawn.\f*straight forward, and sojourn at the extremity of the sea, \add it would be vain\add*, 
\q1
\v 10 for even there your hand would guide me, and your right hand would hold me. 
\q1
\v 11 When I said, Surely the darkness will cover me; even the night \add was\add* light in my \f + \fr 138:11 \ft Comp. \fqa Heb.\f*luxury. 
\q1
\v 12 For darkness will not be darkness with you; but night will be light as day: as its darkness, so will its light \add be to you\add*. 
\q1
\v 13 For you, O Lord, have possessed my reins; you have helped me from my mother's womb. 
\q1
\v 14 I will give you thanks; for you are fearfully wondrous; wondrous are your works; and my soul knows \add it\add* well. 
\q1
\v 15 My bones which you made in secret were not hidden from you, nor my substance, in the lowest parts of the earth. 
\q1
\v 16 Your eyes saw my unwrought \add substance\add*, and all \add men\add* will be written in your book; they will be formed by day, though \add there should for a time\add* be no one among them. 
\p
\q1
\v 17 But your friends, O God, have been greatly honoured by me; their rule has been greatly strengthened. 
\q1
\v 18 I will number them, and they will be multiplied beyond the sand; I awake, and am still with you. 
\p
\q1
\v 19 Oh that you would kill the wicked, O God; depart from me, you men of blood. 
\q1
\v 20 For you will say concerning \add their\add* thought, \add that\add* they will take your cities in vain. 
\q1
\v 21 Have I not hated them, O Lord, that hate you? And wasted away because of your enemies? 
\q1
\v 22 I have hated them with perfect hatred; they were counted my enemies. 
\q1
\v 23 Prove me, O God, and know my heart; examine me, and know my paths; 
\q1
\v 24 and see if \add there is any\add* way of wickedness in me, and lead me in an everlasting way. 
\c 139 
\d
\v 1 For the end, a Psalm of David. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 Rescue me, O Lord, from the evil man; deliver me from the unjust man. 
\q1
\v 3 Who have devised injustice in their hearts; all the day they prepared war. 
\q1
\v 4 They have sharpened their tongue as \add the tongue\add* of a snake; \x + \xo 139:4 \xt Rom. 3. 13.\x* the poison of asps is under their lips. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\q1
\v 5 Keep me, O Lord, from the hand of the sinner; rescue me from unjust men; who have purposed to overthrow my goings. 
\q1
\v 6 The proud have hid a snare for me, and have stretched out ropes \add for\add* snares for my feet; they set a stumbling-block for me near the path. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 7 I said to the Lord, You are my God; listen, O Lord, to the voice of my supplication. 
\q1
\v 8 O Lord God, the strength of my salvation; you have screened my head in the day of battle. 
\q1
\v 9 Don't deliver me, O Lord, to the sinner, according to my desire: they have devised \add mischief\add* against me; don't forsake me, lest they should be exalted. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 10 \add As for\add* the head of those who compass me, the mischief of their lips will cover them. 
\q1
\v 11 Coals of fire will fall upon them on the earth; and you will cast them down in afflictions: they will not bear up \add under them\add*. 
\q1
\v 12 A talkative man will not prosper on the earth: evils will hunt the unrighteous man to destruction. 
\q1
\v 13 I know that the Lord will maintain the cause of the \f + \fr 139:13 \fqa Gr. \ft singular.\f*poor, and the right of the needy ones. 
\q1
\v 14 Surely the righteous will give thanks to your name: the upright will dwell in your presence. 
\c 140 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm of David. 
\p O Lord, I have cried to you; hear me: pay attention to the voice of my supplication, when I cry to you. 
\q1
\v 2 Let my prayer be set forth before you as incense; the lifting up of my hands \add as\add* an evening sacrifice. 
\q1
\v 3 Set a watch, O Lord, on my mouth, and a \f + \fr 140:3 \fqa Lit. \ft a door of fortification.\f*strong door about my lips. 
\q1
\v 4 Incline not my heart to evil things, to \f + \fr 140:4 \fqa Gr. \ft pretend pretences.\f*employ pretexts \f + \fr 140:4 \fqa Gr. \ft in.\f*for sins, with men who work wickedness: and \f + \fr 140:4 \fqa Gr. \ft I will not.\f*don't let me unite with their choice ones. 
\q1
\v 5 The righteous will chasten me with mercy, and reprove me: but don't let the oil of the sinner anoint my head: for yet will my prayer also be in their \f + \fr 140:5 \fqa q. d. \ft lest I be injured by them.\f*pleasures. 
\p
\q1
\v 6 Their mighty ones have been swallowed up near the rock: they will hear my words, for they are sweet. 
\q1
\v 7 As a lump of earth is crushed upon the ground, our bones have been scattered by the \add mouth of\add* the grave. 
\q1
\v 8 For my eyes are to you, O Lord God: I have hoped in you; don't take away my life. 
\q1
\v 9 Keep me from the snare which they have set for me, and from the stumbling-blocks of those who work wickedness. 
\q1
\v 10 Sinners will fall by their own net: I am alone until I will escape. 
\c 141 
\d
\v 1 \add A Psalm\add* of instruction for David, when he was in the cave,—a Prayer. 
\p
\q1
\v 2 I cried to the Lord with my voice; with my voice I made supplication to the Lord. 
\q1
\v 3 I will pour out before him my supplication: I will declare before him my affliction. 
\q1
\v 4 When my spirit was fainting within me, then you knewest my paths; in the very way wherein I was walking, they hid a snare for me. 
\q1
\v 5 I looked on \add my\add* right hand, and behold, for there was none that noticed me; refuge failed me; and there was none that cared for my soul. 
\q1
\v 6 I cried to you, O Lord, and said, You are my hope, my portion in the land of the living. 
\q1
\v 7 Pay attention to my supplication, for I am brought very low; deliver me from those who persecute me; for they are stronger than I. 
\q1
\v 8 Bring my soul out of prison, that I may give thanks to your name, O Lord; the righteous will wait for me, until you recompense me. 
\c 142 
\d
\v 1 A Psalm of David, when his son pursued him. 
\p O Lord, pay attention to my prayer: listen to my supplication in your truth; hear me in your righteousness. 
\q1
\v 2 Don't enter into judgment with your servant, for in your sight will no \add man\add* living be justified. 
\p
\q1
\v 3 For the enemy has persecuted my soul; he has brought my life down to the ground; he has made me to dwell in a dark \add place\add*, as those that have been long dead. 
\q1
\v 4 Therefore my spirit was grieved in me; my heart was troubled within me. 
\q1
\v 5 I remembered the days of old; and I meditated on all your doings: \add yes\add*, I meditated on the works of your hands. 
\q1
\v 6 I spread forth my hands to you; my soul \add thirsts\add* for you, as a dry land. \qs Pause.\qs* 
\p
\q1
\v 7 Hear me speedily, O Lord; my spirit has failed; don't turn away your face from me, else I will be like to those who go down to the pit. 
\q1
\v 8 Cause me to hear your mercy in the morning; for I have hoped in you; make known to me, O Lord, the way wherein I should walk; for I have lifted up my soul to you. 
\q1
\v 9 Deliver me from my enemies, O Lord; for I have fled to you for refuge. 
\q1
\v 10 Teach me to do your will; for you are my God; your good Spirit will guide me in the \f + \fr 142:10 \fqa Alex. \ft as \fqa Heb. \ft 'land of uprightness.'\f*straight \add way\add*. 
\q1
\v 11 You will quicken me, O Lord, for your name's sake; in your righteousness you will bring my soul out of affliction. 
\q1
\v 12 In your mercy you will destroy my enemies, and will destroy all those that afflict my soul; for I am your servant. 
\c 143 
\d
\v 1 \add A Psalm\add* of David concerning Goliad. 
\p Blessed \add be\add* the Lord my God, who instructs my hands for battle, \add and\add* my fingers for war. 
\q1
\v 2 My mercy, and my refuge; my helper, and my deliverer; my protector, in whom I have trusted; who subdues my people under me. 
\p
\q1
\v 3 Lord, what is man, that you are made known to him? Or the son of man, that you takest account of him? 
\q1
\v 4 Man is like to vanity: his days pass as a shadow. 
\p
\q1
\v 5 O Lord, bow your heavens, and come down: touch the mountains, and they will smoke. 
\q1
\v 6 Send lightning, and you will scatter them: send forth your arrows, and you will discomfit them. 
\q1
\v 7 Send forth your hand from on high; rescue me, and deliver me out of great \f + \fr 143:7 \fqa Gr. \ft many.\f*waters, out of the hand of foreign children; 
\q1
\v 8 whose mouth has spoken vanity, and their right hand is a right hand of wickedness. 
\p
\q1
\v 9 O God, I will sing a new song to you: I will play to you on a psaltery of ten strings. 
\q1
\v 10 \add Even\add* to him who gives \f + \fr 143:10 \fqa Or, \ft victory.\f*salvation to kings: who redeems his servant David from the hurtful sword. 
\q1
\v 11 Deliver me, and rescue me from the hand of foreign children, whose mouth has spoken vanity, and their right hand is a right hand of wickedness; 
\q1
\v 12 whose children are as plants, strengthened in their youth: their daughters are beautiful, sumptuously adorned after the similitude of a temple. 
\q1
\v 13 Their garners are full, and bursting with one kind of store after another; their sheep are prolific, multiplying in their streets. 
\q1
\v 14 Their oxen are fat: there is no falling down of a hedge, nor going out, nor cry in their \f + \fr 143:14 \fqa Or, \ft habitations.\f*folds. 
\q1
\v 15 Men bless the people to whom this lot belongs, \add but\add* blessed is the people whose God is the Lord. 
\c 144 
\d
\v 1 David's \add Psalm of\add* praise. 
\p I will exalt you, my God, my king; and I will bless your name \f + \fr 144:1 \fqa Lit. \ft to the age, and to the age of the age.\f*forever and ever. 
\q1
\v 2 Every day will I bless you, and I will praise your name \f + \fr 144:2 \fqa Lit. \ft to the age, and to the age of the age.\f*forever and ever. 
\q1
\v 3 The Lord is great, and greatly to be praised; and there is no end of his greatness. 
\q1
\v 4 Generation after generation will praise your works, and tell of your power. 
\q1
\v 5 They will speak of the glorious majesty of your holiness, and recount your wonders. 
\q1
\v 6 They will speak of the power of your terrible \add acts\add*; and recount your greatness. 
\q1
\v 7 They will utter the memory of the abundance of your goodness, and will exult in your righteousness. 
\p
\q1
\v 8 The Lord is compassionate, and merciful; long-suffering, and abundant in mercy. 
\q1
\v 9 The Lord is good to those that wait \add on him\add*; and his compassions are over all his works. 
\q1
\v 10 Let all your works, O Lord, give thanks to you; and let your saints bless you. 
\q1
\v 11 They will speak of the glory of your kingdom, and talk of your dominion; 
\q1
\v 12 to make known to the sons of men your power, and the glorious majesty of your kingdom. 
\q1
\v 13 Your kingdom is \f + \fr 144:13 \fqa Gr. \ft a kingdom of all ages.\f*an everlasting kingdom, and your dominion \add endures\add* \f + \fr 144:13 \fqa Gr. \ft in every generation and generation.\f*through all generations. 
\q1
\v 13a The Lord is faithful in his words, and holy in all his works. 
\p
\q1
\v 14 The Lord supports all that are falling, and sets up all that are broken down. 
\q1
\v 15 The eyes of all wait upon you; and you givest \add them\add* their food in due season. 
\q1
\v 16 You openest your hands, and fillest every living thing with pleasure. 
\q1
\v 17 The Lord is righteous in all his ways, and holy in all his works. 
\p
\q1
\v 18 The Lord is near to all that call upon him, to all that call upon him in truth. 
\q1
\v 19 He will perform the desire of those who fear him: and he will hear their supplication, and save them. 
\q1
\v 20 The Lord preserves all that love him: but all sinners he will completely destroy. 
\q1
\v 21 My mouth will speak the praise of the Lord: and let all flesh bless his holy name forever and ever. 
\c 145 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia, \add a Psalm\add* of Haggai and Zechariah. 
\p My soul, praise the Lord. 
\q1
\v 2 While I live will I praise the Lord: I will sing praises to my God as long as I exist. 
\q1
\v 3 Don't trust in princes, nor in the children of men, in whom there is no safety. 
\q1
\v 4 His breath will go forth, and he will return to his earth; in that day all his thoughts will perish. 
\p
\q1
\v 5 Blessed is he whose helper is the God of Jacob, whose hope is in the Lord his God: 
\q1
\v 6 who made heaven, and earth, the sea, and all things in them: who keeps truth forever: 
\q1
\v 7 who executes judgment for the wronged: who gives food to the hungry. The Lord looses the fettered ones: 
\q1
\v 8 the Lord gives wisdom to the blind: 
\p The Lord sets up the broken down: the Lord loves the righteous: the Lord preserves the strangers; 
\q1
\v 9 he will relieve the orphan and widow: but will completely remove the way of sinners. 
\q1
\v 10 The Lord will reign forever, \add even\add* your God, O Zion, to all generations. 
\c 146 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia, \add a Psalm\add* of Haggai and Zechariah. 
\p Praise you the Lord: for psalmody is a good thing; let praise be sweetly sung to our God. 
\q1
\v 2 The Lord builds up Jerusalem; and he will gather together the dispersed of Israel. 
\q1
\v 3 He heals the broken in heart, and binds up their wounds. 
\q1
\v 4 He numbers the multitudes of stars; and calls them all by names. 
\q1
\v 5 Great is our Lord, and great is his strength; and his understanding is infinite. 
\q1
\v 6 The Lord lifts up the meek; but brings sinners down to the ground. 
\p
\q1
\v 7 Begin \add the song\add* with thanksgiving to the Lord; sing praises on the harp to our God: 
\q1
\v 8 who covers the heaven with clouds, who prepares rain for the earth, who causes grass to spring up on the mountains, [\f + \fr 146:8 \ft See Ps \xt 103. 14.\f*and green herb for the service of men;] 
\q1
\v 9 and gives to cattle their food, and to the young ravens that call upon him. 
\q1
\v 10 He will not take pleasure in the strength of a horse; neither is he well-pleased with the legs of a man. 
\q1
\v 11 The Lord takes pleasure in those who fear him, and in all that hope in his mercy. 
\c 147 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia, \add a Psalm\add* of Haggai and Zechariah.\f + \fr 147:1 \ft In the original text, the following verses are numbered 12 to 20.\f* 
\p Praise the Lord, O Jerusalem; praise your God, O Zion. 
\q1
\v 2 For he has strengthened the bars of your gates; he has blessed your children within you. 
\q1
\v 3 He makes your borders peaceful, and fills you with the \f + \fr 147:3 \fqa Lit. \ft fat of wheat.\f*flour of wheat. 
\q1
\v 4 He sends his oracle to the earth: his word will run swiftly. 
\q1
\v 5 He gives snow like wool: he scatters the mist like ashes. 
\q1
\v 6 Casting \add forth\add* his ice like morsels: who will stand before his cold? 
\q1
\v 7 He will send out his word, and melt them: he will blow \add with\add* his wind, and the waters will flow. 
\q1
\v 8 He sends his word to Jacob, his ordinances and judgments to Israel. 
\q1
\v 9 He has not done so to \f + \fr 147:9 \fqa Gr. \ft every.\f*any \add other\add* nation; and he has not shown them his judgments. 
\c 148 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia, \add a Psalm\add* of Haggai and Zechariah. 
\p Praise you the Lord from the heavens: praise him in the highest. 
\q1
\v 2 Praise you him, all his angels: praise you him, all his hosts. 
\q1
\v 3 Praise him, sun and moon: praise him, all you stars and light. 
\q1
\v 4 Praise him, you heavens of heavens, and the water that is above the heavens. 
\q1
\v 5 Let them praise the name of the Lord: for he spoke, and they were made; he commanded, and they were created. 
\q1
\v 6 He has established them forever, even forever and ever: he has made an ordinance, and it will not pass away. 
\p
\q1
\v 7 Praise the Lord from the earth, you snakes, and all deeps. 
\q1
\v 8 Fire, hail, snow, ice, stormy wind; the things that perform his word. 
\q1
\v 9 Mountains, and all hills; fruitful trees, and all cedars: 
\q1
\v 10 wild beasts, and all cattle; reptiles, and winged birds: 
\q1
\v 11 kings of the earth, and all peoples; princes, and all judges of the earth: 
\q1
\v 12 young men and virgins, old men with youths: 
\q1
\v 13 let them praise the name of the Lord: for his name only is exalted; his praise is above the earth and heaven, 
\q1
\v 14 and he will exalt the horn of his people, \f + \fr 148:14 \fqa Or, \ft who is the praise of.\f*\add there is\add* a hymn for all his saints, \add even\add* of the children of Israel, a people who draw near to him. 
\c 149 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\p Sing to the Lord a new song: his praise is in the assembly of the saints. 
\q1
\v 2 Let Israel rejoice in the one who made him; and let the children of Zion exult in their king. 
\q1
\v 3 Let them praise his name in the dance: let them sing praises to him with timbrel and psaltery. 
\q1
\v 4 For the Lord takes pleasure in his people; and will exalt the meek with salvation. 
\p
\q1
\v 5 The saints will rejoice in glory; and will exult on their beds. 
\q1
\v 6 The \f + \fr 149:6 \fqa Gr. \ft exaltations, \fqa q. d. \ft extollings.\f*high praises of God will be in their throat, and two-edged swords in their hands; 
\q1
\v 7 to execute vengeance on the nations, \add and\add* punishments among the peoples; 
\q1
\v 8 to bind their kings with fetters, and their nobles with manacles of iron; 
\q1
\v 9 to execute on them the judgment \f + \fr 149:9 \fqa Gr. \ft inscribed, \fqa sc. \ft in the scripture.\f*written: this honour have all his saints. 
\c 150 
\d
\v 1 Alleluia. 
\p Praise God in his holy places: praise him in the firmament of his power. 
\q1
\v 2 Praise him on \add account of\add* his mighty acts: praise him according to his abundant greatness. 
\q1
\v 3 Praise him with the sound of a trumpet: praise him with psaltery and harp. 
\q1
\v 4 Praise him with timbrel and dance: praise him with stringed instruments and the organ. 
\q1
\v 5 Praise him with melodious cymbals: praise him with loud cymbals. 
\q1
\v 6 Let every thing that has breath praise the Lord. 
\c 151 
\d
\v 1 This Psalm is a genuine one of David, though supernumerary, \add composed\add* when he fought in single combat with \f + \fr 151:1 \fqa Alex. \ft Goliath.\f*Goliad. 
\p I was small among my brothers, and youngest in my father's house: I tended my father's sheep. 
\q1
\v 2 My hands formed a musical instrument, and my fingers tuned a psaltery. 
\q1
\v 3 Who will tell my Lord? The Lord himself, he himself hears. 
\q1
\v 4 He sent his angel, and took me from my father's sheep, and he anointed me with the oil of his anointing. 
\q1
\v 5 My brothers were handsome and tall; but the Lord did not take pleasure in them. 
\q1
\v 6 I went out to meet the Philistine; and he cursed me by his idols. 
\q1
\v 7 But I drew his own sword, and beheaded him, and removed reproach from the children of Israel. 
